// Multilevel Master Listening — Part 6 (kitob + audio transkripti)
window.LISTENING_L6=[{"n":1,"ins":1,"title":"Labyrinths","dur":248.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Mazes are a type of {1}. The word maze is derived from a word meaning a feeling of {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Labyrinths represent a journey through life. They have frequently been used in {3} and prayer."},{"k":"p","t":"Ancient carvings on {4} have been found across many cultures."},{"k":"p","t":"Ancient Greeks used the symbol on {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The largest surviving example of a turf labyrinth once had a big {6} at its centre."}],"items":[{"a":["puzzle"],"ps":73.62,"en":77.82,"si":16,"ev":"as it is a kind of puzzle with an intricate network of paths.","hl":"puzzle","uz":"Chunki u murakkab yo'llar tarmog'iga ega jumboqning bir turi.","why":"\"A kind of puzzle\" — \"a type of puzzle\" bilan bir xil ma'no. Gapda \"maze\" labirintdan farqi tushuntirilmoqda."},{"a":["confusion"],"ps":110.1,"en":115.42,"si":23,"ev":"The word 'maze' is believed to come from a Scandinavian word for a state of confusion.","hl":"confusion","uz":"\"Maze\" so'zi skandinavcha \"sarosimalik holati\" degan so'zdan kelib chiqqan deb hisoblanadi.","why":"\"A state of confusion\" → \"a feeling of confusion\". Bo'shliqqa ot kerak: confusion (sarosima)."},{"a":["meditation"],"ps":153.4,"en":159.13,"si":33,"ev":"and have been used as a meditation and prayer tool in many cultures over many centuries.","hl":"meditation","uz":"va ko'plab madaniyatlarda asrlar davomida meditatsiya va ibodat vositasi sifatida ishlatilgan.","why":"\"Meditation and prayer tool\" — topshiriqdagi \"in meditation and prayer\" bilan aynan mos. Bo'shliq \"prayer\" oldida turibdi."},{"a":["stone"],"ps":160.38,"en":167.87,"si":34,"ev":"The earliest examples of the labyrinth spiral pattern have been found carved into stone from Sardinia to Scandinavia.","hl":"stone","uz":"Labirint spiral naqshining eng qadimgi namunalari Sardiniyadan Skandinaviyagacha toshga o'yilgan holda topilgan.","why":"\"Carved into stone\" → \"carvings on stone\". Sardinia/Scandinavia — joy nomlari, bo'shliqqa mos emas."},{"a":["coins"],"ps":187.48,"en":192.09,"si":40,"ev":"The labyrinth spiral was used on coins around 4,000 years ago.","hl":"coins","uz":"Labirint spirali taxminan 4000 yil oldin tangalarda ishlatilgan.","why":"\"Used on coins\" — qadimgi yunonlar belgini tangalarda ishlatgan. Keyingi gapdagi \"mosaics\" — hammomlar haqida, tuzoq."},{"a":["tree"],"ps":229.3,"en":231.9,"si":50,"ev":"which used to have a large tree in the middle of it.","hl":"tree","uz":"uning o'rtasida ilgari katta daraxt bo'lgan.","why":"\"A large tree in the middle\" → \"a big tree at its centre\". Saffron Walden'dagi eng katta turf labirint haqida."}],"segs":[{"s":1.59,"e":8.89,"t":"You will hear an anthropology student giving a presentation on spiral path designs known as labyrinths."},{"s":14.39,"e":18.85,"t":"Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40."},{"s":22.26,"e":26.4,"t":"Labyrinths have existed for well over 4,000 years."},{"s":27.38,"e":33.41,"t":"Labyrinths and labyrinthine symbols have been found in regions as diverse as modern-day Turkey."},{"s":33.88,"e":36.38,"t":"Ireland, Greece and India."},{"s":37.4,"e":39.26,"t":"There are various designs of labyrinth."},{"s":39.74,"e":45.5,"t":"But what they all have in common is a winding spiral path which leads to a central area."},{"s":46.81,"e":48.96,"t":"There is one starting point at the entrance."},{"s":49.46,"e":51.68,"t":"and the goal is to reach the central area."},{"s":52.82,"e":56.96,"t":"Finding your way through a labyrinth involves many twists and turns."},{"s":57.43,"e":59.13,"t":"But it's not possible to get lost."},{"s":59.58,"e":61.66,"t":"as there is only one single path."},{"s":63.38,"e":64.35,"t":"in modern times."},{"s":64.79,"e":67.23,"t":"The word labyrinth has taken on a different meaning."},{"s":67.77,"e":70.59,"t":"and is often used as a synonym for a maze."},{"s":71.42,"e":73.05,"t":"A maze is quite different."},{"s":73.62,"e":77.82,"t":"as it is a kind of puzzle with an intricate network of paths.","uz":"Chunki u murakkab yo'llar tarmog'iga ega jumboqning bir turi."},{"s":78.84,"e":82.94,"t":"Mazes became fashionable in the 15th and 16th centuries in Europe."},{"s":83.42,"e":87.01,"t":"and can still be found in the gardens of great houses and palaces."},{"s":88.12,"e":93.47,"t":"paths are usually surrounded by thick, high hedges so that it's not possible to see over them."},{"s":94.49,"e":102.56,"t":"Entering a maze usually involves getting lost a few times before using logic to work out the pattern and find your way to the centre."},{"s":103.03,"e":103.77,"t":"and then out again"},{"s":105.18,"e":109.18,"t":"There are lots of dead ends and paths which lead you back to where you started."},{"s":110.1,"e":115.42,"t":"The word 'maze' is believed to come from a Scandinavian word for a state of confusion.","uz":"\"Maze\" so'zi skandinavcha \"sarosimalik holati\" degan so'zdan kelib chiqqan deb hisoblanadi."},{"s":116.44,"e":119.1,"t":"This is where the word 'amazing' comes from."},{"s":120.89,"e":122.53,"t":"Labyrinths, on the other hand..."},{"s":123.03,"e":124.45,"t":"have a very different function."},{"s":125.59,"e":130.43,"t":"Although people now often refer to things they find complicated as 'labourines'"},{"s":131.03,"e":133.12,"t":"This is not how they were seen in the past."},{"s":134.26,"e":140.54,"t":"The winding spiral of the labyrinth has been used for centuries as a metaphor for life's journey."},{"s":141.46,"e":146.21,"t":"It served as a spiritual reminder that there is purpose and meaning to our lives."},{"s":146.71,"e":149.18,"t":"and helped to give people a sense of direction."},{"s":150.1,"e":152.8,"t":"Labyrinths are thought to encourage a feeling of calm."},{"s":153.4,"e":159.13,"t":"and have been used as a meditation and prayer tool in many cultures over many centuries.","uz":"va ko'plab madaniyatlarda asrlar davomida meditatsiya va ibodat vositasi sifatida ishlatilgan."},{"s":160.38,"e":167.87,"t":"The earliest examples of the labyrinth spiral pattern have been found carved into stone from Sardinia to Scandinavia.","uz":"Labirint spiral naqshining eng qadimgi namunalari Sardiniyadan Skandinaviyagacha toshga o'yilgan holda topilgan."},{"s":168.31,"e":170.08,"t":"from Arizona to India."},{"s":170.62,"e":171.26,"t":"Africa."},{"s":172.47,"e":176.48,"t":"In Europe, these spiral carvings date from the late Bronze Age."},{"s":177.21,"e":185.05,"t":"The Native American Pima tribe wove baskets with a circular labyrinth design that depicted their own cosmology."},{"s":186.04,"e":187.04,"t":"in ancient Greece."},{"s":187.48,"e":192.09,"t":"The labyrinth spiral was used on coins around 4,000 years ago.","uz":"Labirint spirali taxminan 4000 yil oldin tangalarda ishlatilgan."},{"s":193.27,"e":196.8,"t":"Labyrinths made of mosaics were commonly found in bathhouses."},{"s":197.24,"e":200.19,"t":"villas and tombs throughout the Roman Empire."},{"s":201.69,"e":202.81,"t":"in Northern Europe"},{"s":203.29,"e":206.37,"t":"There were actual physical labyrinths designed for walking off."},{"s":207.7,"e":211.74,"t":"These were cut into the turf or grass, usually in a circular pattern."},{"s":212.63,"e":215.74,"t":"The origin of these walking labyrinths remains unclear."},{"s":216.28,"e":221.12,"t":"they were probably used for fertility rights, which may date back thousands of years."},{"s":222.01,"e":225.28,"t":"Eleven examples of turf labyrinths survive today."},{"s":225.82,"e":228.86,"t":"including the largest one at Saffron Walden, England."},{"s":229.3,"e":231.9,"t":"which used to have a large tree in the middle of it.","uz":"uning o'rtasida ilgari katta daraxt bo'lgan."}]},{"n":2,"ins":2,"title":"Douglas Finch award","dur":247.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Douglas Finch is going to be given the Honorary Degree of Doctor of {1} Administration."},{"k":"p","t":"The Bristol Belle was the first hot air balloon in {2} Europe."},{"k":"p","t":"In 1968 he was issued with the first ever Private Pilot's Licence for Hot Air Balloons."},{"k":"p","t":"The Golden Falcon was designed specifically to fly across the {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"In 1973 he was awarded the Royal Aeronautical Club Silver Medal for the first balloon flight over the {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"In 1978 he attempted to cross the Atlantic in a balloon called Zanussi."},{"k":"p","t":"Doug Finch has advanced the science, technology and art of balloon flight to the highest {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Doug Finch will receive his Honorary {6} at Bristol Business School."}],"items":[{"a":["business"],"ps":15.16,"en":31.01,"si":2,"ev":"Douglas Finch is to be awarded the honorary degree of Doctor of Business Administration in recognition of his outstanding scientific, design and entrepreneurial achievements and their important contribution to the history and reputation of Bristol.","hl":"Business","uz":"Duglas Finch Biznes boshqaruvi doktori faxriy unvoniga sazovor bo'ladi — ilmiy, dizayn va tadbirkorlik yutuqlari uchun.","why":"\"Doctor of Business Administration\" — bo'shliq \"Administration\" oldida: Business."},{"a":["western"],"ps":79.67,"en":83.13,"si":9,"ev":"It was the first modern hot air balloon in Western Europe.","hl":"Western","uz":"Bu G'arbiy Yevropadagi birinchi zamonaviy havo shari edi.","why":"\"In Western Europe\" — bo'shliq \"Europe\" oldida, javob: Western."},{"a":["Sahara"],"ps":125.18,"en":128.61,"si":15,"ev":"balloon designed specifically to fly across the Sahara.","hl":"Sahara","uz":"…Saxaradan uchib o'tish uchun maxsus loyihalangan havo shari.","why":"\"Designed specifically to fly across the Sahara\" — topshiriq bilan so'zma-so'z mos."},{"a":["Alps"],"ps":139.9,"en":155.39,"si":18,"ev":"A year later, he was awarded the Royal Aeronautical Club Silver Medal for the first balloon flight over the Alps. In the same year, he received the Light of an Air Society (USA) Achievement Award for the development of the first hot airship.","hl":"Alps","uz":"Bir yil o'tib, Alp tog'lari ustidan birinchi havo sharida uchgani uchun Qirollik Aeronavtika klubining kumush medali bilan taqdirlandi.","why":"\"The first balloon flight over the Alps\" — Silver medal shu uchun. Atlantika (Atlantic) — oltin medal bilan bog'liq, tuzoq."},{"a":["level"],"ps":219.54,"en":225.57,"si":26,"ev":"Doug Finch has advanced the science, technology and art of balloon flight to the highest level.","hl":"level","uz":"Dag Finch havo sharida uchish ilmi, texnologiyasi va san'atini eng yuqori darajaga olib chiqdi.","why":"\"To the highest level\" — topshiriqda ham aynan shunday."},{"a":["degree"],"ps":235.42,"en":243.74,"si":28,"ev":"Doug Finch will receive his honorary degree of Doctor of Business Administration at the awards ceremony at Bristol Business School.","hl":"degree","uz":"Dag Finch Biznes boshqaruvi doktori faxriy darajasini Bristol Biznes maktabidagi taqdirlash marosimida oladi.","why":"\"Honorary degree\" — bo'shliq \"Honorary\" dan keyin: degree."}],"segs":[{"s":0.06,"e":2.33,"t":"Exercise 2. Part 2."},{"s":7.51,"e":12.57,"t":"You will hear a radio news item about a hot air balloon manufacturer."},{"s":15.16,"e":31.01,"t":"Douglas Finch is to be awarded the honorary degree of Doctor of Business Administration in recognition of his outstanding scientific, design and entrepreneurial achievements and their important contribution to the history and reputation of Bristol.","uz":"Duglas Finch Biznes boshqaruvi doktori faxriy unvoniga sazovor bo'ladi — ilmiy, dizayn va tadbirkorlik yutuqlari uchun."},{"s":32.76,"e":45.34,"t":"Douglas Finch was born near Glasgow and attended Allen Glen School before reading Aeronautical Engineering at Glasgow University, from which he graduated in 1961."},{"s":46.36,"e":53.85,"t":"He gained a master's degree in industrial engineering at Cornell University USA in 1963."},{"s":54.36,"e":59.29,"t":"before returning to the United Kingdom and joining the Bristol Aeroplane Company."},{"s":60.63,"e":67.55,"t":"He joined the Bristol Gliding Club and in 1965 received the Silver Sea Gliding Badge."},{"s":68.44,"e":72.25,"t":"In 1967, he helped build the Bristol Bell."},{"s":72.82,"e":79.01,"t":"a red and white striped balloon, which made its first flights at Weston-on-the-Green, near Oxford."},{"s":79.67,"e":83.13,"t":"It was the first modern hot air balloon in Western Europe.","uz":"Bu G'arbiy Yevropadagi birinchi zamonaviy havo shari edi."},{"s":84.34,"e":91.39,"t":"In 1968, Doug Finch was issued with the first ever private pilot's license for hot air balloons."},{"s":92.28,"e":107.07,"t":"The success of Doug Finch in translating his ballooning expertise into a commercial concern is reflected in the birth and success of his company, Finch Balloons of Bristol, which was formed by Finch in 1971."},{"s":107.58,"e":110.78,"t":"five years after he constructed his first balloon."},{"s":112.02,"e":119.2,"t":"The new company was based in Dutton, Bristol, where a total of 29 balloons were made in the basement of the property."},{"s":120.18,"e":124.61,"t":"1971, also saw Finch build Golden Falcon."},{"s":125.18,"e":128.61,"t":"balloon designed specifically to fly across the Sahara.","uz":"…Saxaradan uchib o'tish uchun maxsus loyihalangan havo shari."},{"s":130.26,"e":135.68,"t":"In 1972, Doug Finch received the Royal Aeronautical Club Bronze Medal."},{"s":136.34,"e":139.26,"t":"the first awarded for hot air airships."},{"s":139.9,"e":155.39,"t":"A year later, he was awarded the Royal Aeronautical Club Silver Medal for the first balloon flight over the Alps. In the same year, he received the Light of an Air Society (USA) Achievement Award for the development of the first hot airship.","uz":"Bir yil o'tib, Alp tog'lari ustidan birinchi havo sharida uchgani uchun Qirollik Aeronavtika klubining kumush medali bilan taqdirlandi."},{"s":156.6,"e":164.51,"t":"Five years later, he attempted the first Atlantic crossing by balloon, for which he received the Royal Aeronautical Club gold medal."},{"s":165.69,"e":178.88,"t":"In 1978, his attempt to make the premier Atlantic crossing by balloon ended when bad weather forced his heated helium balloon Zanussi down after a 2,000-mile flight from Canada."},{"s":180.09,"e":185.05,"t":"The Finch Company moved to its present site in Gellingborough, in 1983."},{"s":185.56,"e":192.89,"t":"And in the following years, all of the records for distance and duration were taken by pilots flying finch balloons."},{"s":193.62,"e":205.82,"t":"In 1989, Finch Balloons Ltd received the Queen's Award for Export, confirmation that Doug Finch had made Bristol the undisputed balloon manufacturing capital of the world."},{"s":206.84,"e":213.47,"t":"During the 1990s, interest in becoming the first to fly around the world by balloon became intense."},{"s":214.04,"e":218.65,"t":"and almost all the contenders have used Finch Helium hot air balloons."},{"s":219.54,"e":225.57,"t":"Doug Finch has advanced the science, technology and art of balloon flight to the highest level.","uz":"Dag Finch havo sharida uchish ilmi, texnologiyasi va san'atini eng yuqori darajaga olib chiqdi."},{"s":226.84,"e":234.14,"t":"His factory in Bristol is the world's largest and last year he was awarded the Prince Philip Design Award."},{"s":235.42,"e":243.74,"t":"Doug Finch will receive his honorary degree of Doctor of Business Administration at the awards ceremony at Bristol Business School.","uz":"Dag Finch Biznes boshqaruvi doktori faxriy darajasini Bristol Biznes maktabidagi taqdirlash marosimida oladi."}]},{"n":3,"ins":2,"title":"Women's sport in the media","dur":461.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"A survey shows that {1} coverage of women's sport makes up only about 4% of stories."},{"k":"p","t":"Greg says the media doesn't publish stories about a sport which not many {2} are interested in."},{"k":"p","t":"It is claimed that in the UK there are over 1 million women who play netball."},{"k":"p","t":"Apart from netball, Greg mentions {3} as an example of a sport that many people do but not many want to read about."},{"k":"p","t":"Greg's magazine has 4 times as many male readers as female readers."},{"k":"p","t":"He thinks the {4} needs a sports magazine especially for female readers."},{"k":"p","t":"Greg says top women tennis players aren't able to spend much time with their {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"There are about 60 women who are members of the Sports Journalist Association of Great Britain."},{"k":"p","t":"The number of TV sports {6} has increased recently, which should improve coverage of women's sport."}],"items":[{"a":["newspaper"],"ps":23.96,"en":29.98,"si":3,"ev":"This year's report, released last month, shows that only 4% of newspaper stories are about women's sport.","hl":"newspaper","uz":"Bu yilgi hisobot shuni ko'rsatadiki, gazeta maqolalarining atigi 4 foizi ayollar sporti haqida.","why":"\"4% of newspaper stories\" → \"newspaper coverage … 4% of stories\"."},{"a":["readers"],"ps":49.94,"en":57.12,"si":8,"ev":"Usually, if we don't publish, it's because it's a minority sport and very few people do it, or very few readers have an interest in it.","hl":"readers","uz":"Odatda biz chop etmasak, sababi bu — kam odam shug'ullanadigan yoki juda kam o'quvchi qiziqadigan sport turi.","why":"\"Very few readers have an interest in it\" → \"not many readers are interested\". Javob: readers."},{"a":["fishing"],"ps":81.53,"en":90.88,"si":12,"ev":"But if you use that argument, then we'll be doing lots of articles about fishing and other big participation sports. As I said, it has absolutely nothing to do with the fact that it's women.","hl":"fishing","uz":"Lekin bu dalilga tayansak, baliq ovi va boshqa ko'p odam shug'ullanadigan sport turlari haqida ham ko'plab maqola yozishimiz kerak bo'lardi.","why":"Netbol bilan birga misol qilingan sport — fishing (baliq ovi): ko'pchilik shug'ullanadi, lekin o'qishni istamaydi."},{"a":["market"],"ps":130.55,"en":139.42,"si":22,"ev":"So I think yeah, there's a gap in the market for a sports magazine aimed at women who take sports seriously and want to read about sport and learn more about sport on all levels.","hl":"market","uz":"Demak, bozorda sportga jiddiy qaraydigan ayollar uchun sport jurnaliga bo'shliq bor.","why":"\"A gap in the market for a sports magazine aimed at women\" — bozorga ayollar uchun sport jurnali kerak. Javob: market."},{"a":["children"],"ps":151.29,"en":160.38,"si":27,"ev":"For example top female tennis players with children find life very difficult. They have to travel all the time to international tournaments and that means they hardly ever see them.","hl":"children","uz":"Masalan, farzandli eng kuchli tennischi ayollarning hayoti juda qiyin: doim xalqaro turnirlarga uchib yurishadi va bolalarini deyarli ko'rishmaydi.","why":"\"Hardly ever see them\" — \"them\" bu yerda \"children\". Javob: children."},{"a":["channels"],"ps":217.69,"en":222.11,"si":39,"ev":"There are more sports channels than ever now, so a lot of big women's events are getting shown.","hl":"channels","uz":"Hozir sport kanallari har qachongidan ko'p, shuning uchun ayollarning ko'plab yirik musobaqalari efirga uzatilmoqda.","why":"\"More sports channels than ever\" → \"number of TV sports channels has increased\". Javob: channels."}],"segs":[{"s":1.56,"e":5.47,"t":"You'll hear a radio interview with a man called Greg Hunter."},{"s":5.88,"e":7.9,"t":"is the editor of a sports magazine."},{"s":17.88,"e":23.29,"t":"Every four years the National Sports Commission does a survey on how the media cover women's sport."},{"s":23.96,"e":29.98,"t":"This year's report, released last month, shows that only 4% of newspaper stories are about women's sport.","uz":"Bu yilgi hisobot shuni ko'rsatadiki, gazeta maqolalarining atigi 4 foizi ayollar sporti haqida."},{"s":30.68,"e":33.25,"t":"Why does women's sport get such a raw deal?"},{"s":33.88,"e":38.91,"t":"Today I'm talking to Greg Hunter, the editor of today's sport magazine. Hi Greg."},{"s":39.45,"e":40.13,"t":"Hello, Amanda."},{"s":40.7,"e":49.34,"t":"You know, people in the media don't see a difference between men and women's sport. In other words, we don't say, \"Oh, this is a sport story about women, so we won't publish it.\""},{"s":49.94,"e":57.12,"t":"Usually, if we don't publish, it's because it's a minority sport and very few people do it, or very few readers have an interest in it.","uz":"Odatda biz chop etmasak, sababi bu — kam odam shug'ullanadigan yoki juda kam o'quvchi qiziqadigan sport turi."},{"s":57.75,"e":61.12,"t":"It's got nothing to do with whether the sport is being played by men or women."},{"s":61.59,"e":73.57,"t":"Well Greg, I don't know that you could really call netball for example a minority sport. I mean the netball association estimates that every week over one million women in the UK play netball. Is that a minority sport?"},{"s":74.26,"e":80.96,"t":"A lot of people say that, and say that it's not fair for women that we don't write anything about netball in newspaper and magazines."},{"s":81.53,"e":90.88,"t":"But if you use that argument, then we'll be doing lots of articles about fishing and other big participation sports. As I said, it has absolutely nothing to do with the fact that it's women.","uz":"Lekin bu dalilga tayansak, baliq ovi va boshqa ko'p odam shug'ullanadigan sport turlari haqida ham ko'plab maqola yozishimiz kerak bo'lardi."},{"s":91.48,"e":96.67,"t":"It's not even about how many people play it. For us, it's about how many people want to read about it."},{"s":97.11,"e":100.48,"t":"So what's the ratio of male to female readers on your magazine?"},{"s":101.18,"e":105.85,"t":"about 4 men for every woman, and that's up maybe 5% from 2 or 3 years ago."},{"s":106.78,"e":108.89,"t":"Why don't more women read your magazine?"},{"s":109.4,"e":112.89,"t":"Do you think that a lot of women are turned off it because it is male-oriented?"},{"s":113.46,"e":114.62,"t":"Oh, without a doubt,"},{"s":115.42,"e":119.1,"t":"And do you think women actually want a sports magazine named \"Soleat Women\"?"},{"s":119.96,"e":122.4,"t":"Absolutely, I think for sure."},{"s":122.94,"e":129.79,"t":"If we look at the sports magazines on the market at the moment, they're definitely more for the male sporty person than the female sporty person."},{"s":130.55,"e":139.42,"t":"So I think yeah, there's a gap in the market for a sports magazine aimed at women who take sports seriously and want to read about sport and learn more about sport on all levels.","uz":"Demak, bozorda sportga jiddiy qaraydigan ayollar uchun sport jurnaliga bo'shliq bor."},{"s":140.18,"e":143.78,"t":"In your experience, what do women want out of a sports magazine?"},{"s":144.21,"e":147.2,"t":"I think women readers care more about the human side of stories.\""},{"s":147.54,"e":148.74,"t":"They like to know about what"},{"s":149.07,"e":150.91,"t":"What's behind a sportsperson?"},{"s":151.29,"e":160.38,"t":"For example top female tennis players with children find life very difficult. They have to travel all the time to international tournaments and that means they hardly ever see them.","uz":"Masalan, farzandli eng kuchli tennischi ayollarning hayoti juda qiyin: doim xalqaro turnirlarga uchib yurishadi va bolalarini deyarli ko'rishmaydi."},{"s":161.08,"e":165.37,"t":"Whenever we run an article about this kind of thing, it's very popular with our women readers."},{"s":166.39,"e":175.81,"t":"But moving away from magazines for a moment, the Sports Commission report also says that in the last four years, television coverage of women's sports has actually decreased."},{"s":176.34,"e":183.71,"t":"Women's sports received only 6% of total TV time available for sport last year, compared to 9% four years ago."},{"s":184.54,"e":185.21,"t":"that be?"},{"s":185.75,"e":192.45,"t":"Okay, I have to admit that one of the reasons women receive little media coverage is that most sports reporting is done by men."},{"s":193.05,"e":199.13,"t":"I heard there are about 600 members of the Sports Journalists Association of Great Britain, but only around 60 are women."},{"s":200.02,"e":204.73,"t":"Perhaps if women were more involved in sports journalism, there'd be better coverage of women's sport."},{"s":205.27,"e":209.05,"t":"But anyway, there have been some improvements in how women's sports are shown on TV."},{"s":209.85,"e":210.49,"t":"Really?"},{"s":211.03,"e":212.03,"t":"Yes, of course."},{"s":212.54,"e":217.05,"t":"For example, last year, the Women's Football World Cup was shown on a number of TV channels."},{"s":217.69,"e":222.11,"t":"There are more sports channels than ever now, so a lot of big women's events are getting shown.","uz":"Hozir sport kanallari har qachongidan ko'p, shuning uchun ayollarning ko'plab yirik musobaqalari efirga uzatilmoqda."},{"s":222.81,"e":229.76,"t":"and in the future, it'll be possible to see a lot of minority sports on cable or satellite channels."}]},{"n":4,"ins":2,"title":"Children and water safety","dur":329.1,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The speaker says a {1} may be dangerous for small children."},{"k":"p","t":"The {2} of the Royal Lifesaving Society website can be found on the fact sheet."},{"k":"p","t":"A child can start swimming lessons when it is 6 months old."},{"k":"p","t":"During swimming lessons, very young children learn to roll onto their backs."},{"k":"p","t":"At a private pool, there should be one supervisor for every {3} children."},{"k":"p","t":"Children must learn not to go close to the {4} unless an adult is supervising them."},{"k":"p","t":"There are many more {5} in private swimming pools than public pools."},{"k":"p","t":"At home, put an alarm on the rear {6} so you hear a noise if your child has gone into the garden."},{"k":"p","t":"Apart from public and private pools, the sea can also be dangerous to children."}],"items":[{"a":["pool"],"ps":12.12,"en":19.93,"si":1,"ev":"So jumping in the pool sounds like a pretty good idea, right?","hl":"pool","uz":"Shunday ekan, basseynga sho'ng'ish yaxshi fikrdek tuyuladi, to'g'rimi?","why":"Keyingi gap: \"a swimming pool can be an extremely risky place for them\" — kichik bolalar uchun xavfli joy — pool."},{"a":["address"],"ps":20.38,"en":41.6,"si":2,"ev":"I have copies of a fact sheet from the Royal Life Saving Society here and you can also visit our website. The address is printed on the back.","hl":"address","uz":"Menda Royal Life Saving Society'ning ma'lumot varaqasi bor, saytimizga ham kirishingiz mumkin. Manzil varaqning orqasida yozilgan.","why":"\"The address is printed on the back\" — sayt manzili varaqda. Javob: address."},{"a":["4","four"],"ps":88.54,"en":100.96,"si":5,"ev":"As a rule there should be one supervising adult for every four kids under eight.","hl":"four","uz":"Qoidaga ko'ra, sakkiz yoshgacha bo'lgan har to'rt bolaga bitta kuzatuvchi kattalar bo'lishi kerak.","why":"\"One supervising adult for every four kids\" — javob: 4 (four). \"Eight\" — bolalarning yoshi, tuzoq."},{"a":["water"],"ps":101.43,"en":106.21,"si":6,"ev":"And there's a simple message to tell your kids. If there's no adult around, you can't go near the water.","hl":"water","uz":"Bolalaringizga oddiy bir qoidani ayting: atrofda kattalar bo'lmasa, suvga yaqin borolmaysan.","why":"\"You can't go near the water\" — \"not to go close to the water\". Javob: water."},{"a":["accidents"],"ps":106.71,"en":121.12,"si":7,"ev":"More than 10 times as many water-related accidents happen at home than in public pools.","hl":"accidents","uz":"Suv bilan bog'liq baxtsiz hodisalar uyda jamoat basseynlariga qaraganda 10 baravardan ko'proq sodir bo'ladi.","why":"\"Accidents happen at home\" — uy basseynlarida baxtsiz hodisalar ko'p. Javob: accidents."},{"a":["door"],"ps":121.62,"en":128.99,"si":8,"ev":"It's also a good idea to have a back door alarm that makes a loud sound if your child ever decides to explore outside by him or herself.","hl":"door","uz":"Bolangiz yolg'iz tashqariga chiqmoqchi bo'lsa, baland ovoz chiqaradigan orqa eshik signalizatsiyasini o'rnatish ham yaxshi fikr.","why":"\"Back door alarm\" → \"alarm on the rear door\". Javob: door."}],"segs":[{"s":0.06,"e":7.13,"t":"Exercise 4. You'll hear someone giving a lecture to a group of parents about keeping children safe in water."},{"s":12.12,"e":19.93,"t":"This week the temperature across the country will be hitting 30 degrees and above. So jumping in the pool sounds like a pretty good idea, right?"},{"s":20.38,"e":41.6,"t":"But if you have little kids you need to know that a swimming pool can be an extremely risky place for them. So I'm really glad to be invited here today to talk to you about keeping your children safe in the water. Oh, and if you want more information afterwards I have copies of a fact sheet from the Royal Life Saving Society here and you can also visit our website. The address is printed on the back."},{"s":42.23,"e":60.29,"t":"Most parents teaching very small kids to swim isn't a high priority, so I'd like to start by quoting the old saying, \"Prevention is better than cure.\" In other words, teach your child to swim as soon as possible. You can take your baby to the pool when it's as young as three months. By the age of six months, the child should be able to begin having lessons."},{"s":60.95,"e":88.16,"t":"After that, you should take your child to the swimming pool as often as possible. What's important is to get them used to the water. After a few lessons, even very young children can be taught to just roll over and float on their backs, blow bubbles and generally enjoy life. That means that if they do fall in a pool accidentally, they're not afraid and they have a good chance of staying alive until an adult finds them. Of course, as parents, you can do much more. Make sure someone is always supervising children around the pool."},{"s":88.54,"e":100.96,"t":"Take your children to public pools which have trained lifeguards and if your child goes to a friend's pool always check to see that there are enough supervisors. As a rule there should be one supervising adult for every four kids under eight."},{"s":101.43,"e":106.21,"t":"And there's a simple message to tell your kids. If there's no adult around, you can't go near the water.","uz":"Bolalaringizga oddiy bir qoidani ayting: atrofda kattalar bo'lmasa, suvga yaqin borolmaysan."},{"s":106.71,"e":121.12,"t":"Talking of private pools, swimming pools in people's homes I mean, these should be your biggest worry in the summer months. More than 10 times as many water-related accidents happen at home than in public pools. By law you must have a securely fastened fence around the pool."},{"s":121.62,"e":128.99,"t":"It's also a good idea to have a back door alarm that makes a loud sound if your child ever decides to explore outside by him or herself.","uz":"Bolangiz yolg'iz tashqariga chiqmoqchi bo'lsa, baland ovoz chiqaradigan orqa eshik signalizatsiyasini o'rnatish ham yaxshi fikr."},{"s":129.56,"e":139.68,"t":"When you go to the beach you have to be extra careful. Always, and I really do mean always, keep an eye on your child. A small child can get into trouble even in small waves."},{"s":140.18,"e":156.29,"t":"Also avoid all those kind of blow-up toys that kids love. They may be fun, but they can easily be blown out to sea. And this may seem an obvious thing to say, but you'd be amazed how many people ignore it. Never, I repeat, never swim when the red flag is flying."},{"s":156.76,"e":159.36,"t":"Apart from that, have a great time at the beach."}]},{"n":5,"ins":2,"title":"Astrology","dur":554.0,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Over 60% of British adults admit to being interested in astrology."},{"k":"p","t":"Less than 3% of people would consult the stars before making {1} decisions."},{"k":"p","t":"Psychologists now believe that time of birth can affect a person's {2} development."},{"k":"p","t":"Time of birth is not the only factor, but it is the foundation for future changes."},{"k":"p","t":"To test his idea, the speaker decided to compare people's choice of {3} and zodiac sign."},{"k":"p","t":"Other connections found by the study were less {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"A fair number of serious sports players were born in the {5} months."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker thinks that the lack of professions dominated by mostly one sign is a little {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["business"],"ps":61.3,"en":73.12,"si":5,"ev":"although only 3.5% would use them to choose a husband or wife, and only 2.9% of people would refer to them in making business decisions.","hl":"business","uz":"…atigi 3,5 foizi turmush o'rtog'ini tanlashda, 2,9 foizi esa biznes qarorlari qabul qilishda yulduzlarga tayanadi.","why":"\"Less than 3%\" = 2,9% — bu biznes qarorlari. 3,5% — er/xotin tanlash, tuzoq."},{"a":["character"],"ps":84.12,"en":93.82,"si":7,"ev":"Psychologists now widely agree that both early life experiences and time of birth are a great influence on the development of a person's character.","hl":"character","uz":"Psixologlar endi erta hayot tajribasi ham, tug'ilgan vaqt ham inson xarakterining rivojlanishiga katta ta'sir qilishini keng tan olishmoqda.","why":"\"Development of a person's character\" → \"a person's character development\". Javob: character."},{"a":["career"],"ps":134.07,"en":141.53,"si":13,"ev":"I have simply made a statistical comparison between people's choice of career and their zodiac sign.","hl":"career","uz":"Men shunchaki odamlarning kasb tanlovi va burjini statistik solishtirdim.","why":"\"People's choice of career and their zodiac sign\" — aynan mos. Javob: career."},{"a":["obvious"],"ps":198.07,"en":202.46,"si":22,"ev":"But there have been others, although they have been less obvious.","hl":"obvious","uz":"Ammo boshqa bog'liqliklar ham bo'lgan, garchi ular kamroq ko'zga tashlansa-da.","why":"\"Less obvious\" — topshiriqda ham \"less\". Javob: obvious."},{"a":["winter"],"ps":209.69,"en":215.84,"si":24,"ev":"and found a sizeable number were born in the winter months of January and February.","hl":"winter","uz":"…va ularning anchagina qismi yanvar va fevral — qish oylarida tug'ilganini aniqladik.","why":"\"Winter months of January and February\" — javob: winter. \"Early spring\" — tez-tez sayohat qiluvchilar haqida, tuzoq."},{"a":["disappointing"],"ps":239.86,"en":249.73,"si":28,"ev":"So far, we haven't found any professions containing large percentages of one particular star sign, which is a little disappointing.","hl":"disappointing","uz":"Hozircha bitta burj ustunlik qiladigan kasbni topmadik, bu biroz ko'ngilni xira qiladi.","why":"\"Which is a little disappointing\" — topshiriqda \"a little {6}\". Javob: disappointing."}],"segs":[{"s":1.82,"e":8.13,"t":"You will hear a psychologist speaking on British radio on the subject of astrology."},{"s":13.75,"e":38.3,"t":"We have with us today the psychologist Simon Calvin, who has recently created quite a stir with some rather unlikely claims about astrology. Simon, are you indeed claiming that our lives are ruled by the stars? No, not at all. I would not for one minute say that all of our lives are affected by the movements of stars in the heavens."},{"s":38.81,"e":43.2,"t":"My research really concerns things that are far more down to earth."},{"s":44.34,"e":53.28,"t":"before I start, I should just say that by no means do the majority of people in general totally disbelieve the value of astrology."},{"s":54.14,"e":60.77,"t":"incredible 62% of British adults say that their stars are of some interest to them."},{"s":61.3,"e":73.12,"t":"although only 3.5% would use them to choose a husband or wife, and only 2.9% of people would refer to them in making business decisions.","uz":"…atigi 3,5 foizi turmush o'rtog'ini tanlashda, 2,9 foizi esa biznes qarorlari qabul qilishda yulduzlarga tayanadi."},{"s":74.23,"e":83.1,"t":"Anyway, coming back to what I said before, I'm not so interested in the stars themselves as I am in the time of year somebody is born."},{"s":84.12,"e":93.82,"t":"Psychologists now widely agree that both early life experiences and time of birth are a great influence on the development of a person's character.","uz":"Psixologlar endi erta hayot tajribasi ham, tug'ilgan vaqt ham inson xarakterining rivojlanishiga katta ta'sir qilishini keng tan olishmoqda."},{"s":94.62,"e":103.01,"t":"Of course, this does not make the whole of a person's character, but rather the foundation or base on which later changes are made."},{"s":103.9,"e":109.47,"t":"However, these later changes in character are not connected with the person's time of birth."},{"s":110.01,"e":124.99,"t":"So the question is then, after all these personality changes have happened, can we look at an adult and see any of this foundation or base as part of their psychological makeup?"},{"s":126.1,"e":130.97,"t":"The technique I have been using to do just this is a very simple one."},{"s":131.64,"e":133.5,"t":"that I believe very effective."},{"s":134.07,"e":141.53,"t":"I have simply made a statistical comparison between people's choice of career and their zodiac sign.","uz":"Men shunchaki odamlarning kasb tanlovi va burjini statistik solishtirdim."},{"s":142.39,"e":148.45,"t":"where somebody has made a strong choice in favor of a particular kind of career"},{"s":149.21,"e":154.14,"t":"I believe that this indicates something very important in their character."},{"s":155.61,"e":160.25,"t":"If you look at a particular profession, say entertainers for example,"},{"s":160.92,"e":167.58,"t":"and find that more than 15% of them were born in a certain short period of the year"},{"s":168.25,"e":177.53,"t":"It suggests that their choice of that profession is in some way connected with their birth at that particular time of the year."},{"s":178.68,"e":180.7,"t":"This is in fact the case."},{"s":181.37,"e":191.07,"t":"An astonishing 20% of artists and entertainers were born in the period between the 12th of July and the 20th of August."},{"s":191.86,"e":196.8,"t":"This, in fact, is the most positive connection we have found so far."},{"s":198.07,"e":202.46,"t":"But there have been others, although they have been less obvious.","uz":"Ammo boshqa bog'liqliklar ham bo'lgan, garchi ular kamroq ko'zga tashlansa-da."},{"s":203.35,"e":209.12,"t":"We looked at keen sports players participating more than five times a week."},{"s":209.69,"e":215.84,"t":"and found a sizeable number were born in the winter months of January and February.","uz":"…va ularning anchagina qismi yanvar va fevral — qish oylarida tug'ilganini aniqladik."},{"s":216.7,"e":225.95,"t":"Another group of people we looked at were frequent travellers who, we discovered, were more likely to have been born in early spring."},{"s":226.94,"e":237.95,"t":"while accountants, bankers, executives and people generally in financial professions more frequently have birthdays in the late spring."},{"s":238.97,"e":239.33,"t":"now."},{"s":239.86,"e":249.73,"t":"So far, we haven't found any professions containing large percentages of one particular star sign, which is a little disappointing.","uz":"Hozircha bitta burj ustunlik qiladigan kasbni topmadik, bu biroz ko'ngilni xira qiladi."},{"s":250.3,"e":259.01,"t":"But this is no doubt because our modern technological world has removed us further and further from the effects of nature."},{"s":259.64,"e":270.78,"t":"If, as was the case in the past, many people lived closer to nature, we could be seeing percentages as high as 40 or 50 or even more."},{"s":271.42,"e":274.14,"t":"This, of course, would mean that we would..."}]},{"n":6,"ins":2,"title":"Anita Lee's food company","dur":421.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"People in millions of British {1} eat Anita Lee's meals."},{"k":"p","t":"The Chinese meals which Anita bought didn't taste like the food cooked by her mother."},{"k":"p","t":"In order to cook for herself, Anita had to find authentic Chinese {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Increased demand made it necessary for Anita to hire people to help."},{"k":"p","t":"Anita's company was given the top prize for ethnic food by a well-known food {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"She needed money to expand the company, but she didn't want to get a {4} from the bank."},{"k":"p","t":"Lania Foods wanted to make changes in the way that the {5} was produced."},{"k":"p","t":"Becoming Businesswoman of the Year was Anita's proudest {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["homes"],"ps":36.15,"en":43.39,"si":3,"ev":"The Chinese meals she used to make for her husband David and two young daughters are now enjoyed in millions of homes all over Britain.","hl":"homes","uz":"U eri Devid va ikki kichik qizi uchun tayyorlagan xitoy taomlari endi butun Britaniya bo'ylab millionlab xonadonlarda iste'mol qilinadi.","why":"\"Millions of homes all over Britain\" — javob: homes."},{"a":["ingredients"],"ps":59.64,"en":67.68,"si":7,"ev":"So I looked around for proper Chinese ingredients and cooked for myself.","hl":"ingredients","uz":"Shuning uchun haqiqiy xitoy masalliqlarini qidirib topib, o'zim pishira boshladim.","why":"\"Proper Chinese ingredients\" → \"authentic Chinese ingredients\". Restoran taomlari ingliz didiga moslashtirilgan edi."},{"a":["magazine"],"ps":129.75,"en":136.67,"si":17,"ev":"Gourmet magazine had given us its top prize for ethnic cuisine, and contracts were coming in from all the big supermarket chains.","hl":"magazine","uz":"Gourmet jurnali bizga etnik oshxona bo'yicha bosh sovrinini bergan edi, barcha yirik supermarket tarmoqlaridan shartnomalar kelayotgandi.","why":"\"Gourmet magazine … its top prize for ethnic cuisine\" — javob: magazine."},{"a":["loan"],"ps":137.4,"en":146.62,"si":18,"ev":"I was reluctant to go to the bank for a loan, and Lanny of Foods came along and offered us the funds we needed.","hl":"loan","uz":"Bankdan qarz olgim kelmasdi, shunda Lania Foods kelib, kerakli mablag'ni taklif qildi.","why":"\"Reluctant to go to the bank for a loan\" → \"didn't want to get a loan from the bank\". Javob: loan."},{"a":["food"],"ps":161.37,"en":173.28,"si":23,"ev":"They even wanted to alter the food production, change some of the ingredients in the recipes.","hl":"food","uz":"Ular hatto taom ishlab chiqarishni o'zgartirmoqchi, retseptlardagi ba'zi masalliqlarni almashtirmoqchi bo'lishdi.","why":"\"Alter the food production\" → \"make changes in the way that the food was produced\". Javob: food. \"Ingredients\" — boshqa narsa, gapga mos kelmaydi."},{"a":["moment"],"ps":207.67,"en":211.9,"si":31,"ev":"That was my proudest moment. It made all the hard work worthwhile.","hl":"moment","uz":"Bu mening eng faxrli lahzam edi. Butun mashaqqatli mehnat o'zini oqladi.","why":"\"My proudest moment\" — javob: moment."}],"segs":[{"s":1.91,"e":9.12,"t":"You'll hear an interview with a woman called Anita Li, who runs a successful business producing ready-made Chinese meals."},{"s":21.24,"e":31.13,"t":"It's a long way from cooking dinner every day for the family to preparing half a million meals a week in a purpose-built £5 million factory of your own design."},{"s":31.58,"e":35.26,"t":"But Anita Lee has made the jump in just a few years."},{"s":36.15,"e":43.39,"t":"The Chinese meals she used to make for her husband David and two young daughters are now enjoyed in millions of homes all over Britain.","uz":"U eri Devid va ikki kichik qizi uchun tayyorlagan xitoy taomlari endi butun Britaniya bo'ylab millionlab xonadonlarda iste'mol qilinadi."},{"s":44.06,"e":51.65,"t":"It's not something that's easily done. So where did she start and why? I started making my own Chinese food because I didn't like what I could buy."},{"s":52.09,"e":55.9,"t":"Chinese meals I bought in the supermarket didn't taste like Chinese food to me."},{"s":56.38,"e":59.07,"t":"And there were nothing like my mother's cooking back home in Hong Kong."},{"s":59.64,"e":67.68,"t":"Even meals from the local Chinese restaurants seem to have been adapted to suit English tastes. So I looked around for proper Chinese ingredients and cooked for myself."},{"s":68.38,"e":73.79,"t":"And when I cooked for my family and friends, they all said how much better things tasted, and how much they enjoyed them."},{"s":75.1,"e":85.41,"t":"Many of us are good cooks at home, but that doesn't make you Businesswoman of the Year overnight. So, what was so special about your cooking that made it so enormously successful?"},{"s":85.98,"e":94.46,"t":"Oh, one of our friends owned the local Chinese restaurant. And whenever he visited our house, he liked my homemade noodles so much that he wanted to use them in the restaurant."},{"s":94.9,"e":107.71,"t":"They were a big success and encouraged me to try out other things for him, like sweet and sour sauce and crackers. He always had trouble getting good cooks and even more trouble keeping them, so he liked to buy in the sauces ready made."},{"s":108.15,"e":112.45,"t":"He liked the arrangements and so did I. Anyway, I started taking on people to help."},{"s":112.95,"e":116.99,"t":"And then I took a unit on an industrial estate in Cowbridge to cope with the demand."},{"s":117.46,"e":121.31,"t":"It all grew from that really. As easy as boiling an egg."},{"s":121.88,"e":125.12,"t":"But in fact, it wasn't always plain sailing for you, was it?"},{"s":125.98,"e":129.25,"t":"Strangely enough, we had trouble when the company became really successful."},{"s":129.75,"e":136.67,"t":"Gourmet magazine had given us its top prize for ethnic cuisine, and contracts were coming in from all the big supermarket chains.","uz":"Gourmet jurnali bizga etnik oshxona bo'yicha bosh sovrinini bergan edi, barcha yirik supermarket tarmoqlaridan shartnomalar kelayotgandi."},{"s":137.4,"e":146.62,"t":"We needed to expand, but didn't really have the capital to do it. I was reluctant to go to the bank for a loan, and Lania Foods came along and offered us the funds we needed."},{"s":147.13,"e":150.97,"t":"It seemed too good to be true. And it was, wasn't it? Sorry?"},{"s":151.48,"e":152.45,"t":"good to be true."},{"s":152.79,"e":153.15,"t":"Oh."},{"s":153.49,"e":161.02,"t":"Yes, yes it was. You see, at first it seemed that Lania Foods was willing to provide the necessary funds and be seen as an equal partner."},{"s":161.37,"e":173.28,"t":"But then, very soon, they tried to take over control of the company. They even wanted to alter the food production, change some of the ingredients in the recipes, things like that. Hmm, nasty."},{"s":173.85,"e":176.19,"t":"Yes, that time was like a living nightmare."},{"s":176.86,"e":180.48,"t":"I really had to fight to protect my products and the business I'd struggle to build up."},{"s":181.21,"e":184.51,"t":"Luckily I had a very loyal workforce who backed me all the way."},{"s":185.08,"e":190.56,"t":"I eventually managed to get a bank loan, but I also had to sell my house to afford to buy out Lania Foods."},{"s":191.06,"e":192.16,"t":"It took a whole year."},{"s":192.73,"e":194.62,"t":"but at least I got my company back."},{"s":195.38,"e":206.43,"t":"By then our sales had skyrocketed and they continued to do so for the next five years. I was able to pay back the loan, buy an even bigger house, then I became businesswoman of the year."},{"s":207.67,"e":211.9,"t":"That was my proudest moment. It made all the hard work worthwhile.","uz":"Bu mening eng faxrli lahzam edi. Butun mashaqqatli mehnat o'zini oqladi."}]},{"n":7,"ins":2,"title":"Swimming instructor","dur":426.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Paul works at a hotel in the south of France."},{"k":"p","t":"He started his job in {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"He particularly likes meeting {2} people there."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul isn't interested in teaching {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"According to Paul, about 50% of all adults can't swim."},{"k":"p","t":"His students have to put their faces into a salad bowl and {4} out below the surface."},{"k":"p","t":"The first thing they do in the pool is to try to {5} in the water with their faces down."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul thinks it's essential to be {6} in the water."},{"k":"p","t":"Most people learn to swim after about 3 lessons."}],"items":[{"a":["1970"],"ps":36.57,"en":41.63,"si":4,"ev":"I started working there in 1970 when I was 18 years old.","hl":"1970","uz":"Men u yerda 1970 yilda, 18 yoshimda ishlay boshladim.","why":"\"Started working there in 1970\" — javob: 1970. \"18\" — yoshi, tuzoq."},{"a":["famous"],"ps":44.31,"en":48.83,"si":6,"ev":"I get to meet a lot of famous people there and um... I guess I enjoy that.","hl":"famous","uz":"U yerda ko'plab mashhur odamlar bilan tanishaman va… menimcha, bu menga yoqadi.","why":"\"Meet a lot of famous people … I enjoy that\" — javob: famous."},{"a":["children"],"ps":60.98,"en":67.23,"si":10,"ev":"There isn't the same challenge teaching children.","hl":"children","uz":"Bolalarni o'rgatishda unchalik qiyinchilik (qiziqish) yo'q.","why":"Pol bolalarga dars berishni qiziq deb bilmaydi: ular deyarli tabiiy suzadi. Kattalar bilan ishlash esa \"much more fun\". Javob: children."},{"a":["breathe"],"ps":121.85,"en":130.17,"si":16,"ev":"Before my students even go into the pool, I teach them how to breathe and to do that I give everyone a salad bowl.","hl":"breathe","uz":"O'quvchilarim basseynga tushishidan oldin ularga nafas olishni o'rgataman, buning uchun har kimga salat kosasi beraman.","why":"Kosadagi suvga yuzni botirib, nafas chiqarish mashqi — javob: breathe."},{"a":["float"],"ps":164.54,"en":173.25,"si":20,"ev":"I tell them that they're going to begin by trying to float with their faces in the water.","hl":"float","uz":"Ularga yuzlarini suvga tiqib, suvda qalqib turishga urinishdan boshlashlarini aytaman.","why":"\"Begin by trying to float with their faces in the water\" — javob: float."},{"a":["confident"],"ps":182.71,"en":187.13,"si":22,"ev":"The swimming technique itself is far less important than feeling confident in the water.","hl":"confident","uz":"Suzish texnikasining o'zi suvda o'zini ishonchli his qilishdan ancha kam ahamiyatga ega.","why":"\"Far less important than feeling confident in the water\" — demak, eng muhimi — confident."}],"segs":[{"s":0.06,"e":4.77,"t":"Exercise 7. You'll hear part of a radio interview with a swimming instructor."},{"s":12.31,"e":21.41,"t":"And now for our sports section, and I have with me today Paul Collison, who is a swimming instructor, with a rather unusual approach."},{"s":21.94,"e":26.59,"t":"Thanks for taking the time during your holiday to come and talk to us Paul. It's very kind of you to invite me."},{"s":27.03,"e":35.42,"t":"Cool. You're THE swimming instructor at the Palace Hotel in the south of France. How long have you been there?"},{"s":36.57,"e":41.63,"t":"I started working there in 1970 when I was 18 years old.","uz":"Men u yerda 1970 yilda, 18 yoshimda ishlay boshladim."},{"s":42.14,"e":43.81,"t":"And you've never moved? Nope."},{"s":44.31,"e":48.83,"t":"I get to meet a lot of famous people there and um... I guess I enjoy that.","uz":"U yerda ko'plab mashhur odamlar bilan tanishaman va… menimcha, bu menga yoqadi."},{"s":49.5,"e":53.63,"t":"and of course a lot of them go there because they want you to teach them to swim."},{"s":54.14,"e":54.62,"t":"One."},{"s":55.58,"e":60.51,"t":"That's true, but I teach plenty of other people too and not all my students are beginners."},{"s":60.98,"e":67.23,"t":"But we're not talking about young children, are we? Not usually. There isn't the same challenge teaching children."},{"s":67.9,"e":77.02,"t":"they have an almost natural ability to swim. Adults are afraid and helping them overcome that is hard but much more fun somehow."},{"s":77.85,"e":87.97,"t":"But don't a lot of people just give up trying to learn once they reach a certain age? Not at all. I get hundreds of calls from people looking for sympathetic instructors."},{"s":88.44,"e":112.09,"t":"I would estimate that about 50% of the adult population can't swim, but they're still keen to learn. So it's just fear that holds them back? Basically, yes. I come across it all the time, and it isn't just beginners. I have students who can swim a bit, but don't make any progress because, like all of them, they hate going underwater. So what's the secret, Paul? Well..."},{"s":112.57,"e":116.64,"t":"You've got to relax in the water and that means that you must control your breathing."},{"s":117.21,"e":121.41,"t":"And I understand you have a special technique to help people do that. Yes."},{"s":121.85,"e":130.17,"t":"Before my students even go into the pool, I teach them how to breathe and to do that I give everyone a salad bowl.","uz":"O'quvchilarim basseynga tushishidan oldin ularga nafas olishni o'rgataman, buning uchun har kimga salat kosasi beraman."},{"s":130.84,"e":135.1,"t":"Right. Everyone in the group gets one of these. Each full of water."},{"s":135.96,"e":149.57,"t":"First, I get them to breathe slowly through the nose and mouth, just normal control breathing. To calm them. And then they all have to put their faces in the bowl and breathe out underwater."},{"s":150.07,"e":163.68,"t":"How does it go? Well, they're all terrified at first. So we repeat the exercise many times and in the end they become quite competitive about who can keep their face down the longest. And that means they've started to forget about their fear. Exactly."},{"s":164.54,"e":173.25,"t":"When I'm sure they're more confident about breathing, I move the group into the pool and I tell them that they're going to begin by trying to float with their faces in the water."},{"s":174.17,"e":181.89,"t":"Once I'm sure they're okay, I start them off and I teach different swimming strokes to different pupils, depending on which one I think they'll find easiest."},{"s":182.71,"e":187.13,"t":"The swimming technique itself is far less important than feeling confident in the water.","uz":"Suzish texnikasining o'zi suvda o'zini ishonchli his qilishdan ancha kam ahamiyatga ega."},{"s":187.58,"e":191.71,"t":"Great! So how many lessons would I need to learn to swim?"},{"s":192.63,"e":196.32,"t":"Well, all my lessons are an hour long."},{"s":196.76,"e":201.21,"t":"And generally it just takes three to overcome the fear and get people swimming."},{"s":201.88,"e":203.74,"t":"A few never make it, but..."},{"s":204.22,"e":208.41,"t":"I'd say 90% end up swimmers. So there's hope for us all yet."},{"s":208.89,"e":209.95,"t":"and now on to Michelle's"}]},{"n":8,"ins":2,"title":"Dolphins","dur":443.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Dolphins have been known to protect swimmers from sharks by getting into a circle."},{"k":"p","t":"Dolphins and humans have {1} of the same size."},{"k":"p","t":"Swimming with dolphins can help common problems like {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Some people think dolphins are able to recognise human {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Dolphins have been used to teach children to {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Swimming with dolphins is used as a {5} in projects with children."},{"k":"p","t":"In one jaw, dolphins have as many as 52 teeth."},{"k":"p","t":"Dolphins make use of sound waves to find fish."},{"k":"p","t":"Dolphins can be caught in {6} or damaged by pollution."}],"items":[{"a":["brain"],"ps":51.42,"en":57.41,"si":6,"ev":"They are, in fact, the only animals in the world whose brains match ours in terms of size.","hl":"brains","uz":"Ular, aslida, dunyoda miyasi hajmi bo'yicha biznikiga teng keladigan yagona hayvonlardir.","why":"\"Brains match ours in terms of size\" → \"brains of the same size\". Javob: brain(s)."},{"a":["stress"],"ps":71.03,"en":78.14,"si":9,"ev":"with a group of dolphins, for example, is a recognized medical activity for everyday problems such as stress.","hl":"stress","uz":"…delfinlar to'dasi bilan suzish stress kabi kundalik muammolar uchun tan olingan tibbiy mashg'ulotdir.","why":"\"Everyday problems such as stress\" — javob: stress."},{"a":["feelings"],"ps":92.31,"en":94.94,"si":13,"ev":"because they were able to read her feelings.","hl":"feelings","uz":"…chunki ular uning his-tuyg'ularini sezib olishga qodir edi.","why":"\"Able to read her feelings\" → \"recognise human feelings\". Javob: feelings."},{"a":["read"],"ps":111.8,"en":116.54,"si":19,"ev":"Dolphins are being used to help children who are slow learners learn to read.","hl":"read","uz":"Delfinlar sekin o'zlashtiradigan bolalarga o'qishni o'rgatishda yordam berish uchun ishlatilmoqda.","why":"\"Help children … learn to read\" — javob: read."},{"a":["reward"],"ps":132.82,"en":134.65,"si":23,"ev":"and they see this as a reward.","hl":"reward","uz":"…va ular buni mukofot deb bilishadi.","why":"Bolalar to'g'ri javob bersa, delfinlar bilan ko'proq suzishadi — \"they see this as a reward\". Javob: reward."},{"a":["nets"],"ps":201.08,"en":205.82,"si":39,"ev":"But we trap them in fishing nets and we pollute the water they swim in.","hl":"nets","uz":"Lekin biz ularni baliq ovlash to'rlariga ilintiramiz va ular suzadigan suvni ifloslantiramiz.","why":"\"Trap them in fishing nets\" → \"caught in nets\". Javob: nets."}],"segs":[{"s":12.57,"e":20.22,"t":"for our last news item today a special report from Diane Hasson on an animal that is rapidly becoming known as man's best friend."},{"s":20.73,"e":21.34,"t":"the dolphin."},{"s":23.22,"e":32.13,"t":"Last week, a 28-year-old diver who went swimming in the Red Sea with a group of dolphins learned the hard way just how caring these creatures can be."},{"s":33.59,"e":41.12,"t":"When the diver was suddenly attacked by a shark, they saved him by forming a circle around him and frightening the shark away."},{"s":42.04,"e":44.51,"t":"It's not the first time such a rescue has happened."},{"s":44.98,"e":50.85,"t":"And it's been known for some time that dolphins will do for humans what they do for their own kind."},{"s":51.42,"e":57.41,"t":"They are, in fact, the only animals in the world whose brains match ours in terms of size.","uz":"Ular, aslida, dunyoda miyasi hajmi bo'yicha biznikiga teng keladigan yagona hayvonlardir."},{"s":57.85,"e":64.61,"t":"and their intelligence and ability to feel emotion continue to fascinate scientists and doctors alike."},{"s":66.52,"e":70.24,"t":"For some time now, their healing powers have been well known."},{"s":71.03,"e":78.14,"t":"with a group of dolphins, for example, is a recognized medical activity for everyday problems such as stress.","uz":"…delfinlar to'dasi bilan suzish stress kabi kundalik muammolar uchun tan olingan tibbiy mashg'ulotdir."},{"s":79.32,"e":83.33,"t":"Some dolphins are playing a far more serious medical role for us than that."},{"s":84.63,"e":88.22,"t":"Amanda Morton, who suffered from a life-threatening illness,"},{"s":88.7,"e":91.84,"t":"argued that being with dolphins saved her life."},{"s":92.31,"e":94.94,"t":"because they were able to read her feelings.","uz":"…chunki ular uning his-tuyg'ularini sezib olishga qodir edi."},{"s":95.54,"e":98.62,"t":"They knew how I was feeling,\" she was quoted as saying."},{"s":99.51,"e":102.27,"t":"And it's the idea that they actually care."},{"s":102.84,"e":106.11,"t":"that they are gentle happy creatures that want to befriend us."},{"s":106.62,"e":108.99,"t":"which has led to projects with children as well."},{"s":109.88,"e":111.26,"t":"in one such project."},{"s":111.8,"e":116.54,"t":"Dolphins are being used to help children who are slow learners learn to read.","uz":"Delfinlar sekin o'zlashtiradigan bolalarga o'qishni o'rgatishda yordam berish uchun ishlatilmoqda."},{"s":117.21,"e":121.05,"t":"The dolphins do things like carrying small boards on their noses."},{"s":121.82,"e":126.11,"t":"These boards show words or pictures which the children are asked to identify."},{"s":126.87,"e":132.22,"t":"When the children get it right, they spend more time swimming with the dolphins and touching them."},{"s":132.82,"e":134.65,"t":"and they see this as a reward.","uz":"…va ular buni mukofot deb bilishadi."},{"s":135.35,"e":139.52,"t":"So what is it that makes contact with dolphins so powerful?"},{"s":140.34,"e":142.49,"t":"They certainly have an engaging smile."},{"s":143.16,"e":148.8,"t":"In each jaw, they have up to 52 teeth, but rather than frightening us to death,"},{"s":149.3,"e":151.97,"t":"It's one of the warmest greetings in the world."},{"s":152.89,"e":155.42,"t":"They're also fantastic swimmers to watch."},{"s":156.06,"e":163.13,"t":"The spotted dolphin has been observed reaching 20 miles an hour and keeping this up for two days at a time."},{"s":163.86,"e":172.35,"t":"and they know they're good at it. So they show off in front of humans by diving in and out of the water and showing us just how much fun they're having."},{"s":173.11,"e":174.88,"t":"They're great communicators too."},{"s":175.64,"e":178.69,"t":"they make all kinds of fascinating high-pitched noises."},{"s":179.26,"e":185.5,"t":"They catch fish, for example, by sending out sound waves, which tell them everything they need to know."},{"s":186.04,"e":187.97,"t":"Where it is, what it is,"},{"s":188.47,"e":189.57,"t":"and how big it is."},{"s":191.48,"e":194.4,"t":"The only creatures that concern dolphins, in fact,"},{"s":194.84,"e":196.67,"t":"are sharks and man."},{"s":198.01,"e":200.45,"t":"we don't necessarily harm them on purpose."},{"s":201.08,"e":205.82,"t":"But we trap them in fishing nets and we pollute the water they swim in.","uz":"Lekin biz ularni baliq ovlash to'rlariga ilintiramiz va ular suzadigan suvni ifloslantiramiz."},{"s":206.78,"e":210.65,"t":"Pollution, in fact, is one of the dolphin's greatest problems."},{"s":212.15,"e":212.61,"t":"So..."},{"s":213.08,"e":214.75,"t":"with all the good they do for us."},{"s":215.45,"e":217.79,"t":"Isn't it time we started caring about them?"}]},{"n":9,"ins":2,"title":"Animal communication","dur":509.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Bees do a special dance to communicate where to find food."},{"k":"p","t":"Although parrots seem to speak, they are only {1} the human sounds."},{"k":"p","t":"Primates can communicate a few basic {2} using simple sounds."},{"k":"p","t":"Monkeys have not been observed to use any kind of {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Although dolphins can make vowel sounds, they cannot accurately imitate our {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Amazingly, dolphins demonstrate {5} of when phrases should be used."},{"k":"p","t":"The songs of the bottle-nosed whale have many of the characteristics of human speech."},{"k":"p","t":"Indeed, a young child needs enough {6} with other people to develop speech."}],"items":[{"a":["copying"],"ps":77.91,"en":87.61,"si":8,"ev":"Such animals are only capable of copying the sounds of human speech.","hl":"copying","uz":"Bunday hayvonlar faqat inson nutqi tovushlarini takrorlashga qodir.","why":"\"Only capable of copying the sounds\" — to'tiqushlar faqat ko'chirib oladi, tushunmaydi. Javob: copying."},{"a":["ideas"],"ps":93.08,"en":106.43,"si":10,"ev":"Monkeys, apes and other primates are capable of communicating a small number of basic ideas using a range of simple sounds.","hl":"ideas","uz":"Maymunlar va boshqa primatlar oddiy tovushlar yordamida bir nechta oddiy fikrni yetkaza oladi.","why":"\"A small number of basic ideas\" → \"a few basic ideas\". Javob: ideas."},{"a":["grammar"],"ps":106.9,"en":132.64,"si":11,"ev":"None of the groups of monkeys observed so far have developed any form of grammar, and so we cannot call this a language.","hl":"grammar","uz":"Hozircha kuzatilgan maymunlarning hech bir guruhida grammatikaning biror shakli shakllanmagan, shuning uchun buni til deb atay olmaymiz.","why":"\"Any form of grammar\" — javob: grammar."},{"a":["consonants"],"ps":146.14,"en":156.35,"si":14,"ev":"They can manage the vowel sounds A, E, I, O, U and so on, but lack the necessary voice equipment to reproduce our consonants.","hl":"consonants","uz":"Ular A, E, I, O, U kabi unli tovushlarni chiqara oladi, lekin undosh tovushlarimizni takrorlash uchun kerakli ovoz apparati yo'q.","why":"Unlilar (vowels) — chiqara oladi; undoshlar (consonants) — yo'q. Javob: consonants."},{"a":["awareness"],"ps":167.64,"en":177.28,"si":17,"ev":"is that dolphins do show an awareness of when to use such phrases and in this sense are actually trying to communicate with humans.","hl":"awareness","uz":"…delfinlar bunday iboralarni qachon ishlatish kerakligini anglashini ko'rsatadi.","why":"\"Show an awareness of when to use such phrases\" — javob: awareness."},{"a":["contact"],"ps":236.41,"en":247.29,"si":24,"ev":"If for any reason a young child does not get enough contact with other people between the ages of one and four, he or she may never fully develop the power of speech.","hl":"contact","uz":"Agar biror sababga ko'ra bola bir yoshdan to'rt yoshgacha boshqa odamlar bilan yetarli muloqotda bo'lmasa, nutqi hech qachon to'liq rivojlanmasligi mumkin.","why":"\"Enough contact with other people\" — javob: contact."}],"segs":[{"s":2.26,"e":7.84,"t":"You will hear part of a radio talk for young people about animals communicating with each other."},{"s":17.27,"e":38.81,"t":"If I asked you what the difference is between animals and human beings, you might think for a bit and then suggest something about the fact that humans can speak to each other using a language, or in some cases more than one language, and in a way you would be right. But that is not the whole story by any means."},{"s":39.26,"e":48.13,"t":"Many animals can communicate in surprisingly complicated ways, but they never quite achieve the range and depth of human languages."},{"s":48.73,"e":61.12,"t":"At the simplest level, several kinds of insect, including bees, have been observed performing a special dance to tell each other where they can find nectar and pollen, which is their food."},{"s":61.91,"e":65.57,"t":"This of course does not mean that they are using a language."},{"s":66.62,"e":70.01,"t":"They are all the same communicating something."},{"s":70.74,"e":74.3,"t":"Many people think that certain birds like parrots can speak."},{"s":75.19,"e":77.47,"t":"This is in fact not true."},{"s":77.91,"e":87.61,"t":"Such animals are only capable of copying the sounds of human speech, but have no understanding of these sounds, and generally use them at the wrong time."},{"s":88.22,"e":92.51,"t":"There is also no apparent logic in the way they select what to copy either."},{"s":93.08,"e":106.43,"t":"On the other hand, monkeys, apes and other primates are capable of communicating a small number of basic ideas using a range of simple sounds that are recognized by other members of their social group."},{"s":106.9,"e":132.64,"t":"Unfortunately, though, none of the groups of monkeys observed so far have developed any form of grammar, and so we cannot call this a language. However, some apes, chimpanzees in particular, can be trained to understand and respond to certain spoken commands by humans. But so far, none have attempted to copy our speech. Now, there is one kind of animal that does just this."},{"s":133.11,"e":136.73,"t":"Although not many people can understand what they are saying."},{"s":137.37,"e":145.44,"t":"Dolphins have different shaped mouths to humans and as a result they are unable to make all the sounds that we can make."},{"s":146.14,"e":156.35,"t":"They can manage the vowel sounds A, E, I, O, U and so on, but lack the necessary voice equipment to reproduce our consonants.","uz":"Ular A, E, I, O, U kabi unli tovushlarni chiqara oladi, lekin undosh tovushlarimizni takrorlash uchun kerakli ovoz apparati yo'q."},{"s":156.98,"e":163.81,"t":"Thus, a simple phrase like \"Hello, how are you?\" becomes \"E-O-R-U\"."},{"s":164.7,"e":167.1,"t":"What makes these noises more amazing?"},{"s":167.64,"e":177.28,"t":"is that dolphins do show an awareness of when to use such phrases and in this sense are actually trying to communicate with humans.","uz":"…delfinlar bunday iboralarni qachon ishlatish kerakligini anglashini ko'rsatadi."},{"s":177.85,"e":183.9,"t":"but by far the most remarkable form of animal communication are the songs of whales."},{"s":184.47,"e":195.36,"t":"These are fast clicking and squeaking noises that whales make underwater and the sounds themselves actually contain more information than human speech."},{"s":196.41,"e":205.25,"t":"Scientists have noticed that some whales repeat certain long phrases of sounds, and this is in fact why they are called songs."},{"s":205.94,"e":214.65,"t":"of particular interest is a species called the bottlenose whale, whose songs have many of the characteristics of human speech."},{"s":215.19,"e":227.29,"t":"But at the end of the day, we are the only species that have developed proper grammatical languages. And most experts now agree that this is because of the large communities that we live in."},{"s":227.99,"e":235.74,"t":"where a child growing up can hear hundreds of different examples of his or her language being spoken every day."},{"s":236.41,"e":247.29,"t":"If for any reason a young child does not get enough contact with other people between the ages of one and four, he or she may never fully develop the power of speech.","uz":"Agar biror sababga ko'ra bola bir yoshdan to'rt yoshgacha boshqa odamlar bilan yetarli muloqotda bo'lmasa, nutqi hech qachon to'liq rivojlanmasligi mumkin."},{"s":248.06,"e":254.33,"t":"can imagine that if whales or dolphins did start living in large communities then well..."}]},{"n":10,"ins":2,"title":"Food packaging","dur":411.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Gordon says that, until quite recently, most food packaging consisted of a brown paper bag."},{"k":"p","t":"Plastic packaging is supposed to keep food {1} and so make it better."},{"k":"p","t":"Maggie Forbes is in charge of packaging and {2} for a chain of supermarkets."},{"k":"p","t":"She says that 30-50% of food is wasted in countries without modern packaging and {3} systems."},{"k":"p","t":"Maggie claims plastic packaging saves money, but Gordon suggests that it is a huge {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Maggie says food stored in the {5} should be wrapped in plastic to prevent loss of water content."},{"k":"p","t":"She points out that glass and stone containers are easily broken and very heavy."},{"k":"p","t":"Gordon is worried that plastic bags have a very bad effect on the {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["fresher"],"ps":42.1,"en":44.89,"si":5,"ev":"We're told this makes the food better and keeps it fresher.","hl":"fresher","uz":"Bizga aytishlaricha, bu ovqatni yaxshilaydi va uni yangiroq saqlaydi.","why":"\"Keeps it fresher\" — javob: fresher (qiyosiy daraja, \"fresh\" emas)."},{"a":["presentation"],"ps":46.1,"en":53.34,"si":6,"ev":"Now, with me in the studio today is Maggie Forbes, who is head of packaging and presentation for the supermarket chain Wostens.","hl":"presentation","uz":"Studiyada men bilan Wostens supermarket tarmog'ining qadoqlash va taqdimot bo'limi boshlig'i Meggi Forbs.","why":"\"Head of packaging and presentation\" — javob: presentation."},{"a":["transport"],"ps":66.36,"en":75.13,"si":10,"ev":"In countries which don't have modern packaging and transport systems, between 30% and 50% of all food deteriorates before it can be eaten.","hl":"transport","uz":"Zamonaviy qadoqlash va transport tizimi bo'lmagan mamlakatlarda barcha oziq-ovqatning 30–50 foizi yeyilmasidan oldin buziladi.","why":"\"Modern packaging and transport systems\" — javob: transport."},{"a":["waste"],"ps":96.38,"en":105.18,"si":14,"ev":"Most of the plastics we see today are just thrown away and far from being a saving, it seems a huge waste.","hl":"waste","uz":"Bugun ko'rayotgan plastiklarning ko'pi shunchaki tashlab yuboriladi; tejash u yoqda tursin, bu juda katta isrofdek tuyuladi.","why":"Gordon: tejash emas, \"a huge waste\". Javob: waste."},{"a":["freezer"],"ps":117.62,"en":123.87,"si":17,"ev":"And if you want to chill food successfully in your freezer, you need a plastic which doesn't let water vapor through.","hl":"freezer","uz":"Ovqatni muzlatgichda muvaffaqiyatli sovutmoqchi bo'lsangiz, suv bug'ini o'tkazmaydigan plastik kerak.","why":"\"In your freezer … plastic which doesn't let water vapour through\" — javob: freezer."},{"a":["environment"],"ps":191.06,"en":192.86,"si":29,"ev":"This is so bad for the environment.","hl":"environment","uz":"Bu atrof-muhit uchun juda yomon.","why":"Plastik paketlar yer ostida 100 yildan ortiq parchalanadi — \"bad for the environment\". Javob: environment."}],"segs":[{"s":1.85,"e":6.08,"t":"You'll hear a radio program on which the host, Gordon Joyce,"},{"s":6.55,"e":9.95,"t":"talks to a woman called Maggie Forbes about food packaging."},{"s":20.18,"e":25.6,"t":"You don't have to go far back to find a time when the most widely used packaging for food was a brown paper bag."},{"s":26.26,"e":35.36,"t":"In fact, I remember as a boy some 40 years ago when everything from bacon to biscuits to butter was measured out and then wrapped just well enough to get it home."},{"s":36.22,"e":41.02,"t":"Since then we've seen the development of plastics and other materials for packaging our food."},{"s":42.1,"e":44.89,"t":"We're told this makes the food better and keeps it fresher.","uz":"Bizga aytishlaricha, bu ovqatni yaxshilaydi va uni yangiroq saqlaydi."},{"s":46.1,"e":53.34,"t":"Now, with me in the studio today is Maggie Forbes, who is head of packaging and presentation for the supermarket chain Wostens.","uz":"Studiyada men bilan Wostens supermarket tarmog'ining qadoqlash va taqdimot bo'limi boshlig'i Meggi Forbs."},{"s":54.07,"e":54.85,"t":"Welcome Maggie."},{"s":55.45,"e":61.89,"t":"Can you tell us, does the new packaging really help us? Or does it create problems for us? Well Gordon..."},{"s":62.33,"e":65.63,"t":"It's very easy to see the benefits of modern food packaging."},{"s":66.36,"e":75.13,"t":"In countries which don't have modern packaging and transport systems, between 30% and 50% of all food deteriorates before it can be eaten.","uz":"Zamonaviy qadoqlash va transport tizimi bo'lmagan mamlakatlarda barcha oziq-ovqatning 30–50 foizi yeyilmasidan oldin buziladi."},{"s":75.77,"e":77.82,"t":"It was probably the same when you were a boy."},{"s":78.36,"e":90.37,"t":"Nowadays in Britain and across Europe, only 2-3% of food is thrown away. It saves a lot of money. That may be so, but do we need so much of today's modern packaging?"},{"s":91.0,"e":95.33,"t":"With freezers at home, surely we only need the brown bags to curry food home."},{"s":96.38,"e":105.18,"t":"Most of the plastics we see today are just thrown away and far from being a saving, it seems a huge waste. I think you're being unfair there."},{"s":105.69,"e":110.17,"t":"Brown paper bags do very little to keep food fresh, clean or wholesome."},{"s":110.97,"e":116.89,"t":"don't stop food drying out and they can actually encourage the bacteria which make food go bad quickly."},{"s":117.62,"e":123.87,"t":"And if you want to chill food successfully in your freezer, you need a plastic which doesn't let water vapor through.","uz":"Ovqatni muzlatgichda muvaffaqiyatli sovutmoqchi bo'lsangiz, suv bug'ini o'tkazmaydigan plastik kerak."},{"s":124.44,"e":136.57,"t":"Without a wrapping like that, food loses most of its water content in the freezer and is unedible. OK, so they may be useful in the freezer, but what about products like milk, which aren't frozen?"},{"s":137.24,"e":141.95,"t":"Surely glass or even stone bottles were just as effective and could be used again."},{"s":142.39,"e":146.11,"t":"Yes, they were certainly effective, but also very heavy."},{"s":146.58,"e":151.33,"t":"I assure you, you wouldn't want to carry all of your food home in glass jars."},{"s":151.77,"e":157.15,"t":"Glass and stone jars are also easy to break, as you will probably remember from your boyhood."},{"s":157.59,"e":161.09,"t":"The benefit of plastic is that it's light and long-lasting."},{"s":161.62,"e":166.14,"t":"It also keeps in smells. You wouldn't want your milk smelling of fish, would you?"},{"s":166.74,"e":169.31,"t":"And lastly, it keeps out bacteria."},{"s":169.91,"e":176.89,"t":"If we seal fresh food in good condition in plastic, then it's certain to be free from contamination when you get it home."},{"s":177.66,"e":183.87,"t":"You probably won't remember, but in your boyhood, food poisoning was much more common than it is today."},{"s":184.7,"e":190.46,"t":"Plastic takes so long to break down in the ground. Plastic bags take over a hundred years."},{"s":191.06,"e":192.86,"t":"This is so bad for the environment.","uz":"Bu atrof-muhit uchun juda yomon."},{"s":193.85,"e":199.01,"t":"I believe that until we use less packaging, the future of our world looks grim."},{"s":199.9,"e":206.08,"t":"But now we've run out of time, so perhaps you could come again, Maggie, and we'll continue this fascinating discussion."}]},{"n":11,"ins":2,"title":"Iberian lynx","dur":248.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The Iberian lynx is also known as the Spanish lynx. The Smilodon, or Sabre Toothed Tiger became extinct 10000 years ago."},{"k":"p","t":"In recent years the number of Iberian lynx has fallen by {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Male Iberian lynx can weigh up to {2} kilograms."},{"k":"p","t":"The main part of an Iberian lynx's diet consists of {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"During bad weather the Iberian lynx will stay in {4} or trees."},{"k":"p","t":"Due to a change in the law it is no longer legal to {5} them."},{"k":"p","t":"Since 2005 6 have been born in the Donana Breeding Centre."},{"k":"p","t":"The World Wildlife Foundation has repeatedly asked the Spanish government to close a {6} which goes through the national park."}],"items":[{"a":["400"],"ps":30.42,"en":33.66,"si":3,"ev":"which is around 400 less than there were in 2000.","hl":"400","uz":"…bu 2000 yildagidan taxminan 400 taga kam.","why":"Hozir 100 ga yaqin qolgan, 2000 yildagidan \"around 400 less\". Javob: 400. \"100\" — hozirgi soni, tuzoq."},{"a":["27"],"ps":50.55,"en":57.98,"si":6,"ev":"Males can weigh between 12.9 and 27 kilograms, which is about half the weight of the average Eurasian lynx.","hl":"27","uz":"Erkaklari 12,9 dan 27 kilogrammgacha bo'lishi mumkin — bu yevroosiyo silovsinining o'rtacha vaznining yarmicha.","why":"\"Up to\" — eng yuqori chegara: 27. \"12.9\" — eng past vazn, tuzoq. (Transkriptdagi \"Nails\" — aslida \"Males\".)"},{"a":["rabbits"],"ps":70.58,"en":82.11,"si":9,"ev":"Rabbits would account for more than 70% of the lynx's food, but due to Spain's declining rabbit population, the lynx has been forced to attack larger mammals such as young deer or roebuck.","hl":"Rabbits","uz":"Quyonlar silovsin ovqatining 70 foizidan ko'pini tashkil qiladi, lekin Ispaniyada quyonlar kamaygani sababli u kattaroq sutemizuvchilarga hujum qilishga majbur bo'lgan.","why":"\"More than 70% of the lynx's food\" — asosiy qismi: rabbits. Kiyiklar (deer) — majburan, tuzoq."},{"a":["caves"],"ps":108.86,"en":112.16,"si":16,"ev":"In extreme weather, they take shelter in caves or trees.","hl":"caves","uz":"Juda og'ir ob-havoda ular g'orlarda yoki daraxtlarda panoh topadi.","why":"\"Take shelter in caves or trees\" — javob: caves."},{"a":["hunt"],"ps":137.18,"en":141.28,"si":20,"ev":"although it is under legal protection and it is no longer legal to hunt them.","hl":"hunt","uz":"…garchi u qonun himoyasida bo'lsa va endi ularni ovlash qonuniy bo'lmasa-da.","why":"\"No longer legal to hunt them\" — javob: hunt."},{"a":["road"],"ps":222.17,"en":230.43,"si":32,"ev":"The World Wildlife Foundation has been urging Spanish authorities for over two years to close a road which crosses the Donana National Park.","hl":"road","uz":"Butunjahon yovvoyi tabiat fondi ikki yildan ortiq Ispaniya hukumatini Donyana milliy bog'idan o'tadigan yo'lni yopishga undab kelmoqda.","why":"\"Close a road which crosses the Doñana National Park\" — javob: road. \"Motorway\" — rejalashtirilgan yangi yo'l haqida, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":2.3,"e":5.53,"t":"You'll hear a talk about an endangered species."},{"s":7.38,"e":23.29,"t":"The most endangered cat species is the Iberian lynx, sometimes called the Spanish lynx. Should this species die out, it would be the first feline extinction since the Smilodon, commonly known as the Sabre-toothed tiger 10,000 years ago."},{"s":24.28,"e":29.89,"t":"Recent studies estimate the number of surviving Iberian lynx to be as few as 100."},{"s":30.42,"e":33.66,"t":"which is around 400 less than there were in 2000.","uz":"…bu 2000 yildagidan taxminan 400 taga kam."},{"s":34.84,"e":36.93,"t":"What does an Iberian Lynx look like?"},{"s":38.04,"e":49.15,"t":"Their leopard-like spots particularly distinguish it from its cousin the Eurasian lynx, and it is also smaller, with a head and body length between 85 and 110 cm."},{"s":50.55,"e":57.98,"t":"Males can weigh between 12.9 and 27 kilograms, which is about half the weight of the average Eurasian lynx.","uz":"Erkaklari 12,9 dan 27 kilogrammgacha bo'lishi mumkin — bu yevroosiyo silovsinining o'rtacha vaznining yarmicha."},{"s":59.51,"e":62.69,"t":"The lynx can live up to a period of 13 years."},{"s":64.02,"e":69.82,"t":"Iberian lynx's size means that it typically hunts for animals no bigger than rabbits or hares."},{"s":70.58,"e":82.11,"t":"Rabbits would account for more than 70% of the lynx's food, but due to Spain's declining rabbit population, the lynx has been forced to attack larger mammals such as young deer or roebuck.","uz":"Quyonlar silovsin ovqatining 70 foizidan ko'pini tashkil qiladi, lekin Ispaniyada quyonlar kamaygani sababli u kattaroq sutemizuvchilarga hujum qilishga majbur bo'lgan."},{"s":83.45,"e":85.31,"t":"The Iberian lynx hunt alone."},{"s":85.78,"e":89.6,"t":"and follows its prey even up to distances of 100 kilometers."},{"s":90.62,"e":93.66,"t":"or it lies in wait for its prey for many hours."},{"s":94.58,"e":99.81,"t":"It uses the four sets of whiskers on its ears and chin to sense its victim."},{"s":101.91,"e":103.13,"t":"are active at night."},{"s":104.02,"e":107.93,"t":"stay active in winter and their fur becomes thicker and paler."},{"s":108.86,"e":112.16,"t":"In extreme weather, they take shelter in caves or trees.","uz":"Juda og'ir ob-havoda ular g'orlarda yoki daraxtlarda panoh topadi."},{"s":114.36,"e":123.77,"t":"The Iberian Lynx was once widespread all over the peninsula but is now restricted to very small areas, mainly mountainous areas covered with vegetation."},{"s":124.76,"e":131.13,"t":"Its drastic decline over recent decades is due to loss of habitat, reduction in prey,"},{"s":131.61,"e":136.64,"t":"and high non-natural mortality from road kills, predator control and hunting."},{"s":137.18,"e":141.28,"t":"although it is under legal protection and it is no longer legal to hunt them.","uz":"…garchi u qonun himoyasida bo'lsa va endi ularni ovlash qonuniy bo'lmasa-da."},{"s":142.71,"e":157.21,"t":"It was recently thought that the only breeding Iberian lynxes were in the Donana National Park in Andalusia, southern Spain, but in 2007 a previously unknown population was discovered in Castilla de la Mancha in central Spain."},{"s":159.06,"e":165.02,"t":"In March 2005, for the first time, Iberian lynxes managed to breed in captivity."},{"s":166.07,"e":169.28,"t":"Three healthy cubs were born at a breeding center in Doniana."},{"s":170.49,"e":175.49,"t":"In 2009, it was announced that three more cubs had been born in the same centre."},{"s":176.54,"e":181.6,"t":"Simply, a mother will give birth to three cubs after a gestation period of 60 days."},{"s":183.67,"e":192.77,"t":"Iberian Lynx conservation is now underway through political campaigning and lobbying from individuals and organizations such as SOS Lynx."},{"s":193.91,"e":196.83,"t":"Important progress has been made in a number of ways."},{"s":197.5,"e":200.25,"t":"the foundation of the breeding program in Andalusia."},{"s":200.82,"e":204.41,"t":"Prevention of further construction in areas the Iberian lynx lives"},{"s":204.86,"e":215.07,"t":"and the halting of proposals for new roads in problematic areas, such as the new motorway that had been planned between Quidade Real in La Mancha and Cordoba in Andalusia."},{"s":217.08,"e":221.28,"t":"despite these successes, challenges and conflicting pressures remain."},{"s":222.17,"e":230.43,"t":"The World Wildlife Foundation has been urging Spanish authorities for over two years to close a road which crosses the Donana National Park.","uz":"Butunjahon yovvoyi tabiat fondi ikki yildan ortiq Ispaniya hukumatini Donyana milliy bog'idan o'tadigan yo'lni yopishga undab kelmoqda."},{"s":231.32,"e":233.98,"t":"Callum Rankin of the WWF says"},{"s":234.49,"e":242.85,"t":"With such a small population, the accidental loss of just one individual on the road brings the species closer to the brink of extinction."}]},{"n":12,"ins":2,"title":"Musical instrument maker","dur":417.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Richard's first ambition was to be a {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"According to Richard, personal {2} provide him with most of his overseas clients."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard says that he is involved in {3} organs, as well as building and selling them."},{"k":"p","t":"In terms of raw materials, only the {4} that Richard uses comes from Britain."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard's new workshop will be in a building that was once used as a school."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard will have to work in a small {5} as well as in his new workshop."},{"k":"p","t":"The new workshop will be perfect for the instruments Richard makes because it is a {6} place."}],"items":[{"a":["composer"],"ps":29.66,"en":54.59,"si":3,"ev":"As a child I had a good teacher who wrote her own music and I always wanted to be a composer too.","hl":"composer","uz":"Bolaligimda o'zi musiqa yozadigan yaxshi o'qituvchim bor edi va men ham doim bastakor bo'lishni xohlardim.","why":"Birinchi orzusi — composer. Ota-onasi esa cholg'u yasashni o'qishga ko'ndirgan; \"businessman\" — hech qachon niyat qilmagan narsa, tuzoq."},{"a":["contacts"],"ps":92.15,"en":104.13,"si":6,"ev":"Most of my commissions are from overseas clients and they're nearly all the result of personal contacts.","hl":"contacts","uz":"Buyurtmalarimning ko'pi chet ellik mijozlardan va deyarli barchasi shaxsiy tanishlar orqali keladi.","why":"\"The result of personal contacts\" — javob: contacts. Reklamadan (advertising) deyarli foydalanmaydi."},{"a":["mending"],"ps":104.6,"en":115.58,"si":7,"ev":"The most profitable part of my business is actually mending organs.","hl":"mending","uz":"Biznesimning eng daromadli qismi — aslida organlarni ta'mirlash.","why":"Qurish va sotishdan tashqari — \"mending organs\". Javob: mending."},{"a":["wood"],"ps":125.5,"en":152.86,"si":10,"ev":"I get the wood from Britain, but most of the other components come from France or Germany.","hl":"wood","uz":"Yog'ochni Britaniyadan olaman, boshqa qismlarning ko'pi Fransiya yoki Germaniyadan keladi.","why":"Britaniyadan faqat \"wood\". Javob: wood."},{"a":["museum"],"ps":153.85,"en":175.97,"si":11,"ev":"In return for using the workshop, I've agreed to spend forty days a year working as a museum attendant.","hl":"museum","uz":"Ustaxonadan foydalanish evaziga yiliga qirq kun muzey nazoratchisi bo'lib ishlashga rozi bo'ldim.","why":"\"Working as a museum attendant\" — kichik muzeyda ishlaydi. Javob: museum."},{"a":["dry"],"ps":188.86,"en":192.57,"si":14,"ev":"It's very easy for the instruments to get damaged so the environment must be dry.","hl":"dry","uz":"Cholg'ular juda oson shikastlanadi, shuning uchun muhit quruq bo'lishi kerak.","why":"Keyingi gap: \"The new workshop is perfect in that respect\" — ya'ni quruq. Javob: dry."}],"segs":[{"s":1.75,"e":8.35,"t":"You'll hear an interview with a man called Richard Porter, who's a maker of musical instruments called organs."},{"s":15.48,"e":22.59,"t":"Good evening, and welcome to the programme where, as you know, we go out and talk to people who run their own companies."},{"s":23.35,"e":28.83,"t":"Today we're talking to Richard Porter, who makes large concert organs as a profession."},{"s":29.66,"e":54.59,"t":"Richard, tell us, just how did you get into this area of work? Well, I played the piano and as a child I had a good teacher who wrote her own music and I always wanted to be a composer too. However, my parents persuaded me that what I needed to do was go to college and study how to make musical instruments rather than play them because they saw more of a future in that. And now I make the organs which are played in churches and concert halls all around the world."},{"s":54.9,"e":80.44,"t":"The one thing that I never intended to do was become a businessman, which is what I am now, really, as well as being an instrument maker. So when did you start making organs? About five years ago. I started from a room in my house, but now I have my own workshop. So it must pay? Well, an organ sells at £9,500, which means around £3,500 profit for me, I suppose. And how long does it take to build one?"},{"s":80.89,"e":91.55,"t":"It might take me three months to complete one. When I say three months, I mean three months of working 70 hours a week. Although that sounds a lot. I have to say I don't mind, because I love the work."},{"s":92.15,"e":104.13,"t":"and I get to meet lots of interesting people. Most of my commissions are from overseas clients and they're nearly all the result of personal contacts. I rarely use advertising these days. So you make a living out of it? Not really."},{"s":104.6,"e":115.58,"t":"The most profitable part of my business is actually mending organs. Generally old large ones, so they can be used for concerts and recording sessions. That can earn me up to £300 each time."},{"s":116.02,"e":121.53,"t":"Which is just as well, because I do need to have money available to buy the raw materials for the larger organs."},{"s":122.3,"e":124.83,"t":"There's a lot of investment to make before I can start to build."},{"s":125.5,"e":152.86,"t":"I get the wood from Britain, but most of the other components come from France or Germany. And I understand you've made a big decision recently? Yeah. I've decided to take the opportunity to move my workshop to a former schoolroom that has become available in Lincolnshire, about a hundred miles away. So you're moving house as well? Yeah. We're moving there in three months' time. Tell me about the new workshop. Oh, it's a lovely old building attached to the town hall in a small market town."},{"s":153.85,"e":175.97,"t":"In return for using the workshop, I've agreed to spend forty days a year working as a museum attendant. There's a small museum in the town that has visiting exhibitions, but is only open on certain days in the year. And is that something you're looking forward to? Not really, but it means that I save around four thousand pounds a year because, apart from paying the heating bill, the workshop is rent free."},{"s":176.57,"e":183.2,"t":"But that's the great thing about the place. It's also very close to our new house, so I'll have the luxury of walking to work each morning, which is nice."},{"s":183.83,"e":188.32,"t":"Is it easy to find a building that is suitable as a workshop? No, it isn't."},{"s":188.86,"e":192.57,"t":"It's very easy for the instruments to get damaged so the environment must be dry.","uz":"Cholg'ular juda oson shikastlanadi, shuning uchun muhit quruq bo'lishi kerak."},{"s":193.05,"e":202.69,"t":"None of the buildings I've worked in so far have been dry enough. The new workshop is perfect in that respect. Oh, right. Well, best of luck to you in that new project."},{"s":203.19,"e":207.23,"t":"Now I think you're going to play as a piece on an organ which you built yourself."}]},{"n":13,"ins":1,"title":"Ceramics","dur":322.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Ceramics date back approximately 29,000 years. The first figurines were made in the area of south Europe."},{"k":"p","t":"Early humans could not use their pots to store {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The Chinese improved the quality of ceramics by mixing {2} with the clay."},{"k":"p","t":"Chinese porcelain was also called white {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Potters added quartz and china {4} to clay to make porcelain."},{"k":"h","t":"Glass"},{"k":"p","t":"Glass production is similar to clay ceramics apart from the rate of {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The Romans introduced the use of glass to make {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["water"],"ps":117.4,"en":124.35,"si":18,"ev":"so that although they could carry water in them, it wasn't possible to store it over a long period.","hl":"water","uz":"…shuning uchun ularda suv tashish mumkin bo'lsa-da, uni uzoq vaqt saqlab bo'lmasdi.","why":"\"Carry water … not possible to store it\" — javob: water. Idishlar g'ovak (porous) bo'lgan."},{"a":["minerals"],"ps":138.23,"en":149.53,"si":21,"ev":"In China, at around 200 BC, they discovered that by adding minerals to the clay, they could improve both the appearance and the strength of the ceramics.","hl":"minerals","uz":"Xitoyda miloddan avvalgi 200 yillarda loyga minerallar qo'shib, keramikaning ko'rinishi va mustahkamligini oshirish mumkinligini kashf qilishgan.","why":"\"Adding minerals to the clay\" → \"mixing minerals with the clay\". Javob: minerals."},{"a":["gold"],"ps":184.15,"en":198.3,"si":28,"ev":"In fact, it became so valuable that it was known as white gold.","hl":"gold","uz":"Aslida u shunchalik qimmatli bo'ldiki, uni \"oq oltin\" deb atashgan.","why":"\"Known as white gold\" — javob: gold."},{"a":["stone"],"ps":230.97,"en":238.94,"si":34,"ev":"He discovered that by adding quartz and a material called China Stone to very high quality clay…","hl":"Stone","uz":"U juda sifatli loyga kvars va \"China Stone\" degan materialni qo'shib…","why":"\"Quartz and … China Stone\" — javob: stone. (Transkriptdagi \"courts\" — aslida \"quartz\".)"},{"a":["cooling"],"ps":268.09,"en":284.64,"si":38,"ev":"The main difference between ceramics made from clay and glass is that clay is made up of crystalline plates which become locked together in the cooling process. whereas glass cools too quickly for crystals to form.","hl":"cooling","uz":"Loy keramikasi bilan shishaning asosiy farqi: loy kristall plastinkalardan iborat bo'lib, ular sovish jarayonida bir-biriga mahkamlanadi, shisha esa kristallar hosil bo'lishi uchun juda tez soviydi.","why":"Farq — sovish tezligida: shisha juda tez soviydi. Javob: cooling (bitta so'z)."},{"a":["windows"],"ps":312.18,"en":321.09,"si":42,"ev":"One of the more innovative uses was to use it in windows, as up until then they had just been holes in walls.","hl":"windows","uz":"Eng yangi qo'llanishlardan biri — uni derazalarda ishlatish edi, chunki shu paytgacha ular devordagi teshiklar edi.","why":"\"Use it in windows\" — javob: windows."}],"segs":[{"s":3.26,"e":9.92,"t":"You will hear a lecture about how the production of ceramics, such as plates, pots and glass, first began."},{"s":16.92,"e":17.95,"t":"Hi everyone!"},{"s":18.74,"e":23.01,"t":"Today I'm going to be talking about the origins of ceramics."},{"s":23.8,"e":28.19,"t":"So first of all, let's start off with what is a ceramic?"},{"s":28.89,"e":39.45,"t":"Well, generally speaking, ceramics are what you get when you apply heat to certain inorganic, non-metallic solids and then allow them to cool."},{"s":40.22,"e":49.34,"t":"And examples of ceramics are everyday things like earthenware pots, crockery, glassware and even concrete."},{"s":50.62,"e":52.45,"t":"So how did it all begin?"},{"s":53.5,"e":58.14,"t":"Well, it all started around 29,000 years ago."},{"s":58.58,"e":66.11,"t":"When humans discovered that if you dig up some soft clay from the ground, mold it into a shape"},{"s":66.68,"e":69.79,"t":"and then heat it up to a very high temperature."},{"s":70.42,"e":76.29,"t":"When it cools, the clay has been transformed into something hard and rigid."},{"s":76.95,"e":80.86,"t":"And so what did those first humans do with their discovery?"},{"s":81.72,"e":92.83,"t":"Well, they created figurines, which were small statues and which depicted animals or gods or any shape that the clay could be moulded into."},{"s":93.98,"e":97.66,"t":"All this activity was centred around southern Europe."},{"s":98.1,"e":102.94,"t":"where there is also evidence of ceramics that were created much later."},{"s":104.22,"e":111.61,"t":"The early humans also found a practical use for their discovery, such as storing things like grain."},{"s":112.28,"e":114.3,"t":"although there were drawbacks."},{"s":114.97,"e":116.8,"t":"Pots were porous."},{"s":117.4,"e":124.35,"t":"so that although they could carry water in them, it wasn't possible to store it over a long period.","uz":"…shuning uchun ularda suv tashish mumkin bo'lsa-da, uni uzoq vaqt saqlab bo'lmasdi."},{"s":124.92,"e":129.89,"t":"and also they were quite brittle and shattered very easily if they were dropped."},{"s":131.29,"e":137.5,"t":"Despite these problems, it was many thousands of years before there were any improvements."},{"s":138.23,"e":149.53,"t":"In China, at around 200 BC, they discovered that by adding minerals to the clay, they could improve both the appearance and the strength of the ceramics.","uz":"Xitoyda miloddan avvalgi 200 yillarda loyga minerallar qo'shib, keramikaning ko'rinishi va mustahkamligini oshirish mumkinligini kashf qilishgan."},{"s":150.42,"e":159.45,"t":"But it took nearly a thousand years before they perfected the process to produce high quality ceramics known as porcelain."},{"s":160.5,"e":164.64,"t":"And once they had perfected the process, they kept it a secret."},{"s":165.21,"e":167.36,"t":"another thousand years."},{"s":168.38,"e":173.44,"t":"Compared to the first ceramics, porcelain was lighter, finer."},{"s":174.01,"e":175.68,"t":"harder and whiter."},{"s":176.22,"e":183.2,"t":"and became an important commodity in China's trading with the rest of the world for hundreds of years."},{"s":184.15,"e":198.3,"t":"In fact, it became so valuable that it was known as white gold, and spies were sent to China to discover what they did to the clay to produce such high-quality merchandise."},{"s":200.06,"e":205.12,"t":"It wasn't until the 18th century that the secret began to unravel."},{"s":206.14,"e":215.1,"t":"A German alchemist called Johann Friedrich Botka was asked by the king to make gold out of lead."},{"s":215.99,"e":220.8,"t":"Unfortunately, Bodger failed to achieve this and soon gave up."},{"s":221.66,"e":226.59,"t":"But in order to please the king, he attempted to make high quality porcelain."},{"s":227.48,"e":230.37,"t":"and after many years of experimentation"},{"s":230.97,"e":238.94,"t":"He discovered that by adding quartz and a material called China Stone to very high quality clay…","uz":"U juda sifatli loyga kvars va \"China Stone\" degan materialni qo'shib…"},{"s":239.54,"e":246.97,"t":"He managed to get the same results that the Chinese had been achieving for the last 1,000 years."},{"s":252.02,"e":261.15,"t":"We'll now look at another ceramic which is made from mixing sand with minerals and heating to over 600 degrees Celsius."},{"s":262.17,"e":267.17,"t":"When this mixture cools, the result is of course glass."},{"s":268.09,"e":284.64,"t":"The main difference between ceramics made from clay and glass is that clay is made up of crystalline plates which become locked together in the cooling process. whereas glass cools too quickly for crystals to form.","uz":"Loy keramikasi bilan shishaning asosiy farqi: loy kristall plastinkalardan iborat bo'lib, ular sovish jarayonida bir-biriga mahkamlanadi, shisha esa kristallar hosil bo'lishi uchun juda tez soviydi."},{"s":285.62,"e":293.37,"t":"Apart from that, the process of heating up naturally occurring materials to transform them is the same."},{"s":294.74,"e":299.52,"t":"The origins of glass date back to 3500 BC."},{"s":300.18,"e":311.23,"t":"But it wasn't until the Roman Empire, two thousand years ago, that the art of glassblowing and the practical uses of glass became more widespread."},{"s":312.18,"e":321.09,"t":"One of the more innovative uses was to use it in windows, as up until then they had just been holes in walls.","uz":"Eng yangi qo'llanishlardan biri — uni derazalarda ishlatish edi, chunki shu paytgacha ular devordagi teshiklar edi."}]},{"n":14,"ins":1,"title":"The Spirit Bear","dur":179.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"It is a white bear belonging to the black bear family. Its colour comes from an uncommon {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Local people believe that it has unusual {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"They protect the bear from {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Tree roots stop {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"It is currently found on a small number of {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Habitat is being lost due to deforestation and construction of {6} by logging companies."}],"items":[{"a":["gene"],"ps":28.41,"en":32.86,"si":3,"ev":"which is the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few.","hl":"gene","uz":"…bu ba'zilarda namoyon bo'ladigan maxsus gen natijasidir.","why":"\"A special gene\" → \"an uncommon gene\". Javob: gene."},{"a":["power","powers"],"ps":41.11,"en":44.48,"si":6,"ev":"Its snowy fur brings with it a special power.","hl":"power","uz":"Uning qordek oq mo'ynasi o'zi bilan maxsus kuch olib keladi.","why":"\"A special power\" → \"unusual power(s)\". Javob: power/powers."},{"a":["strangers"],"ps":55.45,"en":59.52,"si":10,"ev":"It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.","hl":"strangers","uz":"Bu begonalar hududga kelganda uni himoya qilish usulidir.","why":"\"Protecting it when strangers visit\" — javob: strangers."},{"a":["erosion"],"ps":78.23,"en":88.22,"si":15,"ev":"For example, the old growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams.","hl":"erosion","uz":"Masalan, keksa daraxtlarning juda uzun ildizlari baliqli soylar bo'yidagi tuproq eroziyasining oldini oladi.","why":"\"Help prevent erosion\" → \"stop erosion\". Javob: erosion."},{"a":["islands"],"ps":124.82,"en":131.81,"si":24,"ev":"Today, the Spirit Bear lives off the coast of the province of British Columbia on a few islands.","hl":"islands","uz":"Bugun Ruh ayig'i Britaniya Kolumbiyasi provinsiyasi qirg'oqlaridagi bir nechta orolda yashaydi.","why":"\"On a few islands\" → \"a small number of islands\". Javob: islands."},{"a":["roads"],"ps":169.14,"en":178.33,"si":33,"ev":"They have built roads which have fractured the areas where the bear usually feeds, and many hibernation sites have also been lost.","hl":"roads","uz":"Ular ayiq odatda oziqlanadigan hududlarni bo'lib tashlagan yo'llar qurishgan, ko'plab qishki uyqu joylari ham yo'qolgan.","why":"Daraxt kesuvchi kompaniyalar \"built roads\" — javob: roads."}],"segs":[{"s":1.85,"e":10.33,"t":"You will hear a university lecture about an endangered bear in British Columbia, Canada, known as the Spirit Bear."},{"s":12.63,"e":22.78,"t":"Today we continue our series on ecology and conservation with a look at a particularly endangered member of the Black Bear family."},{"s":23.48,"e":27.9,"t":"One in ten black bears is actually born with a white coat."},{"s":28.41,"e":32.86,"t":"which is the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few.","uz":"…bu ba'zilarda namoyon bo'ladigan maxsus gen natijasidir."},{"s":33.88,"e":36.93,"t":"Local people have named it the Spirit Bear."},{"s":37.46,"e":40.64,"t":"and according to the legends of these communities."},{"s":41.11,"e":44.48,"t":"Its snowy fur brings with it a special power.","uz":"Uning qordek oq mo'ynasi o'zi bilan maxsus kuch olib keladi."},{"s":45.37,"e":49.95,"t":"Because of this, it has always been highly regarded by them."},{"s":50.55,"e":53.44,"t":"so much that they do not speak of seeing it."},{"s":53.94,"e":54.91,"t":"anyone else."},{"s":55.45,"e":59.52,"t":"It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.","uz":"Bu begonalar hududga kelganda uni himoya qilish usulidir."},{"s":60.79,"e":63.42,"t":"The white bear's habitat is quite interesting."},{"s":64.28,"e":68.22,"t":"the bear's strong relationship with the old-growth rainforest."},{"s":68.89,"e":69.89,"t":"complex one."},{"s":71.29,"e":77.34,"t":"bear relies on the huge centuries-old trees in the forest in many ways."},{"s":78.23,"e":88.22,"t":"For example, the old growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams.","uz":"Masalan, keksa daraxtlarning juda uzun ildizlari baliqli soylar bo'yidagi tuproq eroziyasining oldini oladi."},{"s":89.05,"e":90.62,"t":"keeping these banks intact"},{"s":91.13,"e":94.4,"t":"is important because these streams are home to salmon."},{"s":94.84,"e":96.89,"t":"which are the bear's main food source."},{"s":98.39,"e":102.59,"t":"In return, the bear's feeding habits nurture the forest."},{"s":103.22,"e":105.05,"t":"as the bears eat the salmon."},{"s":105.75,"e":110.37,"t":"Discard the skin and bones in great amounts on the forest floor."},{"s":110.81,"e":112.73,"t":"which provide vital nutrients."},{"s":113.59,"e":123.29,"t":"These produce lush vegetation that sustains thousands of other types of life forms, from birds to insects and more."},{"s":124.82,"e":131.81,"t":"Today, the Spirit Bear lives off the coast of the province of British Columbia on a few islands.","uz":"Bugun Ruh ayig'i Britaniya Kolumbiyasi provinsiyasi qirg'oqlaridagi bir nechta orolda yashaydi."},{"s":132.5,"e":140.67,"t":"there is great concern for their survival, since it is estimated that less than two hundred of these white bears remain."},{"s":141.66,"e":143.01,"t":"best way to protect them."},{"s":143.48,"e":148.77,"t":"is to make every effort to preserve the delicate balance of their forest environment."},{"s":149.59,"e":150.46,"t":"In other words,"},{"s":151.03,"e":152.29,"t":"their ecosystem."},{"s":154.68,"e":159.23,"t":"The greatest threat to the bear's existence is the loss of its habitat."},{"s":160.28,"e":167.17,"t":"Over many years, logging companies have stripped the land by cutting down a large number of trees."},{"s":168.06,"e":168.57,"t":"edition."},{"s":169.14,"e":178.33,"t":"They have built roads which have fractured the areas where the bear usually feeds, and many hibernation sites have also been lost.","uz":"Ular ayiq odatda oziqlanadigan hududlarni bo'lib tashlagan yo'llar qurishgan, ko'plab qishki uyqu joylari ham yo'qolgan."}]},{"n":15,"ins":1,"title":"Concerts in university arts festival","dur":180.8,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Concert 1"},{"k":"p","t":"Australian composer: Liza Lim."},{"k":"p","t":"Studied piano and {1} before turning to composition."},{"k":"p","t":"Performers and festivals around the world have given a lot of {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Compositions show a great deal of {3} and are drawn from various cultural sources."},{"k":"p","t":"Her music is very expressive and also {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Festival will include her {5} called The Oresteia."},{"k":"p","t":"Lim described the sounds in The Oresteia as {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["violin"],"ps":62.3,"en":70.08,"si":10,"ev":"As a child, Lim originally learned to play the piano, like so many children, and also the violin.","hl":"violin","uz":"Bolaligida Lim ko'p bolalar kabi avval pianino, shuningdek skripka chalishni o'rgangan.","why":"Pianino va skripka — javob: violin."},{"a":["commissions"],"ps":86.74,"en":91.71,"si":14,"ev":"As a composer, she has received commissions from numerous orchestras","hl":"commissions","uz":"Bastakor sifatida u ko'plab orkestrlardan buyurtmalar olgan…","why":"\"Received commissions from numerous orchestras, other performers and festivals\" — javob: commissions."},{"a":["energy"],"ps":97.14,"en":101.57,"si":16,"ev":"Eliza Lim's compositions are vibrant and full of energy.","hl":"energy","uz":"Eliza Limning asarlari yorqin va energiyaga to'la.","why":"\"Full of energy\" → \"a great deal of energy\". Javob: energy."},{"a":["complex"],"ps":115.77,"en":125.53,"si":20,"ev":"Her music is very expressive. So, although it is complex, it has the power of connecting with audiences and performers alike.","hl":"complex","uz":"Uning musiqasi juda ta'sirchan. Murakkab bo'lsa ham, tinglovchi va ijrochilarni birdek bog'lay oladi.","why":"\"Expressive … although it is complex\" — javob: complex."},{"a":["opera"],"ps":133.14,"en":136.25,"si":22,"ev":"This is an opera in seven parts.","hl":"opera","uz":"Bu yetti qismdan iborat opera.","why":"\"An opera in seven parts\" — javob: opera."},{"a":["disturbing"],"ps":171.29,"en":174.78,"si":29,"ev":"The sounds she creates are also disturbing.","hl":"disturbing","uz":"Uning yaratgan tovushlari ham bezovta qiluvchi.","why":"\"The sounds she creates are also disturbing\" — javob: disturbing."}],"segs":[{"s":1.94,"e":5.41,"t":"You will hear a British University lecturer in music"},{"s":5.98,"e":8.77,"t":"talking about concerts in an arts festival."},{"s":15.61,"e":21.02,"t":"As you all know, the University is planning an arts festival for later this year."},{"s":21.5,"e":25.73,"t":"And here in the music department, we've planned three concerts."},{"s":26.33,"e":31.42,"t":"These will be public performances and the program has just been finalised."},{"s":32.22,"e":37.02,"t":"The theme of the festival is links between the UK and Australia."},{"s":37.62,"e":39.52,"t":"and this is reflected in the music."},{"s":40.22,"e":44.57,"t":"Each concert will feature both British and Australian composers."},{"s":45.5,"e":51.26,"t":"I'll tell you briefly about the Australian music, as you probably won't be familiar with that."},{"s":52.63,"e":61.44,"t":"The first concert will include music by Liza Lim, who was born in Perth, Western Australia in 1966."},{"s":62.3,"e":70.08,"t":"As a child, Lim originally learned to play the piano, like so many children, and also the violin.","uz":"Bolaligida Lim ko'p bolalar kabi avval pianino, shuningdek skripka chalishni o'rgangan."},{"s":71.0,"e":75.58,"t":"When she was 11, her teachers encouraged her to start composing."},{"s":76.38,"e":82.17,"t":"She found this was her real strength and she studied and later taught composition."},{"s":82.62,"e":85.66,"t":"both in Australia and in other countries."},{"s":86.74,"e":91.71,"t":"As a composer, she has received commissions from numerous orchestras","uz":"Bastakor sifatida u ko'plab orkestrlardan buyurtmalar olgan…"},{"s":92.15,"e":96.13,"t":"other performers and festivals in several countries."},{"s":97.14,"e":101.57,"t":"Eliza Lim's compositions are vibrant and full of energy.","uz":"Eliza Limning asarlari yorqin va energiyaga to'la."},{"s":102.26,"e":107.45,"t":"and she often explores Asian and Australian Aboriginal cultural sources."},{"s":107.99,"e":111.23,"t":"including the native instrument, the digeridoo."},{"s":111.96,"e":114.97,"t":"This is featured in the work called The Compass."},{"s":115.77,"e":125.53,"t":"Her music is very expressive. So, although it is complex, it has the power of connecting with audiences and performers alike.","uz":"Uning musiqasi juda ta'sirchan. Murakkab bo'lsa ham, tinglovchi va ijrochilarni birdek bog'lay oladi."},{"s":127.13,"e":132.38,"t":"In the festival, we're going to give a semi-staged performance of the Oresteia."},{"s":133.14,"e":136.25,"t":"This is an opera in seven parts.","uz":"Bu yetti qismdan iborat opera."},{"s":136.86,"e":141.41,"t":"based on the trilogy of ancient Greek tragedies by Iskalles."},{"s":142.52,"e":146.11,"t":"Slim composed this when she was in her mid-twenties."},{"s":146.65,"e":150.37,"t":"and she also wrote the text along with Barry Koski."},{"s":151.42,"e":161.47,"t":"It's performed by six singers, a dancer, and an orchestra that, as well as standard orchestral instruments, includes electric guitar,"},{"s":161.91,"e":164.73,"t":"and a traditional Turkish stringed instrument."},{"s":165.72,"e":170.49,"t":"Lim wrote that because the stories in the tragedies are not easy to tell."},{"s":171.29,"e":174.78,"t":"The sounds she creates are also disturbing.","uz":"Uning yaratgan tovushlari ham bezovta qiluvchi."},{"s":175.35,"e":180.74,"t":"and they include breathing, sobbing, laughing and whistling."}]},{"n":16,"ins":2,"title":"A trip to the rainforest","dur":370.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Richard and Matthew abandoned their boat because they couldn't get past a waterfall."},{"k":"p","t":"They decided to walk through the jungle as far as the {1} marked on the map."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard says that during the walk, they were always both hot and wet."},{"k":"p","t":"The first sign of human activity that they found was a {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"In a deserted camp, they found some soup made from unusual {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard says that by the time they had reached the camp, they were lacking in {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Richard says that after the meal, they began to feel {5} about what they'd done."},{"k":"p","t":"Before leaving the camp, they left the sum of {6} to thank their host."}],"items":[{"a":["road"],"ps":41.5,"en":54.05,"si":4,"ev":"We decided to abandon it and walk to the nearest road. … On our map, it looked like a 100km walk.","hl":"road","uz":"Qayiqni tashlab, eng yaqin yo'lgacha piyoda borishga qaror qildik. … Xaritada bu 100 km yo'ldek ko'rinardi.","why":"\"Walk to the nearest road\" — xaritada belgilangan joy — road. Sharshara (waterfall) — qayiq to'xtagan joy, tuzoq."},{"a":["path"],"ps":73.94,"en":82.69,"si":8,"ev":"Then, on the seventh day, we suddenly came across a path. Not an animal trail, but a man-made one. So we knew there must be people living there.","hl":"path","uz":"Keyin, yettinchi kuni, to'satdan so'qmoqqa duch keldik. Hayvon izi emas, odam qilgan so'qmoq edi.","why":"Odamlar faoliyatining birinchi belgisi — \"a path… a man-made one\". Javob: path."},{"a":["meat & vegetables","meat and vegetables"],"ps":113.94,"en":123.29,"si":14,"ev":"because there was a large pot full of thick soup. We couldn't identify either the strange-looking pieces of meat or the unfamiliar vegetables it seemed to be made from.","hl":"meat","uz":"…chunki u yerda quyuq sho'rva to'la katta qozon bor edi. Uning g'alati ko'rinishdagi go'sht bo'laklari va notanish sabzavotlardan qilinganini aniqlay olmadik.","why":"Sho'rva \"strange-looking pieces of meat\" va \"unfamiliar vegetables\" dan qilingan. Javob: meat and vegetables (ikki so'z + \"and\")."},{"a":["energy"],"ps":126.23,"en":134.62,"si":16,"ev":"We had plenty left, we were low on energy. This was our greatest problem.","hl":"energy","uz":"Un va guruch hali ko'p edi, lekin kuchimiz kam qolgandi. Eng katta muammo shu edi.","why":"\"Low on energy\" → \"lacking in energy\". Javob: energy. Ovqat (flour, rice) yetarli edi — tuzoq."},{"a":["worried"],"ps":150.1,"en":156.64,"si":22,"ev":"Afterwards we began to get worried.","hl":"worried","uz":"Keyin xavotirlana boshladik.","why":"\"Began to get worried\" — javob: worried. Uy egasi istalgan daqiqa qaytishi mumkin edi."},{"a":["30 dollars","thirty dollars","30"],"ps":160.73,"en":164.61,"si":24,"ev":"To show we were grateful, we placed $30 in the cleaned-out cooking pot.","hl":"30","uz":"Minnatdorligimizni bildirish uchun tozalangan qozonga 30 dollar qo'ydik.","why":"Qoldirilgan pul — $30. \"$10\" — ovqatning taxminiy narxi, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":2.23,"e":8.54,"t":"You'll hear an explorer called Richard Livingston talking about a trip he made in the rainforest of South America."},{"s":15.06,"e":21.76,"t":"I'd set off with my friend Matthew Price to sail down a little-known river in the rainforest in a home-made boat."},{"s":22.42,"e":33.95,"t":"Our original idea was to go all the way by boat, carrying it past any rough bits, but the river was much rockier and faster flowing than we thought, which meant we were only covering a few kilometers each day."},{"s":34.97,"e":40.64,"t":"Suddenly, we realised that as the river was about to go over a waterfall, we could go no further by boat."},{"s":41.5,"e":54.05,"t":"We decided to abandon it and walk to the nearest road. … On our map, it looked like a 100km walk.","uz":"Qayiqni tashlab, eng yaqin yo'lgacha piyoda borishga qaror qildik. … Xaritada bu 100 km yo'ldek ko'rinardi."},{"s":55.13,"e":60.73,"t":"And that walk through thick rainforest with 25 kilos on our backs was difficult."},{"s":61.59,"e":68.57,"t":"We walked for six days. It was hot and we were permanently wet through, before we came to any sign of civilization."},{"s":69.37,"e":72.93,"t":"There were times when we really wondered if we'd ever get out of that jungle alive."},{"s":73.94,"e":82.69,"t":"Then, on the seventh day, we suddenly came across a path. Not an animal trail, but a man-made one. So we knew there must be people living there.","uz":"Keyin, yettinchi kuni, to'satdan so'qmoqqa duch keldik. Hayvon izi emas, odam qilgan so'qmoq edi."},{"s":83.22,"e":89.79,"t":"It was going roughly in the right direction, so we followed it, and at dusk we came to a deserted camp in a hollow."},{"s":90.3,"e":92.41,"t":"Deserted but not uninhabited."},{"s":93.14,"e":97.92,"t":"There was digging equipment wrapped in plastic alongside two water-filled holes."},{"s":98.68,"e":102.72,"t":"Obviously someone had been digging in search of gold at some time or another."},{"s":104.7,"e":113.44,"t":"Nearby, on a rough wooden table, were some cooking utensils and a few other supplies, and whoever was camping there must have been intending to return soon."},{"s":113.94,"e":123.29,"t":"because there was a large pot full of thick soup. We couldn't identify either the strange-looking pieces of meat or the unfamiliar vegetables it seemed to be made from.","uz":"…chunki u yerda quyuq sho'rva to'la katta qozon bor edi. Uning g'alati ko'rinishdagi go'sht bo'laklari va notanish sabzavotlardan qilinganini aniqlay olmadik."},{"s":123.74,"e":125.53,"t":"but we were in a desperate state."},{"s":126.23,"e":134.62,"t":"Over the previous seven days, we'd only had flour and rice to eat, and although we had plenty left, we were low on energy. This was our greatest problem."},{"s":135.74,"e":141.02,"t":"So, we cooked up some of our rice and decided to have two spoonfuls from the pot with it."},{"s":141.75,"e":142.49,"t":"It was good."},{"s":143.22,"e":144.41,"t":"So we had another spoonful."},{"s":145.34,"e":146.56,"t":"and then another."},{"s":147.13,"e":149.34,"t":"Soon, nothing was left of our host's meal."},{"s":150.1,"e":156.64,"t":"afterwards we began to get worried. People living this sort of life could be very tough, and this one could return any minute."},{"s":157.34,"e":159.36,"t":"we decided to make an early start."},{"s":160.73,"e":164.61,"t":"To show we were grateful, we placed $30 in the cleaned-out cooking pot.","uz":"Minnatdorligimizni bildirish uchun tozalangan qozonga 30 dollar qo'ydik."},{"s":165.05,"e":171.36,"t":"It was quite a lot for the quantity of food. It was probably only worth $10 or so. But that wasn't the point."},{"s":171.86,"e":175.74,"t":"This man wouldn't be able to pop to the supermarket to replace the food we'd eaten."},{"s":176.73,"e":183.01,"t":"I have no regrets, because that dinner gave us the strength to make it the rest of the way through the jungle safely."}]},{"n":17,"ins":2,"title":"Museum tour","dur":358.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"This museum houses objects collected by the cultural society based in the city."},{"k":"p","t":"It has one of the country's best galleries containing {1} science exhibits."},{"k":"p","t":"The museum's displays of butterflies and birds are closed to visitors at present."},{"k":"p","t":"The section called Let's {2} is popular with young people."},{"k":"p","t":"The picture galleries contain works on various themes by German {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"The museum's {4} needs modernising."},{"k":"p","t":"The guide uses the word {5} to describe the Rutland Dinosaur's effect on people."},{"k":"p","t":"Polystyrene was used to reconstruct most of the Rutland Dinosaur's {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["natural"],"ps":36.22,"en":43.39,"si":5,"ev":"It also has one of Britain's top five exhibitions of natural science.","hl":"natural","uz":"Shuningdek, unda Britaniyaning eng yaxshi beshta tabiiy fanlar ko'rgazmasidan biri bor.","why":"\"Top five exhibitions of natural science\" → \"best galleries containing natural science exhibits\". Javob: natural."},{"a":["interact"],"ps":56.02,"en":69.34,"si":8,"ev":"Upstairs, there's a section designed especially for children… It's called Let's Interact.","hl":"Interact","uz":"Yuqori qavatda maxsus bolalar uchun bo'lim bor… U \"Let's Interact\" deb ataladi.","why":"Bo'lim nomi — Let's Interact. Javob: interact."},{"a":["artists"],"ps":85.37,"en":97.34,"si":12,"ev":"The picture galleries… boast a fine collection of drawings, prints and woodcuts by German artists, and the art collection is arranged thematically.","hl":"artists","uz":"Rasm galereyalarida nemis rassomlarining chizmalari, bosma va yog'och o'ymakorligi asarlari to'plami bor, kolleksiya mavzular bo'yicha joylashtirilgan.","why":"\"By German artists\" — javob: artists. \"Thematically\" — topshiriqdagi \"on various themes\"."},{"a":["heating"],"ps":104.54,"en":119.87,"si":14,"ev":"I'm sorry to say the central heating needs a million pound refit, which the city can't afford.","hl":"heating","uz":"Afsuski, markaziy isitish tizimi million funtlik ta'mirga muhtoj, shahar esa buni ko'tara olmaydi.","why":"\"Central heating needs a … refit\" → \"heating needs modernising\". Javob: heating."},{"a":["intimidating"],"ps":133.3,"en":143.2,"si":16,"ev":"As you can see, it's three and a half meters high and 14 meters long. Quite an intimidating sight.","hl":"intimidating","uz":"Ko'rib turganingizdek, balandligi 3,5 metr, uzunligi 14 metr. Ancha qo'rqinchli manzara.","why":"\"Quite an intimidating sight\" — javob: intimidating."},{"a":["tail"],"ps":158.62,"en":164.89,"si":19,"ev":"Most of the neck, some of the spine and a bit of the tail were found in Rutland. The rest of the tail is polystyrene.","hl":"tail","uz":"Bo'ynining ko'p qismi, umurtqasining bir qismi va dumining ozgina qismi Rutlenddan topilgan. Dumining qolgani — polistirol.","why":"Polistiroldan qilingan qism — dumning ko'p qismi. Javob: tail. Bo'yin (neck) — asl suyaklardan, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":2.49,"e":5.66,"t":"You'll hear a guide taking a group of visitors around a museum."},{"s":16.7,"e":19.36,"t":"Welcome to the City Museum and Art Gallery."},{"s":19.8,"e":24.83,"t":"Before we start our tour, I'd like to give you a bit of background information about the place itself."},{"s":25.4,"e":32.51,"t":"The museum was founded in 1849 as a home for the collections built up over the years by the local cultural society."},{"s":33.05,"e":35.77,"t":"and is one of seven museums owned by the city council."},{"s":36.22,"e":43.39,"t":"Its collections of dinosaurs and mummies are well known, and it also has one of Britain's top five exhibitions of natural science."},{"s":43.9,"e":47.58,"t":"Unfortunately, not all areas are open to the public at the moment."},{"s":48.02,"e":55.29,"t":"In the Cellastaurans, for example, there are, amongst other things, display cases full of butterflies and many others full of birds."},{"s":56.02,"e":69.34,"t":"Upstairs, there's a section designed especially for children, for those of you who are interested, where young people can dress up, draw pictures, and find out about the museum at their own pace. It's called Let's Interact."},{"s":69.91,"e":72.67,"t":"And there's more noise there than silence, as you might imagine."},{"s":73.4,"e":77.02,"t":"We find this to be a successful way of attracting children to museums."},{"s":77.46,"e":84.25,"t":"Let's face it, museums in the past have been boring, rather stuffy places for children and indeed adults to visit."},{"s":85.37,"e":97.34,"t":"The picture galleries, which we'll be visiting later, boast a fine collection of drawings, prints and woodcuts by German artists, and the art collection is arranged thematically rather than chronologically."},{"s":98.14,"e":103.9,"t":"The themes we shall see are color, light, movement, signs and symbols."},{"s":104.54,"e":119.87,"t":"It's a bit cold here, I'm afraid. I do apologize for this, but I'm sorry to say the central heating needs a million pound refit, which the city can't afford to undertake at the moment. So, if any of you are millionaires and feeling generous today, please see me after the tour."},{"s":120.89,"e":129.69,"t":"Now, if you will just follow me to the end of the Grand Colonnade, we'll turn right into the first exhibit room on the ground floor."},{"s":133.3,"e":143.2,"t":"This room houses the Rutland Dinosaur. As you can see, it's three and a half meters high and 14 meters long. Quite an intimidating sight. This..."},{"s":143.67,"e":154.4,"t":"The Citiosaurus, as it's called, was found in England's smallest county in 1968. The creature loped across the countryside 175 million years ago."},{"s":155.0,"e":158.08,"t":"and is the most complete example of the breed discovered to date."},{"s":158.62,"e":164.89,"t":"Most of the neck, some of the spine and a bit of the tail were found in Rutland. The rest of the tail is polystyrene.","uz":"Bo'ynining ko'p qismi, umurtqasining bir qismi va dumining ozgina qismi Rutlenddan topilgan. Dumining qolgani — polistirol."},{"s":165.5,"e":176.45,"t":"For those of you who prefer your dinosaurs on a much more human scale, there is a much smaller 200 million year old pellosaur over there. Now, if you'd like to follow me up the stairs..."}]},{"n":18,"ins":2,"title":"Roman tablets","dur":365.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The speaker says that an Ancient Roman 'tablet' was about as thick as a present-day envelope."},{"k":"p","t":"At the site of an old {1}, archaeologists discovered about 200 tablets."},{"k":"p","t":"Roman soldiers often used tablets writing letters or documents of a {2} nature."},{"k":"p","t":"On one tablet mentioned, the word transportation is legible as well as people's names."},{"k":"p","t":"An expert in what's called computer {3} says that the project is very challenging."},{"k":"p","t":"Panels on the tablets were once filled with {4}, which provided the writing surface."},{"k":"p","t":"Efforts to analyse the original texts using {5} photography were unsuccessful."},{"k":"p","t":"New technology is also being applied to other historical texts which were written using {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["fort"],"ps":43.13,"en":46.11,"si":4,"ev":"Nearly 200 were found in one Roman fort alone.","hl":"fort","uz":"Faqat bitta Rim qal'asining o'zida 200 ga yaqini topilgan.","why":"\"In one Roman fort\" — javob: fort."},{"a":["legal"],"ps":74.39,"en":79.42,"si":11,"ev":"Many of the tablets took the form of legal documents and letters written by Roman soldiers.","hl":"legal","uz":"Ko'plab taxtachalar Rim askarlari yozgan huquqiy hujjatlar va xatlar shaklida bo'lgan.","why":"\"Legal documents and letters\" → \"letters or documents of a legal nature\". Javob: legal."},{"a":["vision"],"ps":100.6,"en":109.15,"si":17,"ev":"Professor Mike Brady, a leading figure in what's known as computer vision for many years, admits that this is the hardest project he's ever worked on.","hl":"vision","uz":"Ko'p yillardan beri \"kompyuter ko'rishi\" sohasining yetakchilaridan biri professor Mayk Breydi bu u ishlagan eng qiyin loyiha ekanini tan oladi.","why":"\"What's known as computer vision\" — javob: vision."},{"a":["wax"],"ps":131.74,"en":138.69,"si":22,"ev":"The wax was poured into these and the text was then written into this soft surface using an instrument with a fine metal point.","hl":"wax","uz":"Bu (bo'shliq)larga mum quyilgan va matn shu yumshoq yuzaga ingichka metall uchli asbob bilan yozilgan.","why":"\"The wax was poured into these\" — javob: wax."},{"a":["laser"],"ps":151.67,"en":157.34,"si":25,"ev":"For some time, scientists have attempted to study them with laser photography, but this has proved fruitless.","hl":"laser","uz":"Bir muncha vaqtdan beri olimlar ularni lazer fotografiyasi bilan o'rganishga urindi, lekin bu natija bermadi.","why":"\"Laser photography … proved fruitless\" → \"unsuccessful\". Javob: laser."},{"a":["ink"],"ps":176.79,"en":180.45,"si":29,"ev":"The new technology has already been used on texts in ink as well.","hl":"ink","uz":"Yangi texnologiya siyoh bilan yozilgan matnlarda ham qo'llanib bo'lingan.","why":"\"Texts in ink\" — javob: ink."}],"segs":[{"s":2.3,"e":14.01,"t":"You'll hear a short radio report about how technology is helping archaeologists who want to learn more about some texts written over 2,000 years ago known as Roman tablets."},{"s":22.87,"e":31.39,"t":"At the time of the Roman Empire in Europe around 2,000 years ago, it was common for information to be written not on paper, but on things called tablets."},{"s":32.12,"e":36.25,"t":"These were pieces of wood about the size and thickness of a typical modern envelope."},{"s":37.27,"e":42.43,"t":"Hundreds of such tablets have been unearthed from archaeological sites throughout Europe and the Mediterranean world."},{"s":43.13,"e":46.11,"t":"Nearly 200 were found in one Roman fort alone.","uz":"Faqat bitta Rim qal'asining o'zida 200 ga yaqini topilgan."},{"s":46.87,"e":48.54,"t":"and like most of these discoveries"},{"s":48.98,"e":53.12,"t":"They have been placed in public collections, mainly in museums in northern Europe."},{"s":53.66,"e":56.61,"t":"to be viewed, but not unfortunately to be read."},{"s":57.69,"e":61.95,"t":"This is because, although in some cases traces of writing can still be seen,"},{"s":62.42,"e":64.7,"t":"Most are now illegible to the naked eye."},{"s":65.53,"e":73.18,"t":"But that's all soon to change, because archaeologists hope that with the help of new technology, their secrets may soon be revealed."},{"s":74.39,"e":79.42,"t":"Many of the tablets took the form of legal documents and letters written by Roman soldiers.","uz":"Ko'plab taxtachalar Rim askarlari yozgan huquqiy hujjatlar va xatlar shaklida bo'lgan."},{"s":80.22,"e":86.69,"t":"An example, now at the British Museum, bears the name of the person who wrote it and the name of the person who received it."},{"s":87.13,"e":88.83,"t":"plus the word \"transportation\"."},{"s":89.3,"e":90.65,"t":"which you can just make out"},{"s":91.45,"e":93.05,"t":"The rest remains a mystery."},{"s":93.94,"e":99.58,"t":"Now, with the help of computer techniques, experts hope eventually to be able to read the whole letter."},{"s":100.6,"e":109.15,"t":"Professor Mike Brady, a leading figure in what's known as computer vision for many years, admits that this is the hardest project he's ever worked on.","uz":"Ko'p yillardan beri \"kompyuter ko'rishi\" sohasining yetakchilaridan biri professor Mayk Breydi bu u ishlagan eng qiyin loyiha ekanini tan oladi."},{"s":110.04,"e":117.73,"t":"But the excitement of seeing the latest ideas in computing applied to such a very ancient problem has the archaeological community buzzing."},{"s":119.0,"e":122.69,"t":"So, in simple terms, why has the writing been preserved?"},{"s":123.45,"e":126.14,"t":"How will it be possible to undo the aging process?"},{"s":126.94,"e":130.88,"t":"Well, the tablets were made with thin hollow panels cut across them."},{"s":131.74,"e":138.69,"t":"The wax was poured into these and the text was then written into this soft surface using an instrument with a fine metal point.","uz":"Bu (bo'shliq)larga mum quyilgan va matn shu yumshoq yuzaga ingichka metall uchli asbob bilan yozilgan."},{"s":139.45,"e":146.56,"t":"In virtually all cases, the wax has perished and all that can be detected on the surface of the tablet underneath are scratches."},{"s":147.51,"e":150.3,"t":"These are too faint to be read because they are distorted."},{"s":151.67,"e":157.34,"t":"For some time, scientists have attempted to study them with laser photography, but this has proved fruitless.","uz":"Bir muncha vaqtdan beri olimlar ularni lazer fotografiyasi bilan o'rganishga urindi, lekin bu natija bermadi."},{"s":158.49,"e":165.6,"t":"However, it is now hoped that by enhancing images of the tablets on computer, their original messages will become legible again."},{"s":166.55,"e":171.07,"t":"If this is the case, a whole new source of historical information will be opened up."},{"s":171.64,"e":175.58,"t":"and this promises advances and new knowledge for many decades to come."},{"s":176.79,"e":180.45,"t":"The new technology has already been used on texts in ink as well.","uz":"Yangi texnologiya siyoh bilan yozilgan matnlarda ham qo'llanib bo'lingan."},{"s":180.89,"e":184.96,"t":"and in the future, it will be applied to damaged surfaces of many kinds."}]},{"n":19,"ins":2,"title":"Cherries","dur":310.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The speaker gives the examples of apples as a crop being replaced by cherries."},{"k":"p","t":"To protect young trees from extremes of weather, a {1} may be used."},{"k":"p","t":"Cherries are prone to cracking because there is hardly any {2} on the skin of the fruit."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker compares the cherry to a {3} when explaining the effect of rain on the fruit."},{"k":"p","t":"Shoppers are advised to purchase cherries which have a {4} stem and look fresh and tasty."},{"k":"p","t":"The traditional view was that cherries need up to 4 years before they produce a useful crop."},{"k":"p","t":"The most popular new variety of cherry tree among farmers has the name {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"While picking cherries, keep a cherry {6} in your mouth to stop you eating too many."}],"items":[{"a":["tunnel"],"ps":62.36,"en":66.75,"si":5,"ev":"Quite a few of the smaller trees are covered up against the rain and wind in a plastic tunnel.","hl":"tunnel","uz":"Ancha kichik daraxtlar yomg'ir va shamoldan plastik tunnel bilan yopib qo'yiladi.","why":"\"In a plastic tunnel\" — javob: tunnel."},{"a":["wax"],"ps":78.23,"en":92.13,"si":7,"ev":"The surface of the fruit has very little wax on it… the skin is liable to crack when water gets into it.","hl":"wax","uz":"Mevaning yuzasida mum juda kam… suv kirsa, po'sti yorilib ketishi mumkin.","why":"\"Very little wax\" → \"hardly any wax\". Javob: wax."},{"a":["balloon"],"ps":78.23,"en":92.13,"si":7,"ev":"The fruit bursts with a pop, rather like a balloon.","hl":"balloon","uz":"Meva xuddi havo shari kabi \"pop\" etib yorilib ketadi.","why":"\"Rather like a balloon\" — javob: balloon."},{"a":["green"],"ps":92.95,"en":102.08,"si":8,"ev":"Buy the ones with a green stem. You'll find they taste much better.","hl":"green","uz":"Bandi yashil bo'lganlarini oling — ancha mazaliroq bo'ladi.","why":"\"With a green stem\" — javob: green."},{"a":["sweetheart"],"ps":122.55,"en":135.23,"si":11,"ev":"Sweetheart is being planted in larger numbers than either of them and looks to be a real winner.","hl":"Sweetheart","uz":"Sweetheart ikkalasidan ham ko'proq ekilmoqda va haqiqiy g'olibga o'xshaydi.","why":"Symphony va Staccato — ham muvaffaqiyatli, lekin eng ko'p ekilayotgani — Sweetheart."},{"a":["stone"],"ps":141.46,"en":153.5,"si":13,"ev":"Eat a cherry, suck the stone and keep it on your tongue. It stops you putting any more in.","hl":"stone","uz":"Bitta gilos yeng, danagini so'rib, tilingizda saqlang — boshqasini og'izga solishga qo'ymaydi.","why":"\"Suck the stone and keep it on your tongue\" — javob: stone (danak)."}],"segs":[{"s":2.33,"e":7.93,"t":"You'll hear part of a radio program about cherries, small fruit which grow on trees."},{"s":18.74,"e":36.61,"t":"When I visited a number of fruit farms in central England, I found broad agreement among most of the growers that these days it makes sense to move away from their traditional crops, such as apples, and into cherries instead. Now, in summertime, they have orchard after orchard of beautiful trees heavily laden with bright red fruit."},{"s":37.24,"e":47.17,"t":"UK cherry growers tend to choose the varieties which ripen slowly. This fruit may command a higher price because the harvest is not so early and there are always reliable buyers for it."},{"s":47.64,"e":50.81,"t":"Research is currently being carried out into ways of improving yield."},{"s":51.58,"e":61.44,"t":"A major obstacle to efficient production is the fact that growth may not be consistent from season to season. Sometimes the fruit only grows as big as a pea and then drops to the ground."},{"s":62.36,"e":66.75,"t":"Quite a few of the smaller trees are covered up against the rain and wind in a plastic tunnel.","uz":"Ancha kichik daraxtlar yomg'ir va shamoldan plastik tunnel bilan yopib qo'yiladi."},{"s":67.32,"e":77.57,"t":"Older, larger trees have to take their chance out in the open, but cherries are a delicate fruit and optimum weather conditions are needed to achieve the potential yield of 5 tonnes per hectare."},{"s":78.23,"e":92.13,"t":"The surface of the fruit has very little wax on it, so cherries need to be kept out of the rain as much as possible because the skin is liable to crack when water gets into it. If this occurs, the crop may be lost because the fruit bursts with a pop, rather like a balloon."},{"s":92.95,"e":102.08,"t":"When you're selecting the best cherries to buy, don't get them if they look at all tired or wrinkled, and buy the ones with a green stem. You'll find they taste much better than ones without."},{"s":102.84,"e":106.72,"t":"People often ask, \"How long does it take to get a decent crop from a cherry tree?\""},{"s":107.58,"e":121.82,"t":"There are new varieties, laden with fruit, that are only four years old. But if you go back and read the old fruit-growing textbooks from the 1960s, they tell you cherries don't give a worthwhile crop till they're 12 years old. Some varieties go on cropping till they're 90."},{"s":122.55,"e":135.23,"t":"There are three new varieties which have recently been introduced by growers. Symphony and Staccato are both highly successful so far, but Sweetheart is being planted in larger numbers than either of them and looks to be a real winner."},{"s":136.09,"e":140.96,"t":"Just one problem if you go cherry picking this summer, how do you stop yourself eating them all?"},{"s":141.46,"e":153.5,"t":"One expert who's been picking all her life told me, \"Eat a cherry, suck the stone and keep it on your tongue. It stops you putting any more in. That way, you end up with at least a handful of this delicious fruit in your basket.\""}]},{"n":20,"ins":2,"title":"Stella Prime: mountaineer","dur":409.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"On her first expedition, Stella became aware of feelings of freedom connected with mountaineering."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella had previously taken part in several so-called {1} sports."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella found the mental {2} for climbing Everest particularly hard."},{"k":"p","t":"On her second expedition, Stella was worried about the {3} fall she would have to climb through."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella had regretted taking {4} with her on her first expedition."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella says that she didn't take a {5} with her beyond a certain altitude."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella uses the word {6} to describe the feelings of her party on reaching the summit."},{"k":"p","t":"Stella's book about her experience is entitled Aiming High."}],"items":[{"a":["adventure"],"ps":66.55,"en":75.23,"si":11,"ev":"I'd already done numerous similar activities of the sort people like to call \"adventure sports\", you know, hang-gliding, scuba diving and so on.","hl":"adventure","uz":"Men allaqachon odamlar \"sarguzasht sporti\" deb ataydigan ko'plab mashg'ulotlar bilan shug'ullanganman: deltaplan, akvalang va hokazo.","why":"\"So-called\" = \"people like to call\". Javob: adventure."},{"a":["preparation"],"ps":88.73,"en":91.87,"si":15,"ev":"The bit I found trickier was the mental preparation.","hl":"preparation","uz":"Men qiyinroq deb bilgan qism — ruhiy tayyorgarlik edi.","why":"\"The bit I found trickier was the mental preparation\" — javob: preparation."},{"a":["ice"],"ps":101.66,"en":104.19,"si":18,"ev":"One of them was the icefall that you have to climb through.","hl":"icefall","uz":"Ulardan biri — orasidan o'tib ko'tarilish kerak bo'lgan muz sharsharasi (icefall).","why":"\"The icefall\" — topshiriqda \"the {3} fall\": javob ice."},{"a":["perfume"],"ps":126.97,"en":131.45,"si":23,"ev":"The first time I went, as a journalist, I carried my perfume all the way.","hl":"perfume","uz":"Birinchi marta jurnalist sifatida borganimda atirimni butun yo'l ko'tarib yurdim.","why":"Atir kerak emas ekan — \"carried my perfume all the way\". Javob: perfume."},{"a":["toothbrush"],"ps":138.17,"en":142.14,"si":26,"ev":"On my second trip, I didn't even take my toothbrush above 7000 meters.","hl":"toothbrush","uz":"Ikkinchi safarimda tish cho'tkamni ham 7000 metrdan yuqoriga olib chiqmadim.","why":"\"Didn't even take my toothbrush above 7000 metres\" — javob: toothbrush."},{"a":["satisfaction"],"ps":167.13,"en":175.01,"si":33,"ev":"I think the overriding thing we all felt… a great sense of satisfaction.","hl":"satisfaction","uz":"Menimcha, barchamiz his qilgan asosiy tuyg'u… katta mamnuniyat edi.","why":"\"Exciting\" ham aytiladi, lekin asosiy tuyg'u — \"satisfaction\". Javob: satisfaction."}],"segs":[{"s":2.17,"e":9.44,"t":"You'll hear a mountaineer called Stella Prime talking about her experience of climbing Mount Everest in the Himalayas."},{"s":17.21,"e":20.19,"t":"Hello, I'm Stella Prime and I'm a mountaineer."},{"s":20.92,"e":25.6,"t":"I'm here to tell you about climbing Mount Everest in the Himalayas, the world's highest mountain."},{"s":26.97,"e":35.1,"t":"I was first bitten by the climbing bug, when as a journalist I accompanied an expedition on the north-east ridge of Everest some years back."},{"s":35.77,"e":38.49,"t":"I wanted to write about what made Mountaineers tick."},{"s":39.03,"e":41.73,"t":"and over the couple of months I spent with the expedition."},{"s":42.2,"e":47.01,"t":"I began to understand the sense of freedom and achievement that mountaineering brings."},{"s":47.45,"e":50.46,"t":"and I did lots of personal learning and exploration too."},{"s":51.42,"e":53.79,"t":"I think they were the happiest two months of my life."},{"s":54.78,"e":61.53,"t":"Over the next three and a half years, I honed my newly acquired climbing skills on various mountains all over the world."},{"s":62.3,"e":65.82,"t":"People say, \"Went your family surprised by this new interest.\""},{"s":66.55,"e":75.23,"t":"I'd already done numerous similar activities of the sort people like to call \"adventure sports\", you know, hang-gliding, scuba diving and so on.","uz":"Men allaqachon odamlar \"sarguzasht sporti\" deb ataydigan ko'plab mashg'ulotlar bilan shug'ullanganman: deltaplan, akvalang va hokazo."},{"s":76.28,"e":82.01,"t":"Anyway, eventually I gave up my job, let out my flat, and joined the British Everest expedition."},{"s":83.26,"e":86.49,"t":"To prepare physically for this, I trained at my local gym."},{"s":87.1,"e":88.22,"t":"That was the easy part."},{"s":88.73,"e":91.87,"t":"The bit I found trickier was the mental preparation.","uz":"Men qiyinroq deb bilgan qism — ruhiy tayyorgarlik edi."},{"s":92.34,"e":97.34,"t":"And I'd learnt that whilst you have to be physically fit, that is really only half the story."},{"s":98.39,"e":101.02,"t":"and there were lots of things that frightened me about Everest."},{"s":101.66,"e":104.19,"t":"One of them was the icefall that you have to climb through.","uz":"Ulardan biri — orasidan o'tib ko'tarilish kerak bo'lgan muz sharsharasi (icefall)."},{"s":105.08,"e":109.34,"t":"A friend asked if there was any way I could prepare myself for it. I thought we'll--"},{"s":109.78,"e":113.15,"t":"What can I do? Put myself in a fridge and look at lumps of ice?"},{"s":114.62,"e":116.89,"t":"Everest is certainly not a place for cowards."},{"s":117.46,"e":126.14,"t":"And it's also certainly not a place for life's luxuries. You don't carry anything that isn't necessary because weight multiplies at high altitudes."},{"s":126.97,"e":131.45,"t":"The first time I went, as a journalist, I carried my perfume all the way.","uz":"Birinchi marta jurnalist sifatida borganimda atirimni butun yo'l ko'tarib yurdim."},{"s":131.96,"e":133.21,"t":"that it wasn't necessary."},{"s":134.39,"e":136.99,"t":"You can forget baths and showers on a mountain as well."},{"s":138.17,"e":142.14,"t":"On my second trip, I didn't even take my toothbrush above 7000 meters.","uz":"Ikkinchi safarimda tish cho'tkamni ham 7000 metrdan yuqoriga olib chiqmadim."},{"s":142.74,"e":145.25,"t":"The only source of water is melted snow."},{"s":145.75,"e":151.29,"t":"To melt snow, you need fuel and fuel is heavy so you don't melt snow unless you're going to drink it."},{"s":152.95,"e":154.69,"t":"The question I'm asked most often"},{"s":155.38,"e":157.85,"t":"is how did you feel when you reached the summit?"},{"s":160.02,"e":162.05,"t":"I still get emotional when I think about it."},{"s":163.0,"e":166.14,"t":"Neither of the two climbers with me had been to the top before either."},{"s":167.13,"e":175.01,"t":"I think the overriding thing we all felt… a great sense of satisfaction.","uz":"Menimcha, barchamiz his qilgan asosiy tuyg'u… katta mamnuniyat edi."},{"s":176.66,"e":179.29,"t":"That is the thing that stays with me when I look back."},{"s":180.89,"e":186.78,"t":"Since then, I've gone on to climb a number of other summits, and I plan to tackle Mount Fuji later this year."},{"s":188.12,"e":192.41,"t":"course I've got my new career in TV as a presenter on the program Tomorrow's World."},{"s":193.21,"e":198.94,"t":"I am in demand on the lecturing circuit and my book about my ascent of Everest, aiming high, is a best-seller."},{"s":199.64,"e":199.97,"t":"So"},{"s":200.6,"e":201.57,"t":"That's my story."},{"s":202.33,"e":204.32,"t":"Now, does anyone have any questions?"}]},{"n":21,"ins":2,"title":"A visit to the Arctic Circle","dur":335.1,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"As her plane was landing, seals were the first animals Ruth saw."},{"k":"p","t":"Soon after arriving, the team of biologists was able to identify a {1} in the distance."},{"k":"p","t":"The word {2} is used to describe a small patch of ground where the growth of plants is possible."},{"k":"p","t":"The largest part of the yellow Arctic poppy is its {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"The majority of birds returning to the area in the spring feed on {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"The team stayed in tents with small {5} at the entrance."},{"k":"p","t":"Ruth was given advice on what to do if approached by a polar bear."},{"k":"p","t":"It was difficult for Ruth to carry out her work because the {6} are affected by freezing temperatures."}],"items":[{"a":["wolf"],"ps":47.1,"en":61.34,"si":5,"ev":"Ten minutes after we'd landed, I had my first sighting of a wolf, which my eagle-eyed colleagues pointed out to me, at least seven hundred meters away.","hl":"wolf","uz":"Qo'nganimizdan o'n daqiqa o'tib, o'tkir ko'zli hamkasblarim kamida yetti yuz metr narida turgan bo'rini menga ko'rsatishdi.","why":"Uzoqdan ko'rilgan — wolf. Karibu (caribou) — keyinroq va yaqindan ko'rilgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["oasis"],"ps":70.26,"en":80.22,"si":7,"ev":"You may find what's called an oasis. This is a little confined area with access to water where vegetation can establish itself.","hl":"oasis","uz":"\"Voha\" deb ataladigan joyni topishingiz mumkin. Bu suvga yaqin, o'simliklar o'sa oladigan kichik yopiq maydon.","why":"\"What's called an oasis\" — javob: oasis."},{"a":["roots"],"ps":81.4,"en":92.93,"si":8,"ev":"The yellow Arctic poppy … only has a tiny tuft of leaves visible as the bulk of the plant and network of roots stays underground.","hl":"roots","uz":"Sariq arktika lolaqizg'aldog'ining faqat kichkina barg tutami ko'rinadi, o'simlikning asosiy qismi — ildizlar tarmog'i yer ostida qoladi.","why":"\"The bulk of the plant\" = eng katta qismi — roots. Barglar (leaves) — juda kichik, tuzoq."},{"a":["seeds"],"ps":107.0,"en":116.83,"si":11,"ev":"Most of these birds get their nourishment from seeds, although a predator like the snowy owl feeds on small mammals called lemmings.","hl":"seeds","uz":"Bu qushlarning ko'pchiligi urug'lar bilan oziqlanadi, oq boyo'g'li kabi yirtqich esa lemming degan mayda sutemizuvchilarni yeydi.","why":"\"Most of these birds … seeds\" — javob: seeds. Lemmings va fish — ozchilikniki, tuzoq."},{"a":["tunnels"],"ps":117.91,"en":128.03,"si":12,"ev":"We had tents which looked just like the igloos … with little tunnels at the front.","hl":"tunnels","uz":"Bizning chodirlarimiz iglularga o'xshardi… old tomonida kichik tunnellari bor edi.","why":"\"Little tunnels at the front\" → \"small tunnels at the entrance\". Javob: tunnels."},{"a":["batteries"],"ps":157.98,"en":165.63,"si":17,"ev":"The recorder itself was fine, but batteries just don't work in the cold.","hl":"batteries","uz":"Yozib olish moslamasining o'zi joyida edi, lekin batareyalar sovuqda ishlamaydi.","why":"\"Batteries just don't work in the cold\" — javob: batteries. Recorder — buzilmagan, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":2.1,"e":10.37,"t":"You'll hear a reporter called Ruth Sampson describing a visit she made to the Arctic Circle with a team of Canadian wildlife experts."},{"s":23.7,"e":29.76,"t":"Last year, I found myself flying to the Arctic Circle with five biologists from the Canadian Wildlife Service."},{"s":30.33,"e":36.03,"t":"As our small plane descended towards a snow-covered runway, I looked out of the window at the frozen ocean below."},{"s":36.76,"e":42.59,"t":"You could see small holes in the ice, and around them lots of extraordinary little figures rather like ants."},{"s":43.13,"e":46.33,"t":"I was told they were seals basking on the ice in the sun."},{"s":47.1,"e":61.34,"t":"Ten minutes after we'd landed, I had my first sighting of a wolf, which my eagle-eyed colleagues pointed out to me, at least seven hundred meters away, and later on I was lucky enough to see a caribou with its huge antlers at much closer range."},{"s":62.68,"e":69.53,"t":"The Arctic seems to be a kind of desert, but there are plants and animals around. You just have to look around for them."},{"s":70.26,"e":80.22,"t":"You may find what's called an oasis. This is a little confined area with access to water where vegetation can establish itself and provide nutrients for animals."},{"s":81.4,"e":92.93,"t":"plants have evolved to cope with this harsh environment like the yellow Arctic poppy which only has a tiny tuft of leaves visible as the bulk of the plant and network of roots stays underground."},{"s":93.66,"e":98.01,"t":"Its leaves remain green all winter so it can make the most of the short growing season."},{"s":99.19,"e":106.46,"t":"The diversity of bird species decreases as you travel north, but there are birds which spend the winter here, and others that come back in the spring."},{"s":107.0,"e":116.83,"t":"Most of these birds get their nourishment from seeds, although a predator like the snowy owl feeds on small mammals called lemmings, and others do manage to find fish."},{"s":117.91,"e":128.03,"t":"For accommodation we had tents which looked just like the igloos the local Inuit people built out of ice, with little tunnels at the front. Only ours were orange and made of nylon."},{"s":128.5,"e":131.58,"t":"and our only connection to the outside world was our radio link.\""},{"s":132.34,"e":146.05,"t":"You notice how light the snow cover is. It scatters with the wind and there are hardly any deep drifts. Apart from the cold, the main hazard is the wildlife. And I received a brief introduction on the correct action to take if a polar bear came to visit."},{"s":146.71,"e":150.69,"t":"There are other large animals like the muskox but they seldom pose a threat."},{"s":151.29,"e":157.53,"t":"Another thing was that recording the team's descriptions of wildlife, which was my task, was incredibly difficult."},{"s":157.98,"e":165.63,"t":"The recorder itself was fine, but batteries just don't work in the cold, so I had to hold them inside my thick coat to keep them warm."},{"s":166.23,"e":167.42,"t":"But on the whole, I've"}]},{"n":22,"ins":2,"title":"Skydiving","dur":399.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Kate says that in the USA people from a variety of age groups enjoy skydiving."},{"k":"p","t":"Kate first tried skydiving when she was a {1} and it cost relatively little."},{"k":"p","t":"Kate says skydiving can help overcome fear of {2} and increase confidence."},{"k":"p","t":"More people are buying skydiving equipment from {3} these days."},{"k":"p","t":"Kate recently bought a {4} at a bargain price."},{"k":"p","t":"To become an instructor, a skydiver must have done at least 2,000 previous jumps."},{"k":"p","t":"You can find the Parachute Association by contacting the nearest {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Kate advises people to spend a period of several {6} learning to skydive."}],"items":[{"a":["student"],"ps":53.37,"en":58.4,"si":5,"ev":"So my first jump was as a university student when I was able to get a discount.","hl":"student","uz":"Shuning uchun birinchi sakrashim universitet talabasi bo'lganimda, chegirma bilan bo'lgan.","why":"\"As a university student … a discount\" — javob: student. O'smirlik (teenager) — ota-onasi ruxsat bermagan, tuzoq."},{"a":["heights"],"ps":82.07,"en":86.4,"si":10,"ev":"Of course, some people start skydiving to help them get over a fear of heights.","hl":"heights","uz":"Albatta, ba'zilar balandlikdan qo'rqishni yengish uchun parashyut sportini boshlashadi.","why":"\"Get over a fear of heights\" — javob: heights."},{"a":["websites"],"ps":104.54,"en":110.85,"si":14,"ev":"Nowadays most people buy skydiving kit from websites.","hl":"websites","uz":"Hozir ko'pchilik parashyut jihozlarini veb-saytlardan sotib oladi.","why":"\"From websites\" — javob: websites. Mahalliy sport do'konlarida topish qiyin — tuzoq."},{"a":["helmet"],"ps":117.4,"en":123.23,"si":16,"ev":"I got my skydiving camera that way and last week I got a helmet with a 50% discount.","hl":"helmet","uz":"Kamerani shu yo'l bilan oldim, o'tgan hafta esa 50 foiz chegirma bilan dubulg'a oldim.","why":"\"Last week … a helmet with a 50% discount\" — \"recently, bargain price\". Javob: helmet. Kamera ham shu yo'l bilan olingan, lekin chegirma haqida gap dubulg'ada."},{"a":["airport"],"ps":174.07,"en":181.73,"si":25,"ev":"If you're interested, you need to get in touch with the Parachute Association and you'll find the contact details through your local airport.","hl":"airport","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, Parashyut assotsiatsiyasi bilan bog'lanishingiz kerak; aloqa ma'lumotlarini mahalliy aeroportingizdan topasiz.","why":"\"Through your local airport\" → \"the nearest airport\". Javob: airport."},{"a":["months"],"ps":188.54,"en":194.46,"si":28,"ev":"I suggest the best way is to do it over several months.","hl":"months","uz":"Menimcha, eng yaxshi yo'li — buni bir necha oy davomida o'rganish.","why":"\"Over a weekend\" ham mumkin, lekin Keyt maslahati — \"several months\". Javob: months."}],"segs":[{"s":2.3,"e":8.19,"t":"You'll hear a woman called Kaita Sadi talking to a group of people interested in taking up skydiving."},{"s":19.99,"e":20.41,"t":"So?"},{"s":20.92,"e":25.85,"t":"I'm Kate Asadi and I'm here to talk about my hobby, which is skydiving."},{"s":26.46,"e":45.69,"t":"So, why do people want to jump out of a plane? In the UK, this is still seen as something done by crazy young people. But in the USA, skydiving is a hobby that has been taken up by people from all age groups. By anyone looking for excitement, from 20 year olds to people enjoying an active retirement."},{"s":46.42,"e":52.8,"t":"I wanted to do skydiving as a teenager, but my parents weren't very keen on the idea and wouldn't give their permission."},{"s":53.37,"e":58.4,"t":"So my first jump was as a university student when I was able to get a discount.","uz":"Shuning uchun birinchi sakrashim universitet talabasi bo'lganimda, chegirma bilan bo'lgan."},{"s":58.87,"e":65.34,"t":"Immediately, I was hooked. I couldn't afford to do it regularly though until I started working as a lawyer."},{"s":66.68,"e":68.73,"t":"Why do I do it? Well..."},{"s":69.21,"e":72.96,"t":"Skydiving makes you feel great. You forget all your problems."},{"s":73.5,"e":81.15,"t":"There aren't really any health benefits, although I know several business executives with stressful jobs who do skydiving to help them relax."},{"s":82.07,"e":86.4,"t":"Of course, some people start skydiving to help them get over a fear of heights.","uz":"Albatta, ba'zilar balandlikdan qo'rqishni yengish uchun parashyut sportini boshlashadi."},{"s":86.87,"e":95.49,"t":"If they can face up to their fear and jump out of a plane at a height of 3,000 meters, it helps them to build up the confidence to tackle other things."},{"s":96.5,"e":97.98,"t":"So, how do you start?"},{"s":98.71,"e":103.9,"t":"The equipment for skydiving is specialised and not easy to get in local sports shops."},{"s":104.54,"e":110.85,"t":"Nowadays most people buy skydiving kit from websites. There's more choice and you can see photographs."},{"s":111.48,"e":116.48,"t":"So when you're buying second hand on the internet, you should ask to see the equipment first."},{"s":117.4,"e":123.23,"t":"I got my skydiving camera that way and last week I got a helmet with a 50% discount.","uz":"Kamerani shu yo'l bilan oldim, o'tgan hafta esa 50 foiz chegirma bilan dubulg'a oldim."},{"s":123.86,"e":128.29,"t":"You need a good helmet by the way. It's the most important part of your equipment."},{"s":129.18,"e":139.17,"t":"For your first skydive, you jump from a height of over 3,000 metres, strapped to an instructor who is required to have done at least 2,000 jumps before."},{"s":140.06,"e":148.93,"t":"dive down in free fall for 30 seconds and when the parachute opens you float down sedately landing very gently"},{"s":149.53,"e":152.29,"t":"After that, most people can't wait to have another go."},{"s":153.4,"e":156.03,"t":"Still nervous? Don't worry."},{"s":156.6,"e":167.87,"t":"All trainee skydivers must wear an appliance known as the automatic parachute. It's compulsory. So even if you black out, your parachute will still open on its own."},{"s":168.5,"e":170.53,"t":"These rules are for safety reasons."},{"s":171.13,"e":172.99,"t":"So, what's stopping you?"},{"s":174.07,"e":181.73,"t":"If you're interested, you need to get in touch with the Parachute Association and you'll find the contact details through your local airport.","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, Parashyut assotsiatsiyasi bilan bog'lanishingiz kerak; aloqa ma'lumotlarini mahalliy aeroportingizdan topasiz."},{"s":182.33,"e":184.41,"t":"They'll give advice on how to get started."},{"s":185.02,"e":187.9,"t":"You can learn to skydive over a weekend."},{"s":188.54,"e":194.46,"t":"but I suggest the best way is to do it over several months. That allows you to build up your confidence gradually."},{"s":195.51,"e":197.18,"t":"Skydiving's great!"},{"s":197.72,"e":200.06,"t":"It'll give you a whole new outlook on life."}]},{"n":23,"ins":2,"title":"Making mosaics","dur":429.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Rosa feels that the real experts in mosaics were the Greeks."},{"k":"p","t":"Rosa says that the greatest changes have occurred in the {1} of mosaics."},{"k":"p","t":"Until recently, modern mosaics were mostly found in public {2} and swimming pools."},{"k":"p","t":"Rosa says that the process of making mosaics calls for both time and motivation."},{"k":"p","t":"Most students attend what's called a weekend {3} as part of their course."},{"k":"p","t":"Rosa admits that making mosaics can be compared to doing {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Rosa gives the example of ashtrays and soap {5} as objects that are now being made using mosaics."},{"k":"p","t":"Rosa has even considered putting a mosaic border on chests of {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["design"],"ps":68.06,"en":71.58,"si":7,"ev":"It's the designs which have undergone a really radical change.","hl":"designs","uz":"Tubdan o'zgargani — bu dizaynlar.","why":"\"Designs … a really radical change\". Texnika esa 5000 yilda deyarli o'zgarmagan, tuzoq. Javob: design."},{"a":["libraries"],"ps":72.34,"en":84.8,"si":8,"ev":"In the recent past, modern mosaics have been restricted to the walls of public libraries and the odd swimming pool.","hl":"libraries","uz":"Yaqin o'tmishda zamonaviy mozaikalar faqat jamoat kutubxonalari devorlari va ba'zi basseynlarda bo'lgan.","why":"\"Public libraries\" — javob: libraries."},{"a":["workshop"],"ps":141.3,"en":149.89,"si":14,"ev":"Each course includes a weekend workshop which is attended by the majority of the students.","hl":"workshop","uz":"Har bir kursda dam olish kunlari bo'ladigan amaliy mashg'ulot bor, unga talabalarning ko'pchiligi qatnashadi.","why":"\"Weekend workshop\" — javob: workshop."},{"a":["puzzles"],"ps":150.97,"en":159.68,"si":15,"ev":"I'm often asked if I do puzzles, and it's not such a silly question as it sounds because it's a very good comparison of skills.","hl":"puzzles","uz":"Mendan tez-tez boshqotirma yechasizmi, deb so'rashadi. Bu unchalik ahmoqona savol emas, chunki ko'nikmalar juda o'xshash.","why":"\"A very good comparison of skills\" — mozaika boshqotirmaga o'xshatiladi. Javob: puzzles."},{"a":["dishes"],"ps":177.78,"en":185.92,"si":19,"ev":"Not only do you see mosaic ashtrays and soap dishes, but you can actually now find them decorating underground station walls.","hl":"dishes","uz":"Mozaikali kuldonlar va sovun idishlarini ko'rasiz, hatto metro bekatlari devorlarida ham uchratasiz.","why":"\"Soap dishes\" — javob: dishes."},{"a":["drawers"],"ps":194.01,"en":200.99,"si":21,"ev":"Although I often find myself looking at chests of drawers and thinking… Hmmm, just a border perhaps.","hl":"drawers","uz":"Garchi ko'pincha tortmali javonlarga qarab: \"Hmm, balki faqat cheti…\" deb o'ylab qolsam-da.","why":"\"Chests of drawers … just a border\" — javob: drawers."}],"segs":[{"s":2.26,"e":11.58,"t":"You'll hear an art teacher called Rosa Weston giving a talk about making mosaics, works of art that are made out of small pieces of glass and stone."},{"s":28.41,"e":32.48,"t":"I started teaching art for about 10 years when I went on holiday to Greece."},{"s":33.24,"e":41.15,"t":"While I was there, I became really interested in the art of making mosaics and decided to include this in the courses I run."},{"s":42.23,"e":48.35,"t":"Many people assumed that the Romans invented mosaic, but it was the Greeks who were the true craftsmen."},{"s":48.82,"e":52.67,"t":"and they in turn probably picked it up from the Sumerians."},{"s":53.56,"e":56.61,"t":"But it was the Romans who brought mosaics to Britain."},{"s":57.53,"e":67.01,"t":"and apart from the introduction of nylon backing to hold the tiles together, the techniques themselves haven't changed much over 5,000 years."},{"s":68.06,"e":71.58,"t":"It's the designs which have undergone a really radical change.","uz":"Tubdan o'zgargani — bu dizaynlar."},{"s":72.34,"e":84.8,"t":"In the recent past, modern mosaics have been restricted to the walls of public libraries and the odd swimming pool, and by and large, it looked as if the true art of the mosaic could well disappear."},{"s":85.4,"e":87.65,"t":"Unfortunately, that has not happened."},{"s":88.86,"e":98.24,"t":"People often ask me why I prefer to spend hours teaching my students to stick tiny squares onto tiles when I could be doing something else."},{"s":98.87,"e":115.77,"t":"And it's certainly the case that the process demands both time and motivation on occasions. It can even give you a really bad headache. But in fact, there's something very therapeutic about it. I think it has something to do with breaking things up and then reconstructing them."},{"s":117.02,"e":131.17,"t":"For every course I teach, we have jars and jars of brightly coloured glass, odd bits of china, broken plates and dishes, and most people just can't wait to start sticking them onto larger stretches of concrete."},{"s":132.12,"e":140.57,"t":"For the beginners, we produce mosaic packs which contain all the essentials you need and explain clearly how to go about things."},{"s":141.3,"e":149.89,"t":"Each course includes a weekend workshop which is attended by the majority of the students and it's actually a wonderful way of relaxing."},{"s":150.97,"e":159.68,"t":"I'm often asked if I do puzzles, and it's not such a silly question as it sounds because it's a very good comparison of skills.","uz":"Mendan tez-tez boshqotirma yechasizmi, deb so'rashadi. Bu unchalik ahmoqona savol emas, chunki ko'nikmalar juda o'xshash."},{"s":160.34,"e":166.72,"t":"some people do get a bit scared faced with all that choice but that's why the mosaic packs are so popular"},{"s":167.22,"e":170.21,"t":"But I try to teach people to be inventive as well."},{"s":171.7,"e":176.96,"t":"If you look around yourself, there's plenty of evidence that the art is enjoying a revival."},{"s":177.78,"e":185.92,"t":"Not only do you see mosaic ashtrays and soap dishes, but you can actually now find them decorating underground station walls.","uz":"Mozaikali kuldonlar va sovun idishlarini ko'rasiz, hatto metro bekatlari devorlarida ham uchratasiz."},{"s":187.03,"e":193.44,"t":"Now I'm not suggesting that you start pulling your own home to pieces and replacing everything with mosaics"},{"s":194.01,"e":200.99,"t":"Although I often find myself looking at chests of drawers and thinking… Hmmm, just a border perhaps.","uz":"Garchi ko'pincha tortmali javonlarga qarab: \"Hmm, balki faqat cheti…\" deb o'ylab qolsam-da."},{"s":201.98,"e":214.4,"t":"Still, my reply to my over-anxious students is, \"All right, I know it takes hours, but after all, it's a labour of love, and you have something which will give pleasure for a long time afterwards.\""},{"s":215.35,"e":218.62,"t":"Now if you're interested in trying out the effect in your own"}]},{"n":24,"ins":2,"title":"The albatross","dur":380.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Tim thinks that the name 'albatross' comes originally from a word in the Arabic language."},{"k":"p","t":"There are currently thought to be a total of {1} species of albatross."},{"k":"p","t":"The fact that it relies on {2} explains why the albatross isn't found in some areas."},{"k":"p","t":"By using a locking mechanism in its {3}, the albatross can save energy when flying."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim explains that the albatross has a surprisingly good sense of {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim was surprised to discover that {5} attack albatross nests."},{"k":"p","t":"The albatross used to be hunted mostly for its {6} as well as for food."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim gives the example of bottle caps as plastic objects commonly eaten by albatrosses."}],"items":[{"a":["21","twenty-one"],"ps":63.19,"en":69.76,"si":9,"ev":"Nowadays, a figure of 21 is widely accepted, with 19 of those identified as being in danger of extinction.","hl":"21","uz":"Hozir 21 raqami keng qabul qilingan, ulardan 19 tasi yo'qolib ketish xavfi ostida.","why":"\"A figure of 21 is widely accepted\" — javob: 21. 13 va 80 — eski taxminlar; 19 — xavf ostidagilar, tuzoq."},{"a":["wind"],"ps":70.55,"en":87.29,"si":10,"ev":"The bird … depends on the wind to a great extent. That's why you rarely find them in tropical areas where long periods of calm are common.","hl":"wind","uz":"Qush ko'p jihatdan shamolga bog'liq. Shuning uchun uzoq shamolsiz davrlar bo'ladigan tropik hududlarda kam uchraydi.","why":"\"Depends on the wind … that's why\" — javob: wind."},{"a":["shoulders"],"ps":92.89,"en":101.82,"si":12,"ev":"Apart from take off and landing it rarely flaps its huge wings and actually there's a locking mechanism in its shoulder that keeps the wings in place as it glides through the air.","hl":"shoulder","uz":"Uchish va qo'nishdan tashqari u ulkan qanotlarini kamdan-kam qoqadi; yelkasida qanotlarni bir holatda ushlab turadigan qulf mexanizmi bor.","why":"\"A locking mechanism in its shoulder\" — javob: shoulders (shoulder)."},{"a":["smell"],"ps":109.11,"en":113.53,"si":14,"ev":"What I didn't expect to find, however, was that it can also detect the smell of its food.","hl":"smell","uz":"Kutmaganim shu bo'ldiki, u ovqatining hidini ham sezar ekan.","why":"Ko'rish (eyesight) — kutilgan; hid bilish — kutilmagan. Javob: smell."},{"a":["mice"],"ps":148.79,"en":152.51,"si":19,"ev":"Apparently even little mice can be a problem at nest sites which is incredible.","hl":"mice","uz":"Aytishlaricha, hatto kichkina sichqonlar ham uyalar uchun muammo bo'lishi mumkin — bu aql bovar qilmaydigan narsa.","why":"\"Incredible\" → \"surprised\". Rats va cats — kutilgan, tuzoq. Javob: mice."},{"a":["feathers"],"ps":153.3,"en":162.17,"si":20,"ev":"Sailors used to eat them, and at one time their feathers were highly valued, which was actually the main reason.","hl":"feathers","uz":"Dengizchilar ularni yeyishgan, bir paytlar patlari juda qadrlangan — asosiy sabab aslida shu edi.","why":"\"Feathers … the main reason\" — javob: feathers."}],"segs":[{"s":4.85,"e":6.4,"t":"giving a class presentation."},{"s":6.64,"e":9.46,"t":"about a seabird called the albatross."},{"s":23.51,"e":27.87,"t":"Hi, my name's Tim and the topic of my presentation is a seabird called the albatross."},{"s":28.38,"e":35.58,"t":"It's the largest seabird and it's always been a great favourite with sailors. It's also well known because it features in a famous English poem."},{"s":36.25,"e":43.65,"t":"The word albatross came into the English language via the Portuguese word alcatraz that was used for similar birds called ganets."},{"s":44.15,"e":47.23,"t":"The famous American prison island was also named after them."},{"s":47.74,"e":51.65,"t":"But the real origin of the word is thought to be Arabic, where it means 'diver'."},{"s":52.41,"e":57.95,"t":"There's lots of different species of Albatross and scientists are always arguing about exactly how many."},{"s":58.52,"e":62.56,"t":"Over the years estimates have varied from 13 to as many as 80."},{"s":63.19,"e":69.76,"t":"Nowadays, a figure of 21 is widely accepted, with 19 of those identified as being in danger of extinction.","uz":"Hozir 21 raqami keng qabul qilingan, ulardan 19 tasi yo'qolib ketish xavfi ostida."},{"s":70.55,"e":87.29,"t":"The albatross is mostly found in the southern hemisphere and there's none in the North Atlantic. The bird travels long distances in search of its food, fish and squid mostly, and depends on the wind to a great extent. That's why you rarely find them in tropical areas where long periods of calm are common."},{"s":88.12,"e":92.38,"t":"The Albatross manages to cover such long distances by conserving energy."},{"s":92.89,"e":101.82,"t":"Apart from take off and landing it rarely flaps its huge wings and actually there's a locking mechanism in its shoulder that keeps the wings in place as it glides through the air.","uz":"Uchish va qo'nishdan tashqari u ulkan qanotlarini kamdan-kam qoqadi; yelkasida qanotlarni bir holatda ushlab turadigan qulf mexanizmi bor."},{"s":102.65,"e":108.57,"t":"As you'd expect, the bird's got good eyesight and will swoop down when it sees signs of food near the surface of the water."},{"s":109.11,"e":113.53,"t":"What I didn't expect to find, however, was that it can also detect the smell of its food.","uz":"Kutmaganim shu bo'ldiki, u ovqatining hidini ham sezar ekan."},{"s":113.98,"e":117.6,"t":"This explains why it follows fishing boats that use dead fish as bait."},{"s":118.1,"e":123.74,"t":"Indeed, one of the reasons the albatross is such an endangered bird is that it tends to get caught up in fishing nets."},{"s":124.41,"e":137.6,"t":"Another reason the albatross faces extinction is it takes a long time to reproduce. The bird can live for 60 years and only starts breeding from the age of 5. Even then, each pair of birds only produces one egg per year."},{"s":138.39,"e":148.29,"t":"Build nests on remote uninhabited islands because animals like rats, which arrive at the same time as humans, will eat the eggs and predictably cats will kill the chicks."},{"s":148.79,"e":152.51,"t":"Apparently even little mice can be a problem at nest sites which is incredible.","uz":"Aytishlaricha, hatto kichkina sichqonlar ham uyalar uchun muammo bo'lishi mumkin — bu aql bovar qilmaydigan narsa."},{"s":153.3,"e":162.17,"t":"And, of course, the albatross has always been killed by people. Sailors used to eat them, and at one time their feathers were highly valued, which was actually the main reason."},{"s":162.81,"e":168.77,"t":"Even the birds bones were used in certain ceremonies by local populations, though that wasn't on a big scale."},{"s":169.56,"e":173.5,"t":"These days plastic is the biggest enemy and there's tons of it in the sea."},{"s":174.01,"e":195.45,"t":"Eating plastic doesn't in itself kill an albatross, but it tends to stay in the stomach and so cut down the amount of food the bird can digest, which then weakens it. Some dead birds have even been found with weird things like plastic cigarette lighters and toy soldiers in their stomachs, as well as the all too common bottle caps. There must be a way of stopping those getting into the sea."},{"s":196.34,"e":198.11,"t":"Anyway, before I go on to talk about-"}]},{"n":25,"ins":2,"title":"Learning the sport of surfing","dur":384.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Carl recommends the National Park as the best place for learning to surf in his area."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl uses the term {1} to describe the distance between waves."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl advises getting a wetsuit that has a {2} fit."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl says it's important to check the quantity of material beneath the {3} of a new wetsuit."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl says that the wetsuit, {4} and footwear all need washing regularly."},{"k":"p","t":"According to Carl, a hanger made of {5} is best for storing wetsuits."},{"k":"p","t":"Beginners most often damage surfboards through contact with {6}."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl suggests using a hair-dryer as the first step in removing wax from a surfboard."}],"items":[{"a":["period"],"ps":58.74,"en":63.29,"si":5,"ev":"The distance between waves is measured in seconds and we call that the period.","hl":"period","uz":"To'lqinlar orasidagi masofa soniyalarda o'lchanadi va biz uni \"period\" deymiz.","why":"\"We call that the period\" — javob: period. \"Fetch\" va \"sets\" — boshqa atamalar, tuzoq."},{"a":["tight"],"ps":73.91,"en":82.08,"si":8,"ev":"A new suit should almost feel too tight.","hl":"tight","uz":"Yangi kostyum deyarli juda tor tuyulishi kerak.","why":"\"Feel too tight\" — javob: tight. Bo'sh (loose) bo'lsa, ko'proq suv ushlaydi."},{"a":["arms"],"ps":92.79,"en":105.28,"si":11,"ev":"Make sure you have lots of length in the legs and that you have no folds of material under your arms.","hl":"arms","uz":"Oyoqlarda uzunlik yetarli bo'lsin, qo'ltiq ostida mato burmalari bo'lmasin.","why":"\"Under your arms\" — javob: arms."},{"a":["gloves"],"ps":105.82,"en":119.52,"si":12,"ev":"Use a mild detergent … to wash your suit, and especially your boots and gloves regularly.","hl":"gloves","uz":"Kostyumni, ayniqsa botinka va qo'lqoplarni muntazam yumshoq vosita bilan yuving.","why":"Kostyum, footwear (boots) va gloves — javob: gloves."},{"a":["plastic"],"ps":120.44,"en":131.26,"si":13,"ev":"Keep your suit on a wide plastic hanger. Metal hangers … will create creases … and wooden hangers aren't much better.","hl":"plastic","uz":"Kostyumni keng plastik ilgichda saqlang. Metall ilgichlar burma qoldiradi, yog'ochlari ham yaxshi emas.","why":"Eng yaxshisi — plastic. Metal va wooden — tuzoq."},{"a":["knees"],"ps":144.95,"en":170.52,"si":17,"ev":"The main problem is when beginners hit the board with their knees and put great dents in them.","hl":"knees","uz":"Asosiy muammo — yangi boshlovchilar taxtaga tizzalari bilan urib, katta chuqurchalar qoldirishadi.","why":"\"The main problem … knees\" — javob: knees. Mashina va devorlar — ikkinchi darajali."}],"segs":[{"s":3.48,"e":10.53,"t":"You'll hear a man called Carl Pittman giving a group of tourists practical advice about learning the sport of surfing."},{"s":16.47,"e":41.44,"t":"Hi, I've come along to tell you about surfing here on the island, something I know many of you want to learn. Now, you can learn to surf anywhere that waves break on a swimmable shoreline. On this island, most of the local population lives around the north coast. We often see waves on it, but you rarely see surfers there. The National Park, on the other hand, has miles of sandy shoreline with plenty of elbow room for beginners to develop their surfing skills."},{"s":41.56,"e":43.65,"t":"I'd say that was your best choice of venue."},{"s":44.41,"e":49.5,"t":"Now, surfers need waves, and waves are generated by wind moving across water."},{"s":50.01,"e":58.08,"t":"The further the wind drags across the water, called fetch, the more powerful the waves, which then spread out and fall into groups we call sets."},{"s":58.74,"e":63.29,"t":"The distance between waves is measured in seconds and we call that the period.","uz":"To'lqinlar orasidagi masofa soniyalarda o'lchanadi va biz uni \"period\" deymiz."},{"s":63.86,"e":68.45,"t":"We see just the very top of waves. Most of the energy goes deep into the ocean."},{"s":69.18,"e":73.44,"t":"The ocean here is not warm, so surfers wear wetsuits most of the time."},{"s":73.91,"e":82.08,"t":"These keep you warm by trapping a thin layer of water against your body, which your body heats. A new suit should almost feel too tight."},{"s":82.68,"e":86.24,"t":"If the fit of your suit is too loose, then it will hold more water."},{"s":86.68,"e":92.06,"t":"If you start shivering uncontrollably, then this may be the problem and you should go in and get warm."},{"s":92.79,"e":105.28,"t":"New materials will stretch out and conform to your body. Make sure you have lots of length in the legs and that you have no folds of material under your arms. It's also important to check that it fits well over your lower back."},{"s":105.82,"e":119.52,"t":"Rinse your suit thoroughly every time you use it. Use a mild detergent or a wetsuit-specific soap in warm water to wash your suit, and especially your boots and gloves regularly. Hot water is not recommended for wetsuits."},{"s":120.44,"e":131.26,"t":"keep your suit on a wide plastic hanger. Metal hangers, especially wire ones, will create creases that will be the first wear out points on your suit and wooden hangers aren't much better."},{"s":132.06,"e":133.82,"t":"increases decrease lifespan"},{"s":134.36,"e":141.02,"t":"Do not store your suit in direct sunlight. It will lose elasticity and become stiff and brittle before its time."},{"s":141.69,"e":144.51,"t":"Now the other thing you'll need is a surfboard."},{"s":144.95,"e":170.52,"t":"Don't go out and buy a new one straight away. The surfboard you use as an accomplished surfer will be far too fragile to take you through the learning process. The main problem is when beginners hit the board with their knees and put great dents in them. But they also tend to lean surfboards against cars and walls where they can fall over or bump into pointy things when carrying them. So I'd say always borrow your friends board to learn on."},{"s":170.74,"e":172.22,"t":"Or maybe rent one."},{"s":173.34,"e":190.17,"t":"Your board will need waxing. Surfers use wax to help them stay on their boards whereas skaters and snowboarders use it to make their boards slide. If you want to clean old wax off, leave your board in the sun for a while or better still, use a hair dryer and then use a wax comb or plastic scraper."},{"s":190.81,"e":196.86,"t":"Citrus based cleaner on a cloth will clean up the rest now before I go on to the next"}]},{"n":26,"ins":2,"title":"Working with chocolate","dur":380.0,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Janine trained as a chemist before working for her current employer."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine found her background particularly helpful when working on a project to put {1} into chocolate."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine uses the word {2} to describe chocolate as a substance to work with."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine mentions the method of {3} the cocoa beans as a variable affecting the taste of her chocolate."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine says that ideas for new types of chocolate generally come from her company's {4} department."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine says the staff responsible for packaging play a surprisingly important role in developing a new chocolate product."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine gives the example of {5} as a group that need to be considered when designing the label for a product."},{"k":"p","t":"Janine thinks that {6} is the most essential quality needed for her job."}],"items":[{"a":["bubbles"],"ps":58.58,"en":71.07,"si":7,"ev":"Last month I had to come up with a way of introducing bubbles into the chocolate mixture.","hl":"bubbles","uz":"O'tgan oy shokolad aralashmasiga pufakchalar kiritish usulini o'ylab topishim kerak edi.","why":"\"Introducing bubbles into the chocolate\" → \"put bubbles into chocolate\". Javob: bubbles. Karamel — hozirgi ishi, tuzoq."},{"a":["problematic"],"ps":78.52,"en":95.26,"si":9,"ev":"It's not exactly a simple substance to work with. I'd even go so far as to call it problematic.","hl":"problematic","uz":"Bu ishlash oson modda emas. Hatto uni muammoli deb ham atagan bo'lardim.","why":"\"Call it problematic\" — javob: problematic."},{"a":["drying"],"ps":104.82,"en":112.86,"si":11,"ev":"Things like the climate of the region where the beans are grown have an effect, as does the technique used for drying them.","hl":"drying","uz":"Donlar yetishtiriladigan hudud iqlimi, shuningdek ularni quritish usuli ta'sir qiladi.","why":"\"Technique used for drying them\" → \"method of drying the cocoa beans\". Javob: drying."},{"a":["marketing"],"ps":122.2,"en":133.95,"si":13,"ev":"The marketing team will come up with a concept for a new range and it's my job in research and development to bring that idea to life.","hl":"marketing","uz":"Marketing jamoasi yangi mahsulot g'oyasini o'ylab topadi, men esa tadqiqot va ishlanmalar bo'limida uni hayotga tatbiq etaman.","why":"G'oya — marketing bo'limidan. Javob: marketing."},{"a":["vegetarians"],"ps":161.85,"en":169.18,"si":18,"ev":"We need to be aware whether we're making something that's not suitable for vegetarians, say, but we haven't stated this in our labelling.","hl":"vegetarians","uz":"Vegetarianlar uchun mos bo'lmagan narsa qilayotgan bo'lsak-u, buni yorliqda ko'rsatmagan bo'lsak — buni bilishimiz kerak.","why":"Yorliqda hisobga olinadigan guruh — vegetarians."},{"a":["initiative"],"ps":173.3,"en":180.89,"si":20,"ev":"Well, a curiosity about how things work and why. But above and beyond all else, you need initiative and lots of it.","hl":"initiative","uz":"Narsalar qanday va nima uchun ishlashiga qiziqish. Lekin hammasidan muhimi — tashabbuskorlik, va ko'p.","why":"\"Curiosity\" ham kerak, lekin \"above and beyond all else\" — initiative."}],"segs":[{"s":5.53,"e":10.4,"t":"You'll hear a woman called Janine Rogers giving a talk about her work."},{"s":17.88,"e":26.11,"t":"Hello everyone, my name is Janine Rogers and I've got what many people would regard as a dream job. I'm a chocolate taster."},{"s":26.74,"e":37.66,"t":"My route into the job came after graduation. As a qualified chemist, I was looking to specialise as a lab technician, but when nothing came up, I considered retraining as a chef."},{"s":38.1,"e":43.52,"t":"Then I spotted a vacancy in the company I'm in now, and that's where my career started."},{"s":44.28,"e":49.41,"t":"Everyone has a very specific professional title, mine being Product Developer."},{"s":49.94,"e":54.24,"t":"It doesn't cover everything I do, but it perfectly describes one aspect of the role."},{"s":55.29,"e":58.11,"t":"My background has been a real asset to my work here."},{"s":58.58,"e":71.07,"t":"I'm currently creating the perfect fillings for our chocolate. At the moment it's caramel, but last month I had to come up with a way of introducing bubbles into the chocolate mixture. It may sound trivial, but it's what sells the chocolate."},{"s":71.51,"e":77.02,"t":"And I suspect only someone with my technical knowledge would have had the know-how to pull that off."},{"s":78.52,"e":95.26,"t":"It may sound wonderful to work with chocolate all day but it's not exactly a simple substance to work with. I'd even go so far as to call it problematic. That's because we're using a blend of fat as well as cocoa, which means the approaches we use and the time we spend blending it can be crucial."},{"s":96.73,"e":104.35,"t":"A lot of variables can affect how chocolate tastes. It doesn't naturally occur as the sweet tasting confection we're all familiar with."},{"s":104.82,"e":112.86,"t":"Things like the climate of the region where the beans are grown have an effect, as does the technique used for drying them and the amount of sugar we put in the chocolate."},{"s":114.2,"e":121.73,"t":"I spend about 20% of my time actually tasting chocolate. But of course the end result is all the work of a team."},{"s":122.2,"e":133.95,"t":"For example, the marketing team will come up with a concept for a new range and it's my job in research and development to bring that idea to life. Then we'll make samples and test them on consumers."},{"s":135.29,"e":143.87,"t":"After that, we'll speak to the engineers in manufacturing and also the people in charge of packaging, which, believe it or not, is an essential early stage."},{"s":144.31,"e":147.71,"t":"There's no point in creating something that can't be wrapped up and sold."},{"s":148.18,"e":154.3,"t":"Liquid chocolate is a good example. It's delicious but difficult to preserve in that state for sale."},{"s":155.77,"e":161.37,"t":"We also rely heavily on advice from our legal team about the claims we make for our chocolate in our advertising."},{"s":161.85,"e":169.18,"t":"We need to be aware whether we're making something that's not suitable for vegetarians, say, but we haven't stated this in our labelling.","uz":"Vegetarianlar uchun mos bo'lmagan narsa qilayotgan bo'lsak-u, buni yorliqda ko'rsatmagan bo'lsak — buni bilishimiz kerak."},{"s":170.42,"e":172.83,"t":"So what qualities are required in my job?"},{"s":173.3,"e":180.89,"t":"Well, a curiosity about how things work and why. But above and beyond all else, you need initiative and lots of it.","uz":"Narsalar qanday va nima uchun ishlashiga qiziqish. Lekin hammasidan muhimi — tashabbuskorlik, va ko'p."},{"s":181.4,"e":186.59,"t":"There'll be times when no one's giving you specific instructions and you need to get on by yourself."},{"s":187.51,"e":189.57,"t":"Of course, you need to love chocolate."}]},{"n":27,"ins":2,"title":"Protecting the seas from pollution","dur":492.0,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The organisation Sarah works for is called Water Response."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah was surprised to learn that seabirds have been known to eat light {1} on occasions."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah says that plastic can be compared to a {2} because of the way it absorbs dangerous substances."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah learned that the toxins in plastic harm the {3} system of many creatures."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah explains how the breakdown of plastic items into small particles is caused by wave action and the effects of the sun."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah says that most plastic in the sea has its origin in {4} sources."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah gives the example of lemon {5} as something to use instead of household detergents."},{"k":"p","t":"Sarah strongly advises car owners to prevent oil {6} from their vehicles."}],"items":[{"a":["bulbs"],"ps":78.9,"en":88.35,"si":7,"ev":"We rescue birds that have consumed everything from plastic bags to balloons and even light bulbs on occasion, would you believe?","hl":"bulbs","uz":"Plastik paketlardan tortib sharlargacha, hatto ba'zan lampochkalarni yutgan qushlarni qutqaramiz — ishonasizmi?","why":"\"Even light bulbs … would you believe\" — ajablanish. Javob: bulbs."},{"a":["sponge"],"ps":109.27,"en":116.06,"si":11,"ev":"This is because plastics draw in a high concentration of damaging poisons, acting like a sort of chemical sponge.","hl":"sponge","uz":"Chunki plastik zararli zaharlarning yuqori konsentratsiyasini o'ziga tortadi va o'ziga xos kimyoviy shimgichdek ishlaydi.","why":"\"Acting like a sort of chemical sponge\" — javob: sponge."},{"a":["reproductive"],"ps":120.18,"en":129.92,"si":13,"ev":"These chemicals affect not only a seabird's digestive system, which is to be expected, but what was news to me was that they also damage its reproductive system.","hl":"reproductive","uz":"Bu kimyoviy moddalar dengiz qushining nafaqat ovqat hazm qilish tizimiga ta'sir qiladi — bu kutilgan, — balki men uchun yangilik shu bo'ldiki, ular ko'payish tizimiga ham zarar yetkazadi.","why":"\"What was news to me\" = \"learned\" — reproductive. Digestive — kutilgan; immune — oldindan bilardi, tuzoq."},{"a":["land"],"ps":178.74,"en":189.82,"si":19,"ev":"The majority of this gets there from land sources, although marine sources are actually responsible for dumping as much as 3.5 million tons.","hl":"land","uz":"Bu plastikning ko'p qismi quruqlikdagi manbalardan keladi, dengiz manbalari esa yiliga 3,5 million tonnagacha tashlaydi.","why":"\"The majority … from land sources\" — javob: land. Marine — ozroq qismi, tuzoq."},{"a":["juice"],"ps":213.37,"en":220.77,"si":22,"ev":"I encourage others to try simple ingredients such as lemon juice for various household chores instead of their regular cleaning product.","hl":"juice","uz":"Boshqalarni uy yumushlarida odatiy tozalash vositasi o'rniga limon sharbati kabi oddiy narsalarni sinab ko'rishga undayman.","why":"\"Lemon juice … instead of their regular cleaning product\" — javob: juice."},{"a":["leaks","leaking"],"ps":224.44,"en":237.41,"si":24,"ev":"Even things like keeping cars well maintained is essential for ocean protection because oil leaks get washed down drains.","hl":"leaks","uz":"Hatto mashinani yaxshi holatda saqlash ham okeanni himoya qilish uchun muhim, chunki oqib chiqqan moy kanalizatsiyaga yuviladi.","why":"\"Oil leaks\" — javob: leaks. Tashlangan shinalar (tyres) — kamroq ifloslantiradi, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":4.47,"e":14.21,"t":"You'll hear a woman called Sarah Harvey talking about her work with an environmental organization which helps to protect the seas from pollution."},{"s":25.59,"e":30.97,"t":"Welcome to my talk about my work to protect the oceans from the growing problem of pollution."},{"s":31.93,"e":38.88,"t":"I think many people are unaware of just how serious this is and the consequences it has for marine life."},{"s":39.61,"e":48.8,"t":"My interest started when I was working as a volunteer on a beach cleanup project called Cleaner Coasts and was introduced to my current boss."},{"s":49.27,"e":58.33,"t":"He persuaded me to come and work full time for the environmental group he'd just established under the name \"Water Response.\" And I've never regretted my decision."},{"s":59.35,"e":73.53,"t":"I soon found myself face to face with the direct consequences of ocean pollution, as my job involves helping to save seabirds who've swallowed the litter found floating on ocean surfaces, mistaking it for food."},{"s":74.68,"e":78.46,"t":"There is such a wide range of garbage entering the oceans now."},{"s":78.9,"e":88.35,"t":"We rescue birds that have consumed everything from plastic bags to balloons and even light bulbs on occasion, would you believe?","uz":"Plastik paketlardan tortib sharlargacha, hatto ba'zan lampochkalarni yutgan qushlarni qutqaramiz — ishonasizmi?"},{"s":89.05,"e":93.92,"t":"Things like plastic bottle tops are common finds, unfortunately, too."},{"s":94.65,"e":100.06,"t":"Another aspect of my work is removing as much of this debris from the coast as possible."},{"s":101.24,"e":108.57,"t":"Plastics are particularly dangerous for marine creatures as they contain what are known as organic pollutants."},{"s":109.27,"e":116.06,"t":"This is because plastics draw in a high concentration of damaging poisons, acting like a sort of chemical sponge.","uz":"Chunki plastik zararli zaharlarning yuqori konsentratsiyasini o'ziga tortadi va o'ziga xos kimyoviy shimgichdek ishlaydi."},{"s":116.76,"e":119.49,"t":"This is really bad news, you see."},{"s":120.18,"e":129.92,"t":"These chemicals affect not only a seabird's digestive system, which is to be expected, but what was news to me was that they also damage its reproductive system.","uz":"Bu kimyoviy moddalar dengiz qushining nafaqat ovqat hazm qilish tizimiga ta'sir qiladi — bu kutilgan, — balki men uchun yangilik shu bo'ldiki, ular ko'payish tizimiga ham zarar yetkazadi."},{"s":130.46,"e":139.36,"t":"I was well aware that toxins are also notoriously harmful to the immune system, making it harder for many marine species to fight disease."},{"s":140.7,"e":154.62,"t":"Another problem with plastic is its durability. It doesn't go away like natural materials do, but just goes from being, say, a floating bottle to tiny plastic particles, attractive to marine creatures."},{"s":155.32,"e":161.37,"t":"This results from the action of sunlight, but wave action also plays a part in the fragmentation process."},{"s":162.01,"e":168.99,"t":"Unfortunately, ocean pollution is increasing, despite various international conventions set up to control it."},{"s":169.98,"e":178.05,"t":"Around 100 million tons of plastic are produced annually, of which a shocking 10 million tons end up in the sea."},{"s":178.74,"e":189.82,"t":"The majority of this gets there from land sources, although marine sources are actually responsible for dumping as much as 3.5 million tons.","uz":"Bu plastikning ko'p qismi quruqlikdagi manbalardan keladi, dengiz manbalari esa yiliga 3,5 million tonnagacha tashlaydi."},{"s":191.61,"e":198.56,"t":"As well as removing debris and caring for marine animals, I'm also involved in raising public awareness of the problem."},{"s":199.35,"e":212.38,"t":"I help run educational projects teaching people how to make small changes in their daily lives, like avoiding chemical-based detergents which can get into waterways and eventually find their way into the sea."},{"s":213.37,"e":220.77,"t":"I encourage others to try simple ingredients such as lemon juice for various household chores instead of their regular cleaning product.","uz":"Boshqalarni uy yumushlarida odatiy tozalash vositasi o'rniga limon sharbati kabi oddiy narsalarni sinab ko'rishga undayman."},{"s":221.53,"e":223.58,"t":"This can be remarkably effective."},{"s":224.44,"e":237.41,"t":"Even things like keeping cars well maintained is essential for ocean protection because oil leaks get washed down drains and end up causing more pollution than the car tires you see abandoned on beaches."},{"s":238.2,"e":240.61,"t":"Irresponsible though tire dumping is"},{"s":241.08,"e":244.77,"t":"We've at least got a chance of stopping the tires from getting into the sea."},{"s":246.3,"e":247.61,"t":"I want to show you a video"}]},{"n":28,"ins":2,"title":"Robots like termites","dur":444.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Jim says termites differ from bees in that a queen is not responsible for organising their building work."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim uses the word {1} to refer to the group of robots he's created to function as independent units."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim observed termites depositing partially consumed {2} in shared habitats, which activated a response from other termites."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim states that the robots receive {3} to help them correct any errors they make."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim got a single robot to finish the construction of a {4} when publicly demonstrating how simple structure building is performed."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim predicts that his robots will soon be able to move sandbags into position to help people cope with the threat of floods."},{"k":"p","t":"Jim compares both termites and his robots to brain cells, in that they all create a superior form of {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"A group of Turkish researchers has observed Jim's work in the hope of coming up with a {6} they can learn from."}],"items":[{"a":["colony"],"ps":60.89,"en":66.81,"si":7,"ev":"So we decided to make and program what I like to call a colony of robots.","hl":"colony","uz":"Shuning uchun men \"robotlar koloniyasi\" deb ataydigan narsani yasab, dasturlashga qaror qildik.","why":"\"What I like to call a colony of robots\" — javob: colony."},{"a":["wood"],"ps":96.22,"en":103.9,"si":13,"ev":"One deposits some soil, for example, or half-eaten wood. Another one comes along later, and on seeing this, a reaction is triggered.","hl":"wood","uz":"Masalan, biri ozgina tuproq yoki yarim yeyilgan yog'och qoldiradi. Keyinroq boshqasi kelib, buni ko'rib, reaksiya qiladi.","why":"\"Half-eaten wood\" → \"partially consumed wood\". Javob: wood. \"Soil\" — yeyilmaydi, gapga mos emas."},{"a":["feedback"],"ps":116.18,"en":125.6,"si":16,"ev":"Rather than trying to prevent those errors, we give them enough feedback to help with the recognition and correction process, so they try again until they get it right.","hl":"feedback","uz":"Xatolarning oldini olish o'rniga, ularni tanib, tuzatishga yordam beradigan yetarli qayta aloqa (feedback) beramiz.","why":"\"We give them enough feedback\" — javob: feedback."},{"a":["staircase"],"ps":136.79,"en":143.2,"si":19,"ev":"It had to try to complete the structure I asked it to, in this case a staircase, and there was a block missing at the top.","hl":"staircase","uz":"U men so'ragan inshootni — bu holda zinapoyani — tugatishi kerak edi, tepasida bitta blok yetishmasdi.","why":"\"In this case a staircase\" — javob: staircase."},{"a":["intelligence"],"ps":179.51,"en":188.89,"si":23,"ev":"In a sense, termites are like cells in your brain, all acting independently, but interacting with each other and out of that comes a higher intelligence.","hl":"intelligence","uz":"Qaysidir ma'noda termitlar miyangizdagi hujayralarga o'xshaydi: hammasi mustaqil harakat qiladi, lekin bir-biri bilan o'zaro ta'sirlashadi va natijada yuksakroq aql paydo bo'ladi.","why":"\"A higher intelligence\" → \"a superior form of intelligence\". Javob: intelligence."},{"a":["(mathematical) model"],"ps":201.69,"en":221.95,"si":25,"ev":"A Turkish group has been working alongside us to see if the way the robots and termites operate can actually be captured in a mathematical model.","hl":"model","uz":"Turk guruhi biz bilan birga robotlar va termitlar ishlash usulini matematik modelda ifodalash mumkinmi, shuni o'rganmoqda.","why":"\"A mathematical model\" — javob: (mathematical) model."}],"segs":[{"s":3.77,"e":13.09,"t":"You will hear a scientist called Jim Willer giving a talk about some robots he has created and how they function like insects called termites."},{"s":22.65,"e":23.2,"t":"I'm Jim"},{"s":23.77,"e":31.29,"t":"And together with colleagues, I've been attempting to create a group of robots that build things in the same impressive way that termites do."},{"s":32.15,"e":37.92,"t":"termites are like large ants and build amazingly complex structures called mounds to live in."},{"s":38.71,"e":43.26,"t":"Unlike bees, termites don't receive instructions from their queen about what to do."},{"s":43.7,"e":51.07,"t":"In fact, a single worker doesn't know what the other termites are doing or what the current overall state of the mound looks like."},{"s":51.8,"e":60.13,"t":"This tells us that large numbers of units working independently can, paradoxically, build complicated large-scale things together."},{"s":60.89,"e":66.81,"t":"So we decided to make and program what I like to call a colony of robots.","uz":"Shuning uchun men \"robotlar koloniyasi\" deb ataydigan narsani yasab, dasturlashga qaror qildik."},{"s":67.29,"e":77.82,"t":"Now, by giving the robots a picture of what we want them to build, and it doesn't matter how many of them there are or which robot does what, they do indeed end up building what they're asked for."},{"s":78.87,"e":82.24,"t":"The robots and termites both have very restricted sensing."},{"s":82.74,"e":86.3,"t":"A single unit can only tell what's going on right around itself."},{"s":86.87,"e":88.25,"t":"It's the same with communicating."},{"s":88.82,"e":95.65,"t":"Rather than communicating with one another directly, termites make alterations to their shared environment and others respond."},{"s":96.22,"e":103.9,"t":"One deposits some soil, for example, or half-eaten wood. Another one comes along later, and on seeing this, a reaction is triggered.","uz":"Masalan, biri ozgina tuproq yoki yarim yeyilgan yog'och qoldiradi. Keyinroq boshqasi kelib, buni ko'rib, reaksiya qiladi."},{"s":104.57,"e":108.22,"t":"We observed this and devised a similar system with the robots."},{"s":109.14,"e":115.49,"t":"Like termites, the robots often make errors. For example, trying to pick up a brick and failing."},{"s":116.18,"e":125.6,"t":"Rather than trying to prevent those errors, we give them enough feedback to help with the recognition and correction process, so they try again until they get it right.","uz":"Xatolarning oldini olish o'rniga, ularni tanib, tuzatishga yordam beradigan yetarli qayta aloqa (feedback) beramiz."},{"s":126.1,"e":130.14,"t":"so they keep patrolling the structure, fixing only what needs fixing."},{"s":131.1,"e":136.19,"t":"I've demonstrated this in action several times in public presentations with one of our robots."},{"s":136.79,"e":143.2,"t":"It had to try to complete the structure I asked it to, in this case a staircase, and there was a block missing at the top.","uz":"U men so'ragan inshootni — bu holda zinapoyani — tugatishi kerak edi, tepasida bitta blok yetishmasdi."},{"s":143.8,"e":152.06,"t":"so it had to try and pick up building material from the loading area and walk up the structure until it discovered exactly what needed attention."},{"s":153.14,"e":161.53,"t":"In the long term, one day robots like this could build for us in inaccessible or dangerous settings, such as underwater or on Mars."},{"s":162.14,"e":178.46,"t":"In the shorter term, the same principle applies. So, for instance, if you wanted to position sandbags to protect against rising floodwater, or build in difficult Antarctic surroundings, you can imagine how hardware and approaches very much like this could be used."},{"s":179.51,"e":188.89,"t":"In a sense, termites are like cells in your brain, all acting independently, but interacting with each other and out of that comes a higher intelligence.","uz":"Qaysidir ma'noda termitlar miyangizdagi hujayralarga o'xshaydi: hammasi mustaqil harakat qiladi, lekin bir-biri bilan o'zaro ta'sirlashadi va natijada yuksakroq aql paydo bo'ladi."},{"s":189.62,"e":200.99,"t":"And in a similar kind of way, our robots are individuals, moving around independently with no central coordination and together, hopefully, producing complicated structures."},{"s":201.69,"e":221.95,"t":"One spin-off piece of research has already been put into place. A Turkish group has been working alongside us to see if the way the robots and termites operate can actually be captured in a mathematical model to be used in future projects. It's a fascinating idea, and I believe there are similar studies with flocks of birds and shoals of fish."},{"s":223.13,"e":223.55,"t":"mean move"}]},{"n":29,"ins":2,"title":"Vanilla","dur":369.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Susie says that, despite its cost, vanilla is the world's most popular spice."},{"k":"p","t":"The vanilla plant is originally from Mexico, where it depends on a local {1} for its existence."},{"k":"p","t":"Susie says the term green {2} is used to talk about vanilla plants on the island."},{"k":"p","t":"Recently the vanilla harvest has been affected by {3} and this impacts on the price."},{"k":"p","t":"These days the vanilla plants are covered by netting for protection."},{"k":"p","t":"Sometimes there are {4} in the vanilla seed pods to show which farm they come from."},{"k":"p","t":"The vanilla pods are sun-dried and then {5} briefly before being packed in boxes."},{"k":"p","t":"The boxes used to store the pods are wrapped in {6} to keep the heat in."}],"items":[{"a":["insect"],"ps":58.14,"en":67.13,"si":4,"ev":"It originated in Mexico, where there's a particular insect which can pollinate the plant.","hl":"insect","uz":"U Meksikadan kelib chiqqan, u yerda o'simlikni changlata oladigan maxsus hasharot bor.","why":"\"A particular insect which can pollinate the plant\" — javob: insect."},{"a":["gold"],"ps":72.22,"en":78.85,"si":6,"ev":"I heard local people referring to the plants as green gold.","hl":"gold","uz":"Mahalliy aholining o'simliklarni \"yashil oltin\" deb atashini eshitdim.","why":"\"Green gold\" — javob: gold."},{"a":["storms"],"ps":88.89,"en":99.87,"si":8,"ev":"There's been a problem with supplying customers recently as storms have had a detrimental effect on the harvest.","hl":"storms","uz":"Yaqinda bo'ronlar hosilga zarar yetkazgani uchun mijozlarni ta'minlashda muammo bo'ldi.","why":"\"Storms … detrimental effect on the harvest\" — javob: storms. Kasalliklar (diseases) — yo'q qilingan, tuzoq."},{"a":["holes"],"ps":132.82,"en":138.94,"si":12,"ev":"Pickers often make small holes at one end of the pods as a means of identifying their farm or plantation.","hl":"holes","uz":"Teruvchilar ko'pincha qo'zoqlarning bir uchida kichik teshiklar ochishadi — fermasini belgilash uchun.","why":"\"Small holes … identifying their farm\" — javob: holes. \"Black marks\" — yaroqsiz qo'zoqlar belgisi, tuzoq."},{"a":["boiled"],"ps":144.15,"en":155.61,"si":14,"ev":"Healthy-looking pods are dried outside in the sun. Then they are boiled for about three minutes.","hl":"boiled","uz":"Sog'lom qo'zoqlar tashqarida quyoshda quritiladi. Keyin taxminan uch daqiqa qaynatiladi.","why":"Quritilgandan keyin \"boiled for about three minutes\" — javob: boiled."},{"a":["blankets"],"ps":159.32,"en":164.13,"si":16,"ev":"Then the pods are put in boxes which have blankets wrapped round them to retain the heat.","hl":"blankets","uz":"Keyin qo'zoqlar issiqlikni saqlash uchun adyolga o'ralgan qutilarga solinadi.","why":"\"Blankets wrapped round them to retain the heat\" — javob: blankets. Polistirol — sinab ko'rilgan, yaramagan."}],"segs":[{"s":3.7,"e":14.11,"t":"You'll hear a radio report by the journalist Susie Stubbs, who's been to the tropical island of Reunion, to find out about the flavouring called vanilla."},{"s":22.65,"e":31.61,"t":"This week's edition of World Farming comes from the island of Reunion, off the south-east coast of Africa, where there are vanilla plantations as far as the eye can see."},{"s":32.57,"e":39.68,"t":"Vanilla is an exotic spice which is very nearly the most expensive in the world, second only to saffron and certainly the most popular."},{"s":40.5,"e":57.34,"t":"We're used to tasting it in sweet dishes, but people are now beginning to use it in savoury ones as well. In fact, there's a restaurant near where I live in London called Fresh Tastes where chef Antonio Meltini adds vanilla to almost all the dishes and quite delicious they are too."},{"s":58.14,"e":67.13,"t":"These days, vanilla is grown in the Caribbean, East Asia and Africa, but it originated in Mexico, where there's a particular insect which can pollinate the plant."},{"s":67.9,"e":71.42,"t":"This morning I visited a vanilla plantation here on Reunion."},{"s":72.22,"e":78.85,"t":"I heard local people referring to the plants as green gold, which isn't surprising when you think of all the money they represent."},{"s":79.61,"e":88.16,"t":"Good vanilla is always in great demand and the price at the moment is between £150 and £180 a kilo for top quality."},{"s":88.89,"e":99.87,"t":"In fact there's been a problem with supplying customers recently as storms have had a detrimental effect on the harvest. All the more unfortunate, now the various diseases which used to decimate the crop have been eradicated."},{"s":101.21,"e":115.42,"t":"I'm told that some of the earlier producers had their vanilla growing in the shelter of trees. But on modern plantations the plants are grown under nets which can easily be removed when it's time to harvest the vanilla seed pods which are the valuable part of the plant."},{"s":116.25,"e":125.57,"t":"After three or four years of growth, the first flowers appear, but they only bloom for a day. They need to be pollinated then, either naturally or artificially."},{"s":126.42,"e":131.81,"t":"Later on, the pods, they're a kind of shell or case which holds the seeds, are harvested."},{"s":132.82,"e":138.94,"t":"Pickers often make small holes at one end of the pods as a means of identifying their farm or plantation.","uz":"Teruvchilar ko'pincha qo'zoqlarning bir uchida kichik teshiklar ochishadi — fermasini belgilash uchun."},{"s":139.8,"e":143.58,"t":"Pods with black marks on them will probably be rejected at this stage."},{"s":144.15,"e":155.61,"t":"Healthy-looking pods are dried outside in the sun. Then they are boiled for about three minutes, which surprised me rather. But if this isn't done, the pods will open and all the seeds will be lost."},{"s":156.25,"e":158.65,"t":"So it's a very important part of the process."},{"s":159.32,"e":164.13,"t":"Then the pods are put in boxes which have blankets wrapped round them to retain the heat.","uz":"Keyin qo'zoqlar issiqlikni saqlash uchun adyolga o'ralgan qutilarga solinadi."},{"s":164.63,"e":169.79,"t":"Materials like polystyrene have been experimented with and found unsatisfactory apparently."},{"s":170.68,"e":177.37,"t":"Finally, when the pods have dried out enough, they're put into new boxes to allow their characteristic aroma to develop."},{"s":178.58,"e":180.8,"t":"I was allowed to open up one of these boxes."},{"s":181.27,"e":183.2,"t":"They're really just like treasure chests."},{"s":183.74,"e":185.05,"t":"Fragrance is one..."}]},{"n":30,"ins":2,"title":"Inventing the microwave oven","dur":392.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The invention of the microwave oven began when a chocolate peanut bar melted in Percy Spencer's pocket."},{"k":"p","t":"Spencer had previously invented a method for {1} the tubes used in radar equipment."},{"k":"p","t":"Spencer's first experiment involved putting {2} near to some radar equipment."},{"k":"p","t":"In his next experiment, an egg was put into a kettle and it {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"The first microwave oven was set up in {4} in Boston in 1946."},{"k":"p","t":"The first microwave oven got its name as a result of {5} at the company."},{"k":"p","t":"One problem with the first microwave oven was that meat did not change colour in it."},{"k":"p","t":"When a microwave oven that could be placed on top of a {6} was produced, sales began to rise."}],"items":[{"a":["mass-producing"],"ps":59.38,"en":71.93,"si":9,"ev":"But it wasn't until Spencer … worked out a way of mass producing the tubes that radar made a real difference in the war.","hl":"mass producing","uz":"Faqat Spenser bu trubkalarni ommaviy ishlab chiqarish usulini topgandan keyingina radar urushda haqiqiy farq yaratdi.","why":"\"Mass producing the tubes\" — javob: mass-producing."},{"a":["popcorn"],"ps":73.43,"en":78.59,"si":10,"ev":"The day after the chocolate incident, Spencer sent a boy out to buy some popcorn.","hl":"popcorn","uz":"\"Shokolad voqeasi\"dan ertasi kuni Spenser bir bolani makkajo'xori (popkorn) olib kelishga yubordi.","why":"Birinchi tajriba — popkornni magnetron trubkasi yoniga qo'yish. Javob: popcorn. Shokolad — tasodifiy voqea, tajriba emas."},{"a":["exploded"],"ps":96.44,"en":102.46,"si":15,"ev":"One unlucky director bent down to take a closer look just at the moment the egg exploded.","hl":"exploded","uz":"Bir omadsiz direktor yaqinroq qarash uchun engashgan paytda tuxum portlab ketdi.","why":"\"The egg exploded\" — javob: exploded."},{"a":["restaurant"],"ps":120.12,"en":130.81,"si":18,"ev":"The first microwave, five foot six inches tall and weighing 750 pounds, was installed in a Boston restaurant for testing in 1946.","hl":"restaurant","uz":"Balandligi besh fut olti dyuym, og'irligi 750 funt bo'lgan birinchi mikroto'lqinli pech 1946 yilda Boston restoranida sinov uchun o'rnatildi.","why":"\"Installed in a Boston restaurant\" — javob: restaurant."},{"a":["competition"],"ps":136.66,"en":142.4,"si":20,"ev":"It was named \"Radar Range\" following a competition among Raytheon employees.","hl":"competition","uz":"U Raytheon xodimlari o'rtasidagi tanlovdan so'ng \"Radar Range\" deb nomlandi.","why":"\"Following a competition among Raytheon employees\" — javob: competition."},{"a":["counter"],"ps":170.94,"en":178.69,"si":26,"ev":"Not until the 1960s, when the first countertop microwave was produced, did sales at last begin to take off.","hl":"counter","uz":"Faqat 1960-yillarda, birinchi stol ustiga qo'yiladigan mikroto'lqinli pech chiqqandagina savdo nihoyat o'sa boshladi.","why":"\"Countertop\" — \"counter\" (oshxona stoli) ustiga qo'yiladigan. Javob: counter."}],"segs":[{"s":3.19,"e":7.81,"t":"You'll hear part of a talk about the invention of the microwave oven."},{"s":22.94,"e":25.5,"t":"One day in spring 1945"},{"s":26.01,"e":31.33,"t":"Physics engineer Percy Spencer was walking past a switched on piece of radar equipment"},{"s":31.8,"e":33.89,"t":"when he felt something sticky in his pocket."},{"s":34.65,"e":38.88,"t":"It turned out to be a chocolate peanut bar he had been saving for his coffee break."},{"s":39.8,"e":44.06,"t":"Intrigued, he set out to discover why it had suddenly melted."},{"s":44.95,"e":47.81,"t":"and the equipment concerned was a magnetron tube."},{"s":48.44,"e":49.66,"t":"Part of a radar set."},{"s":50.52,"e":58.59,"t":"Radar had been invented by the British in World War II to detect enemy aircraft at night using short waves or microwaves."},{"s":59.38,"e":71.93,"t":"But it wasn't until Spencer … worked out a way of mass producing the tubes that radar made a real difference in the war.","uz":"Faqat Spenser bu trubkalarni ommaviy ishlab chiqarish usulini topgandan keyingina radar urushda haqiqiy farq yaratdi."},{"s":73.43,"e":78.59,"t":"The day after the chocolate incident, Spencer sent a boy out to buy some popcorn.","uz":"\"Shokolad voqeasi\"dan ertasi kuni Spenser bir bolani makkajo'xori (popkorn) olib kelishga yubordi."},{"s":79.7,"e":82.46,"t":"Place the kernels near the magnetron tube."},{"s":83.22,"e":86.17,"t":"They immediately started popping round the lab."},{"s":87.16,"e":91.36,"t":"His next experiment was with an egg, which he put inside a kettle."},{"s":92.28,"e":95.68,"t":"Curious colleagues gathered round to watch it quaking."},{"s":96.44,"e":102.46,"t":"One unlucky director bent down to take a closer look just at the moment the egg exploded.","uz":"Bir omadsiz direktor yaqinroq qarash uchun engashgan paytda tuxum portlab ketdi."},{"s":103.83,"e":115.52,"t":"Spencer came to realize that the microwaves were heating the food by agitating its water and fat molecules, which meant that the inside cooked just as fast as the outside."},{"s":116.57,"e":119.23,"t":"Raytheon engineers soon refined the idea."},{"s":120.12,"e":130.81,"t":"The first microwave, five foot six inches tall and weighing 750 pounds, was installed in a Boston restaurant for testing in 1946.","uz":"Balandligi besh fut olti dyuym, og'irligi 750 funt bo'lgan birinchi mikroto'lqinli pech 1946 yilda Boston restoranida sinov uchun o'rnatildi."},{"s":132.22,"e":136.0,"t":"first commercial microwave hit the market the following year."},{"s":136.66,"e":142.4,"t":"It was named \"Radar Range\" following a competition among Raytheon employees.","uz":"U Raytheon xodimlari o'rtasidagi tanlovdan so'ng \"Radar Range\" deb nomlandi."},{"s":143.45,"e":147.45,"t":"Spencer and his colleagues confidently expected a cooking revolution."},{"s":148.54,"e":154.14,"t":"The machine was primitive, enormous, and at $3,000, too expensive."},{"s":155.0,"e":158.37,"t":"All too soon, chefs realized its main drawback."},{"s":159.13,"e":163.65,"t":"Meat refused to brown and food emerged limp and flabby."},{"s":164.5,"e":169.82,"t":"The company chairman's chef quit in disgust because he was told to use the radar range."},{"s":170.94,"e":178.69,"t":"Not until the 1960s, when the first countertop microwave was produced, did sales at last begin to take off.","uz":"Faqat 1960-yillarda, birinchi stol ustiga qo'yiladigan mikroto'lqinli pech chiqqandagina savdo nihoyat o'sa boshladi."},{"s":179.8,"e":185.73,"t":"The first model in 1967 was 100 volts and cost just under $500."},{"s":186.62,"e":191.74,"t":"By 1975, sales of microwaves overtook gas cookers in the U.S."},{"s":192.38,"e":198.37,"t":"Now, nearly 90% of households in Britain and the US use a microwave oven."}]},{"n":31,"ins":2,"title":"The Grand Union Canal","dur":463.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The canals were built despite the fact that there was no public finance and very little technology."},{"k":"p","t":"From 1790 to 1929, there were many canals that were {1} with each other but which were not uniform in size."},{"k":"p","t":"The new union of canals provided a {2} link between major industrial cities."},{"k":"p","t":"There are plenty of natural {3} for a variety of wildlife on and around the canals."},{"k":"p","t":"Walkers can go to the nearest waterway office to get information on circular walks so they can start and end at the same place."},{"k":"p","t":"Anglers can fish in the canals and {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"If you want to go fishing, you must buy a {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The waterways authority request that people are {6} towards the canal users."}],"items":[{"a":["competing"],"ps":41.53,"en":57.5,"si":6,"ev":"From 1790 to 1929, a large number of competing independently owned canals were constructed. their waterways not uniform in size, and often unable to carry the larger vessels from other sections.","hl":"competing","uz":"1790–1929 yillarda mustaqil egalarga tegishli, bir-biri bilan raqobatlashuvchi ko'plab kanallar qurildi. Ularning suv yo'llari bir xil o'lchamda emasdi.","why":"\"Competing independently owned canals\" → \"competing with each other\". Javob: competing."},{"a":["continuous"],"ps":58.78,"en":72.99,"si":7,"ev":"Through a series of takeovers, the various companies eventually amalgamated and created a union of canals which could form a continuous link between Birmingham, London and other important industrial areas.","hl":"continuous","uz":"Bir qator qo'shib olishlar natijasida kompaniyalar birlashdi va Birmingem, London va boshqa sanoat hududlarini uzluksiz bog'laydigan kanallar ittifoqini yaratdi.","why":"\"A continuous link\" — javob: continuous."},{"a":["habitats"],"ps":108.09,"en":115.42,"si":13,"ev":"Natural habitats are numerous as a result of cleaner waters and the declining industrial traffic.","hl":"habitats","uz":"Toza suv va sanoat transportining kamayishi tufayli tabiiy yashash joylari ko'p.","why":"\"Natural habitats are numerous\" → \"plenty of natural habitats\". Javob: habitats."},{"a":["reservoirs"],"ps":169.53,"en":177.98,"si":20,"ev":"We are keen to encourage both experienced and inexperienced anglers onto the well-stocked canal network and reservoirs.","hl":"reservoirs","uz":"Tajribali va tajribasiz baliqchilarni baliqqa boy kanal tarmog'i va suv omborlariga taklif qilamiz.","why":"\"Canal network and reservoirs\" — javob: reservoirs."},{"a":["licenses","licences"],"ps":194.04,"en":199.52,"si":23,"ev":"Rod licenses are obligatory and can be obtained from your local post office.","hl":"licenses","uz":"Qarmoq litsenziyasi majburiy, uni mahalliy pochta bo'limidan olish mumkin.","why":"\"Rod licences are obligatory\" → \"must buy a licence\". Javob: licences."},{"a":["considerate"],"ps":216.25,"en":223.07,"si":27,"ev":"We can all share the delights of the canal system, so please be considerate to other users.","hl":"considerate","uz":"Kanal tizimining zavqini hammamiz baham ko'rishimiz mumkin, shuning uchun boshqalarga nisbatan e'tiborli bo'ling.","why":"\"Please be considerate to other users\" — javob: considerate."}],"segs":[{"s":2.52,"e":6.94,"t":"You will hear a representative from British waterways called John Sampson."},{"s":7.51,"e":9.69,"t":"talking about a canal network in England."},{"s":13.37,"e":21.57,"t":"The extensive network which makes up the Grand Union Canal is without doubt a truly extraordinary piece of engineering."},{"s":22.26,"e":32.06,"t":"Begun in the late 18th century, the majority of the canal system was built without the benefits of modern technology or public finance."},{"s":33.11,"e":35.42,"t":"It is a truly grand canal."},{"s":36.38,"e":40.22,"t":"But why is it known as the Grand Union Canal?"},{"s":41.53,"e":57.5,"t":"From 1790 to 1929, a large number of competing independently owned canals were constructed. their waterways not uniform in size, and often unable to carry the larger vessels from other sections.","uz":"1790–1929 yillarda mustaqil egalarga tegishli, bir-biri bilan raqobatlashuvchi ko'plab kanallar qurildi. Ularning suv yo'llari bir xil o'lchamda emasdi."},{"s":58.78,"e":72.99,"t":"Through a series of takeovers, the various companies eventually amalgamated and created a union of canals which could form a continuous link between Birmingham, London and other important industrial areas.","uz":"Bir qator qo'shib olishlar natijasida kompaniyalar birlashdi va Birmingem, London va boshqa sanoat hududlarini uzluksiz bog'laydigan kanallar ittifoqini yaratdi."},{"s":74.07,"e":78.85,"t":"Along every stretch of canal, you will find this heritage retained."},{"s":79.64,"e":85.95,"t":"Traditionally painted narrow boats are still guided by original mileposts."},{"s":86.42,"e":95.2,"t":"while working examples of mills, pump houses, ancient locks and keeper's cottages are a common sight on any journey."},{"s":96.44,"e":102.27,"t":"The Grand Union Canal boasts an extraordinary variety of wildlife."},{"s":103.06,"e":107.36,"t":"feeding herons and hunting owls to rare water voles."},{"s":108.09,"e":115.42,"t":"Natural habitats are numerous as a result of cleaner waters and the declining industrial traffic.","uz":"Toza suv va sanoat transportining kamayishi tufayli tabiiy yashash joylari ko'p."},{"s":116.18,"e":127.97,"t":"The hedgerows and canal banks have proved an ideal location for a number of diverse species to thrive in this tranquil and often unique environment."},{"s":129.4,"e":137.73,"t":"car-free and carefree way to appreciate the beauty of the canal and at your own pace is by walking."},{"s":138.58,"e":145.15,"t":"Whether you are looking for organized or independent two-path walks, we can help you with your planning."},{"s":145.62,"e":156.29,"t":"Each waterway office can supply information on circular walks, waterside pubs, plus suggested routes and specific points of interest."},{"s":156.79,"e":161.85,"t":"There are many stations within easy reach of the Grand Union Canal."},{"s":162.78,"e":168.19,"t":"Why not try a one-way walk returning to your starting point by train?"},{"s":169.53,"e":177.98,"t":"We are keen to encourage both experienced and inexperienced anglers onto the well-stocked canal network and reservoirs.","uz":"Tajribali va tajribasiz baliqchilarni baliqqa boy kanal tarmog'i va suv omborlariga taklif qilamiz."},{"s":178.74,"e":185.09,"t":"We lease certain sections to established clubs who welcome non-members for a small daily fee."},{"s":185.82,"e":193.05,"t":"Before you fish, check with your local British Waterways Office for information on access and availability."},{"s":194.04,"e":199.52,"t":"Rod licenses are obligatory and can be obtained from your local post office.","uz":"Qarmoq litsenziyasi majburiy, uni mahalliy pochta bo'limidan olish mumkin."},{"s":200.28,"e":204.8,"t":"Last but not least, the towpaths are wonderful for cycling."},{"s":205.72,"e":209.95,"t":"free of traffic, free of fumes and free of hills."},{"s":210.39,"e":215.61,"t":"miles of accessible towpaths through some of England's finest countryside."},{"s":216.25,"e":223.07,"t":"We can all share the delights of the canal system, so please be considerate to other users.","uz":"Kanal tizimining zavqini hammamiz baham ko'rishimiz mumkin, shuning uchun boshqalarga nisbatan e'tiborli bo'ling."},{"s":223.83,"e":230.97,"t":"Surfaces vary from stony pathways to smooth asphalt, but that's all part of the enjoyment."}]},{"n":32,"ins":2,"title":"The probation worker","dur":216.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Georgia grew up on a council estate."},{"k":"p","t":"Georgia didn't think she had enough {1} for a career in probation work."},{"k":"p","t":"While studying for her degree, Georgia worked as a {2} in three different places."},{"k":"p","t":"Being able to work out which {3} is the most urgent is an important skill."},{"k":"p","t":"While working face to face with an offender, you both have emotional {4} to deal with."},{"k":"p","t":"Georgia works in the prison, in court and her office."},{"k":"p","t":"The worst part of Georgia's job is dealing with domestic {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Georgia has to work with the courts to decide on a fair {6} for each offender."}],"items":[{"a":["qualifications"],"ps":20.66,"en":26.33,"si":2,"ev":"I was interested in probation work, but having left school with little in the way of qualifications, I never thought I could do it.","hl":"qualifications","uz":"Probatsiya ishiga qiziqardim, lekin maktabni deyarli malakasiz tugatganim uchun buni uddalay olaman deb o'ylamagandim.","why":"\"Little in the way of qualifications\" → \"not enough qualifications\". Javob: qualifications."},{"a":["volunteer"],"ps":33.02,"en":42.17,"si":5,"ev":"At the same time I was a volunteer for the St John's Ambulance Service, the Probation Service and at a residential children's school.","hl":"volunteer","uz":"Shu bilan birga St John's tez yordam xizmati, Probatsiya xizmati va bolalar maktab-internatida ko'ngilli bo'lib ishladim.","why":"Uchta joyda — volunteer. Armiya — o'qishdan oldin, tuzoq."},{"a":["deadline"],"ps":45.43,"en":56.54,"si":7,"ev":"Time management is the most important skill. Especially the need to prioritise deadlines.","hl":"deadlines","uz":"Vaqtni boshqarish — eng muhim ko'nikma. Ayniqsa muddatlarni muhimligiga qarab tartiblash.","why":"\"Prioritise deadlines\" → \"work out which deadline is the most urgent\". Javob: deadline. (Transkriptdagi \"High management\" — aslida \"Time management\".)"},{"a":["barriers"],"ps":57.02,"en":62.65,"si":8,"ev":"There's a lot of one to one work with offenders and this requires you to work through both your own and their emotional barriers.","hl":"barriers","uz":"Jinoyatchilar bilan yakkama-yakka ishlash ko'p, bu o'zingizning ham, ularning ham hissiy to'siqlaringizni yengishni talab qiladi.","why":"\"Both your own and their emotional barriers\" — javob: barriers."},{"a":["violence"],"ps":76.6,"en":85.44,"si":12,"ev":"The worst thing is … there are times when you have to engage with people that have committed crimes that involve domestic violence.","hl":"violence","uz":"Eng yomoni — ba'zan oilaviy zo'ravonlik bilan bog'liq jinoyat qilgan odamlar bilan ishlashga to'g'ri keladi.","why":"\"The worst thing … domestic violence\" — javob: violence."},{"a":["sentence"],"ps":91.32,"en":96.06,"si":14,"ev":"I liaise with the courts which is basically providing guidance on the best sentences for people to be given.","hl":"sentences","uz":"Men sudlar bilan hamkorlik qilaman — asosan odamlarga qanday jazo berish eng to'g'ri ekani bo'yicha tavsiya beraman.","why":"\"The best sentences for people\" → \"a fair sentence\". Javob: sentence."}],"segs":[{"s":2.62,"e":6.33,"t":"You will hear a woman talking about her job as a probation officer."},{"s":11.1,"e":19.93,"t":"My background is from a family of six children from a council estate where I saw friends drifting and out of crime. I had a desire to help people see that there are choices in life."},{"s":20.66,"e":26.33,"t":"I was interested in probation work, but having left school with little in the way of qualifications, I never thought I could do it.","uz":"Probatsiya ishiga qiziqardim, lekin maktabni deyarli malakasiz tugatganim uchun buni uddalay olaman deb o'ylamagandim."},{"s":26.81,"e":30.21,"t":"It was only after taking an IQ test that I realised I might have a chance."},{"s":30.71,"e":32.57,"t":"After leaving school I joined the army."},{"s":33.02,"e":42.17,"t":"Then I started to study for a degree in health and social care. At the same time I was a volunteer for the St John's Ambulance Service, the Probation Service and at a residential children's school."},{"s":42.68,"e":44.83,"t":"Then I applied to be a trainee probation officer."},{"s":45.43,"e":56.54,"t":"Time management is the most important skill. Especially the need to prioritise deadlines, read and digest information and then write clear reports for the courts. I also have to be able to interact with people from all walks of life."},{"s":57.02,"e":62.65,"t":"There's a lot of one to one work with offenders and this requires you to work through both your own and their emotional barriers.","uz":"Jinoyatchilar bilan yakkama-yakka ishlash ko'p, bu o'zingizning ham, ularning ham hissiy to'siqlaringizni yengishni talab qiladi."},{"s":63.13,"e":64.32,"t":"Every day is different."},{"s":64.76,"e":70.11,"t":"Of a working week, about three days are spent in the office with the remainder split between prison and being in court."},{"s":70.78,"e":76.09,"t":"The best thing is that you get to work with a huge spectrum of people from the homeless to professionals who've made mistakes."},{"s":76.6,"e":85.44,"t":"The worst thing is that the job is generally very pressured and there are times when you have to engage with people that have committed crimes that involve domestic violence. That's really hard to take."},{"s":86.3,"e":90.81,"t":"My role is currently that of case manager where I manage up to 35 offenders at one time."},{"s":91.32,"e":96.06,"t":"I liaise with the courts which is basically providing guidance on the best sentences for people to be given.","uz":"Men sudlar bilan hamkorlik qilaman — asosan odamlarga qanday jazo berish eng to'g'ri ekani bo'yicha tavsiya beraman."},{"s":96.63,"e":99.42,"t":"I also visit prisons where I'm involved in the release process."},{"s":99.99,"e":106.94,"t":"As a next step I'd see myself as a practice manager monitoring a team and ultimately I'd like to be a senior probation officer."}]},{"n":33,"ins":2,"title":"Radio reporter","dur":379.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"While attending university, Sally did a degree in communication studies."},{"k":"p","t":"Having graduated from university, Sally got her first job of a marketing {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Sally uses the word {2} to describe what the first day at a radio station felt like."},{"k":"p","t":"Sally later got an offer to join a {3} scheme from the boss of the Brighton radio station."},{"k":"p","t":"Sally found doing {4} on air during her time in Brighton to be most enjoyable."},{"k":"p","t":"A colleague from Brighton advised Sally to study journalism at evening classes."},{"k":"p","t":"At the national broadcasting company, the majority of Sally's work was on the {5} desk."},{"k":"p","t":"Sally believes {6} to be the main advantage of doing work experience."}],"items":[{"a":["assistant"],"ps":56.38,"en":68.51,"si":6,"ev":"When I graduated, I took the first job I was offered… And I soon realised being a marketing assistant was too far away from this.","hl":"assistant","uz":"Bitirgach, taklif qilingan birinchi ishni oldim… Tez orada marketing yordamchisi bo'lish bunga juda uzoq ekanini angladim.","why":"\"Being a marketing assistant\" — javob: assistant. DJ — faqat orzu, tuzoq."},{"a":["intimidated"],"ps":78.87,"en":93.82,"si":8,"ev":"Although I was intimidated for the first couple of hours, it was actually a very relaxed sort of place.","hl":"intimidated","uz":"Dastlabki bir-ikki soat o'zimni noqulay (qo'rqib) his qilgan bo'lsam ham, aslida u juda erkin joy ekan.","why":"\"Intimidated for the first couple of hours\" — javob: intimidated. \"Relaxed\" — joyning tavsifi, uning his-tuyg'usi emas."},{"a":["trainee"],"ps":97.34,"en":106.72,"si":10,"ev":"He immediately offered me a place on the station's trainee scheme.","hl":"trainee","uz":"U darhol menga stansiyaning stajyorlik dasturidan joy taklif qildi.","why":"\"Trainee scheme\" — javob: trainee."},{"a":["interviews"],"ps":122.68,"en":127.52,"si":14,"ev":"And even once or twice conducted live interviews, I got the biggest buzz of all from that.","hl":"interviews","uz":"Hatto bir-ikki marta jonli intervyu o'tkazdim — eng katta zavqni shundan oldim.","why":"\"The biggest buzz\" = eng zavqli. Javob: interviews. Traffic reports — \"fun\", lekin eng yoqqani emas."},{"a":["news"],"ps":162.04,"en":170.56,"si":19,"ev":"I was taken on to work on the sports desk but soon got transferred to the news desk where I worked out the rest of my placement.","hl":"news","uz":"Sport bo'limiga olingandim, lekin tez orada yangiliklar bo'limiga o'tkazildim va qolgan stajirovkani o'sha yerda o'tadim.","why":"Ko'p vaqti — news desk. Sports va travel — qisqa muddat, tuzoq."},{"a":["flexibility"],"ps":180.54,"en":185.5,"si":22,"ev":"If I had to say what the main benefit of work experience was, I'd say it gives you flexibility.","hl":"flexibility","uz":"Ish tajribasining asosiy foydasi nima desangiz, u sizga moslashuvchanlik beradi deyman.","why":"\"The main benefit … flexibility\" — javob: flexibility."}],"segs":[{"s":2.68,"e":5.85,"t":"You'll hear a radio reporter called Sally Nelson."},{"s":6.33,"e":12.09,"t":"telling a group of teenagers about how work experience schemes have helped her in her career."},{"s":22.33,"e":31.2,"t":"Hi, my name's Sally Nelson and I'm a radio reporter specialising in current affairs. I'm here to tell you how useful work experience placements have been in my career."},{"s":31.96,"e":43.1,"t":"Although I'm in my dream job now, at school I lacked ambition and made a poor choice of university course. Some of my colleagues did subjects like media studies which have a direct application to the work."},{"s":43.7,"e":51.33,"t":"Although my subject sounds relevant, it's known as 'communication studies', I think a degree in English and Drama would have been just as useful."},{"s":51.93,"e":55.68,"t":"My course centered on the sociological use of language rather than the media."},{"s":56.38,"e":68.51,"t":"When I graduated, I took the first job I was offered. I'd always been interested in music and clubbing and had considered training as a DJ. And I soon realised being a marketing assistant was too far away from this."},{"s":68.98,"e":78.11,"t":"My friends had more interesting jobs than me. One was even working as a manager for a rock band. So I quit the job and rang another friend who was a radio presenter in Brighton."},{"s":78.87,"e":93.82,"t":"I organised a sit-in on his show for a few days, which was a bit cheeky of me, and although I was intimidated for the first couple of hours, it was actually a very relaxed sort of place, and it gave me exactly the sort of insight I needed to confirm that radio was for me."},{"s":94.78,"e":96.89,"t":"So I approached the boss of the station."},{"s":97.34,"e":106.72,"t":"He immediately offered me a place on the station's trainee scheme. It's a bit like a work experience scheme really and involves spending two days a week working unpaid at the station."},{"s":107.26,"e":109.98,"t":"To fund myself, I did waitressing jobs the rest of the week."},{"s":110.81,"e":114.69,"t":"The station's a small company so the work was varied and very hands-on."},{"s":115.19,"e":122.21,"t":"I got to do traffic reports on air which was fun, background research about musicians which was more interesting than I expected."},{"s":122.68,"e":127.52,"t":"And even once or twice conducted live interviews, I got the biggest buzz of all from that.","uz":"Hatto bir-ikki marta jonli intervyu o'tkazdim — eng katta zavqni shundan oldim."},{"s":128.5,"e":144.83,"t":"In this industry you have to network and that's why work experience, however short the placement, is so important. I met people in Brighton who really opened doors for me. One colleague said technical training would help my job prospects and told me about a journalism course which you can do in the evening."},{"s":145.5,"e":151.23,"t":"At twenty-five I was much older than my fellow students, but I was very focused and it stood me in good stead."},{"s":152.18,"e":159.04,"t":"Thanks to someone I met on that course, I got another work experience placement, this time with a larger national broadcasting company."},{"s":159.51,"e":161.53,"t":"I worked for six months unpaid there."},{"s":162.04,"e":170.56,"t":"I was taken on to work on the sports desk but soon got transferred to the news desk where I worked out the rest of my placement with occasional days on the travel desk."},{"s":171.06,"e":174.56,"t":"Although I was on a steep learning curve, it was fantastic from day one."},{"s":175.58,"e":179.84,"t":"Working for free was exhausting because I had to hold down other jobs to keep myself."},{"s":180.54,"e":185.5,"t":"If I had to say what the main benefit of work experience was, I'd say it gives you flexibility.","uz":"Ish tajribasining asosiy foydasi nima desangiz, u sizga moslashuvchanlik beradi deyman."},{"s":186.01,"e":194.91,"t":"You learn on the job and make mistakes without feeling you're about to get sacked, and that's just as important for your confidence and employability as any number of qualifications."}]},{"n":34,"ins":2,"title":"Videogame designer","dur":366.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Paul says that people tend to think he's a game developer rather than a designer."},{"k":"p","t":"As a part of his education Paul did a course in {1} which significantly helped his career."},{"k":"p","t":"In his first job, Paul was mostly designing book covers."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul worked with what is known as user {2} in his first job."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul mentions a videogame titled {3} City as the one he found most enjoyable to work on."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul uses the word {4} to describe what multiplayers in a game can create for themselves."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul says that getting the {5} level right is one of the most challenging aspects of game design."},{"k":"p","t":"Paul names {6} as the most crucial quality any game designer should have."}],"items":[{"a":["animation"],"ps":61.69,"en":78.3,"si":7,"ev":"I did courses in painting and drawing … as well as one in computer graphics … and one in animation. That was the one which enabled me to build up the key … design skills I use now.","hl":"animation","uz":"Rangtasvir, chizmachilik, kompyuter grafikasi va animatsiya kurslarini o'qidim. Hozir ishlatayotgan asosiy dizayn ko'nikmalarini aynan animatsiya kursi berdi.","why":"\"That was the one which enabled me…\" — animation. Kompyuter grafikasi — faqat qiziqtirgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["interfaces"],"ps":92.18,"en":102.85,"si":10,"ev":"An opening came up … to work on things called user interfaces.","hl":"interfaces","uz":"\"Foydalanuvchi interfeyslari\" deb ataladigan narsalar ustida ishlash uchun bo'sh o'rin chiqdi.","why":"\"Things called user interfaces\" — javob: interfaces."},{"a":["star"],"ps":130.26,"en":138.72,"si":16,"ev":"But the one I got most out of was Star City because I was working on defining the multiplayer experience.","hl":"Star","uz":"Lekin eng ko'p zavq olganim — Star City, chunki ko'p o'yinchili tajribani shakllantirgandim.","why":"\"Got most out of\" = eng yoqqani. Javob: Star. Purple Moon va Defending Planet X — tuzoq."},{"a":["narrative"],"ps":139.26,"en":147.49,"si":17,"ev":"We wanted multi-players to play the game as if they were creating their own narrative.","hl":"narrative","uz":"Ko'p o'yinchilar o'yinni o'z hikoyasini yaratayotgandek o'ynashini xohladik.","why":"\"Creating their own narrative\" — javob: narrative. \"Story\" — bitta o'yinchi uchun biz yaratgan hikoya, tuzoq."},{"a":["difficulty"],"ps":152.57,"en":163.97,"si":19,"ev":"The most challenging aspect of the game, however, is hitting the right level of difficulty.","hl":"difficulty","uz":"O'yinning eng qiyin tomoni — qiyinlik darajasini to'g'ri topish.","why":"\"The right level of difficulty\" — javob: difficulty."},{"a":["dedication"],"ps":179.54,"en":185.37,"si":22,"ev":"Above all, you need dedication to see your vision through.","hl":"dedication","uz":"Hammasidan ham ko'proq — g'oyangizni oxiriga yetkazish uchun fidoyilik kerak.","why":"Creativity va communication ham kerak, lekin \"above all\" — dedication."}],"segs":[{"s":3.06,"e":9.5,"t":"You'll hear a man called Paul Osborne giving a careers talk about his work as a computer game designer."},{"s":21.08,"e":32.25,"t":"Hi, my name's Paul Osborne. I work as a designer in the computer game industry. Like a lot of my colleagues, I grew up playing video games, wasting money on arcades, playing the early game consoles,"},{"s":32.76,"e":35.29,"t":"Computer games have always been a big part of my life."},{"s":36.06,"e":38.88,"t":"Basically, lots of people are involved in the production of a game."},{"s":39.58,"e":44.7,"t":"As a designer, I'm largely concerned with the visual material that you see, so my background's artistic."},{"s":45.34,"e":58.14,"t":"People sometimes wrongly assume that I'm a developer. That's the guy with a maths background who actually figures out how the game works. We work closely together of course, also with the games market researcher who tells us what players are asking for."},{"s":58.87,"e":61.15,"t":"So, how did I get into game designing?"},{"s":61.69,"e":78.3,"t":"I did courses in painting and drawing … as well as one in computer graphics … and one in animation. That was the one which enabled me to build up the key … design skills I use now.","uz":"Rangtasvir, chizmachilik, kompyuter grafikasi va animatsiya kurslarini o'qidim. Hozir ishlatayotgan asosiy dizayn ko'nikmalarini aynan animatsiya kursi berdi."},{"s":78.97,"e":83.42,"t":"But I wasn't afraid of technology, so my career could have gone in a number of directions."},{"s":84.25,"e":91.68,"t":"My first job was as a graphic designer, doing book covers largely, though occasionally video game boxes or CD sleeves did come my way too."},{"s":92.18,"e":102.85,"t":"After a while, an opening came up in the company's games division for someone who had art and design sensibilities, along with some technical acumen, to work on things called user interfaces."},{"s":103.32,"e":106.46,"t":"I saw that as the opportunity to move into designing software."},{"s":107.13,"e":111.52,"t":"It was interesting to put together visual design, ergonomics, psychology and technology."},{"s":112.09,"e":116.89,"t":"I had some great mentorship from the head of my section and really developed a passion for the work."},{"s":117.78,"e":122.27,"t":"Basically, what you're responsible for as a designer is whether it aims fun or not."},{"s":122.74,"e":129.76,"t":"I've worked on a number of great games. Purple Moon was my first big challenge and I had a key role on Defending Planet X."},{"s":130.26,"e":138.72,"t":"but the one I got most out of was Star City because I was working on defining the multiplayer experience. That's when two or more people play against each other."},{"s":139.26,"e":147.49,"t":"We wanted multi-players to play the game as if they were creating their own narrative, as compared to a single player when they're experiencing a story you've made up for them."},{"s":148.41,"e":152.06,"t":"I love being able to come up with a cool idea and actually see it happen."},{"s":152.57,"e":163.97,"t":"The most challenging aspect of the game, however, is hitting the right level of difficulty. You want the game to be hard enough to reward people who gain expertise, but not so hard that people become frustrated and stop playing."},{"s":165.62,"e":167.13,"t":"What does it take to be a game designer"},{"s":167.77,"e":178.81,"t":"You need the creativity to have a vision. See what will make a game fun and create a great experience. You need the communication to articulate that vision to other people and get them to do what you think needs to be done."},{"s":179.54,"e":185.37,"t":"Above all, you need dedication to see your vision through, to work your way through the disappointments and failures."},{"s":185.82,"e":190.62,"t":"When you're three months from shipping, working until two in the morning, that's what sees you through."}]},{"n":35,"ins":2,"title":"Llama","dur":376.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Jon says that you can tell llamas and alpacas apart by the shape of their face."},{"k":"p","t":"Jon discovered that the wild ancestor of the llama was mostly light brown in colour."},{"k":"p","t":"In ancient times, domesticated llamas could often be found working in {1} areas."},{"k":"p","t":"Jon says that the word {2} is most commonly used to describe llamas."},{"k":"p","t":"Jon found out that llamas that are trained properly would only kick and spit when they feel {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Jon describes the noise llamas use to communicate as a {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Jon says that llama fleece is popular with weavers because it doesn't contain any {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The most common goods made from llama hair are {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["mining"],"ps":91.86,"en":104.06,"si":8,"ev":"The largest numbers worked as beasts of burden in mining districts rather than being associated with farming.","hl":"mining","uz":"Ularning eng ko'pi dehqonchilikda emas, konchilik hududlarida yuk tashuvchi hayvon sifatida ishlagan.","why":"\"Mining districts rather than farming\" — javob: mining. Dehqonchilik (plough) — tuzoq."},{"a":["curious"],"ps":111.38,"en":122.4,"si":10,"ev":"Although the one that comes up most often when people talk about their character is curious.","hl":"curious","uz":"Lekin ularning fe'li haqida gapirganda eng ko'p tilga olinadigan so'z — \"qiziquvchan\".","why":"Docile va friendly ham aytiladi, lekin \"most often\" — curious."},{"a":["threatened"],"ps":129.75,"en":148.61,"si":12,"ev":"In a well-brought up llama, such behaviour would be a sign that they're feeling threatened and not a sign that they feel bored or bad-tempered.","hl":"threatened","uz":"Yaxshi tarbiyalangan lamada bunday xatti-harakat zerikish yoki jahldan emas, xavf his qilayotganidan darak beradi.","why":"\"Feeling threatened\" — javob: threatened. Bored / bad-tempered — inkor qilingan, tuzoq."},{"a":["hum"],"ps":149.37,"en":163.42,"si":13,"ev":"They communicate using various noises, a gentle hum keeps them in touch with their friends and family.","hl":"hum","uz":"Ular turli tovushlar bilan muloqot qiladi: yumshoq g'uvillash do'st va oilasi bilan aloqada bo'lishga yordam beradi.","why":"Muloqot tovushi — hum. \"Bray\" — xavf haqida ogohlantirish, tuzoq."},{"a":["grease"],"ps":164.22,"en":176.41,"si":14,"ev":"It's particularly valued because it's grease-free, as well as being lightweight, warm and rather luxurious.","hl":"grease","uz":"U ayniqsa yog'siz bo'lgani, shuningdek yengil, issiq va hashamatli bo'lgani uchun qadrlanadi.","why":"\"Grease-free\" → \"doesn't contain any grease\". Javob: grease."},{"a":["rugs"],"ps":177.11,"en":188.41,"si":15,"ev":"Alpaca hair tends to make the best pullovers however, with llama being used for other things, especially rugs.","hl":"rugs","uz":"Eng yaxshi sviterlar alpaka junidan bo'ladi, lama juni esa boshqa narsalarga — ayniqsa gilamlarga ishlatiladi.","why":"\"Especially rugs\" — javob: rugs. Pullovers — alpakadan, ropes — \"quite often\", lekin asosiysi emas. (Transkriptdagi \"Packer\" — aslida \"Alpaca\".)"}],"segs":[{"s":3.13,"e":8.13,"t":"You'll hear a student called John giving a class presentation about the lama."},{"s":8.63,"e":11.26,"t":"an animal that comes originally from South America."},{"s":24.06,"e":41.63,"t":"Hi there, my name's John and the topic of my presentation is an animal which originally comes from South America. It's called the llama and it's becoming an increasingly common sight in North America and Europe, where it's used as a guard animal to protect flocks of domestic sheep and goats from predators."},{"s":42.2,"e":52.73,"t":"Just the presence of a llama is apparently enough to keep foxes and other predators away. And they are quite large animals, standing as tall as me, but weighing a lot more."},{"s":53.4,"e":61.73,"t":"But llamas themselves are domesticated animals, closely related to another smaller animal called the alpaca. People sometimes confuse the two."},{"s":62.17,"e":69.53,"t":"Alpacas have the same long and slightly curved ears, narrow feet and thick coat, but have a different face, which is shorter."},{"s":70.23,"e":85.18,"t":"Both animals are related to wild animals, which are still found in the Andes Mountains, but whereas llamas come in a range of colours including dark brown, black and white and often a mixture of the three, the animal from which it is descended tends only to be light brown."},{"s":85.69,"e":90.97,"t":"This wild animal still lives high up in the mountains near the snow line, but there aren't that many of them left."},{"s":91.86,"e":104.06,"t":"Llamas were domesticated long before European settlers arrived in the Americas. Although their meat was eaten, the largest numbers worked as beasts of burden in mining districts rather than being associated with farming."},{"s":104.57,"e":110.62,"t":"Ancient pictures do show llamas pulling a plough, but they were soon replaced by the horses and mules introduced from Europe."},{"s":111.38,"e":122.4,"t":"Llamas are one of those animals that people seem to like. You hear words like docile and friendly use to describe their character, although the one that comes up most often when people talk about their character is curious."},{"s":122.87,"e":128.93,"t":"I guess that's why they've been domesticated for so long. They approached humans and seemed more useful than dangerous."},{"s":129.75,"e":148.61,"t":"Some people think that llamas, like the camels to which they are related, sometimes kick people or even spit at them, but I read that this is a sign of poor training by the humans concerned, that in a well-brought up llama, such behaviour would be a sign that they're feeling threatened and not a sign that they feel bored or bad-tempered."},{"s":149.37,"e":163.42,"t":"Llamas are naturally very sociable animals which like to live in groups. They communicate using various noises, a gentle hum keeps them in touch with their friends and family, whereas a bray like a donkey would be a warning to others in the group of impending danger."},{"s":164.22,"e":176.41,"t":"These days, llama hair is still used in the spinning and weaving industries, where it's particularly valued because it's grease-free, as well as being lightweight, warm and rather luxurious when knitted into garments."},{"s":177.11,"e":188.41,"t":"Alpaca hair tends to make the best pullovers however, with llama being used for other things, especially rugs, but also wool hangings. And llama is quite often used to make useful things like ropes too."},{"s":189.4,"e":197.89,"t":"So, those are the basic facts about the llama. I'd now like to show you some video footage of the animal, but before I do that, does anyone have any questions?"},{"s":201.53,"e":202.05,"t":"Hi there!"}]},{"n":36,"ins":2,"title":"The swift","dur":410.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Kerry says that the Latin name for the swift translates to the words without feet in English."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry describes the noise made by swifts as a scream."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry says many people think that the bird's shape most resembles a new {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry thinks that the swifts' natural nesting site is on {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry was surprised to learn that {3} is a common material found in swifts' nests."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry has observed swifts flying fast to avoid {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Kerry says that swifts tend to be strangely {5} when they are in Africa."},{"k":"p","t":"In the past, a rich family's {6} often used the swift as a symbol."}],"items":[{"a":["moon"],"ps":89.08,"en":105.63,"si":7,"ev":"Some people say this reminds them of a new moon, and the birds certainly crescent shaped… But for me, the thing that comes to mind when I see a swift is a boomerang.","hl":"moon","uz":"Ba'zilar bu yangi oyni eslatadi deyishadi, qushlar haqiqatan ham o'roqsimon… Lekin menga qaldirg'ochni ko'rganda bumerang esga keladi.","why":"\"Many people think\" → \"some people say … a new moon\". Javob: moon. Bumerang — Kerrining o'z fikri, tuzoq."},{"a":["cliff","cliffs"],"ps":126.58,"en":133.82,"si":11,"ev":"Probably cliffs were their original preference, but even out of town, these days they tend to go for man-made places like quarries.","hl":"cliffs","uz":"Ehtimol, avvaliga ular qoyalarni afzal ko'rishgan, lekin hozir shahar tashqarisida ham karyer kabi sun'iy joylarni tanlashadi.","why":"\"Original preference\" = tabiiy uya joyi — cliffs. Quarries — sun'iy joy, tuzoq."},{"a":["paper"],"ps":134.65,"en":150.65,"si":12,"ev":"As you'd expect, leaves and grasses are used to build the nests, but … amazingly paper is often used.","hl":"paper","uz":"Kutilganidek, uya qurishga barg va o't ishlatiladi, lekin hayratlanarlisi — ko'pincha qog'oz ham ishlatiladi.","why":"\"Amazingly paper\" — ajablantirgan narsa. Javob: paper. Barg, o't, patlar — kutilgan."},{"a":["thunderstorm"],"ps":160.57,"en":170.33,"si":14,"ev":"I was once lucky enough to observe a large group of swifts travelling at great speed to get out of the way of a thunderstorm.","hl":"thunderstorm","uz":"Bir marta katta qaldirg'ochlar to'dasi momaqaldiroqdan qochish uchun juda tez uchib ketayotganini ko'rish nasib qilgan.","why":"\"Get out of the way of a thunderstorm\" — javob: thunderstorm."},{"a":["silent"],"ps":184.41,"en":190.37,"si":16,"ev":"One strange fact I discovered in my research is that once it gets back to Africa, the bird is silent.","hl":"silent","uz":"Tadqiqotimda aniqlagan g'alati fakt shuki, Afrikaga qaytgach, bu qush jim bo'lib qoladi.","why":"\"The bird is silent\" — javob: silent."},{"a":["(youngest) sons","(younger) sons"],"ps":195.0,"en":214.94,"si":18,"ev":"Traditionally in Europe, the bird was used as a symbol by the younger sons of wealthy families who, without land to inherit, were destined to wander the globe.","hl":"sons","uz":"An'anaga ko'ra Yevropada bu qush meros yeri bo'lmagani uchun dunyo kezishga mahkum boy oilalarning kichik o'g'illari ramzi bo'lgan.","why":"\"The younger sons of wealthy families\" — javob: (younger) sons."}],"segs":[{"s":3.58,"e":10.72,"t":"You'll hear a student called Carrie giving a class presentation about a type of bird called the swift."},{"s":25.43,"e":41.5,"t":"Hi, my name's Kerry and the topic of my presentation this evening is a bird called the swift. For people living in most of Europe, the swifts are familiar bird, but it only stays in the northern hemisphere for a few weeks each summer. The rest of the year it spends in sub-Saharan Africa."},{"s":42.07,"e":49.28,"t":"Indeed, one of the best known facts about this incredible bird is that it has one of the longest migrations of any living creature."},{"s":49.88,"e":59.07,"t":"The other incredible fact is that a swift spends most of its life in the air, where it eats, drinks and sleeps, only landing to build a nest and raise its young."},{"s":59.58,"e":70.81,"t":"Indeed the name of the bird in German translates to \"wall glider\" in English, whereas its Latin name means \"without feet\", both reflecting the fact that the bird never seems to touch the ground."},{"s":71.45,"e":86.78,"t":"In Europe, swifts are a familiar sight, wheeling around high up on summer evenings, making a lot of noise. But swifts don't produce a song, like sunbirds, nor do they go tweet-tweet. Instead, they produce what can only be called a scream."},{"s":87.22,"e":88.41,"t":"You must have heard it."},{"s":89.08,"e":105.63,"t":"The Swifts are not large birds, but they have a very characteristic shape in flight. Some people say this reminds them of a new moon, and the birds certainly crescent shaped with a very noticeable forked tail. But for me, the thing that comes to mind when I see a Swift is a boomerang."},{"s":106.07,"e":109.82,"t":"You know, the thing made and thrown by traditional peoples in Australia."},{"s":110.74,"e":119.39,"t":"So swifts come to Europe to breed, and they often make their nests in buildings, especially chimneys and for some reason ancient monuments."},{"s":119.96,"e":125.95,"t":"Because they can't land, the swift's nest needs to be in places from which they can launch themselves into the air."},{"s":126.58,"e":133.82,"t":"Probably cliffs were their original preference, but even out of town, these days they tend to go for man-made places like quarries.","uz":"Ehtimol, avvaliga ular qoyalarni afzal ko'rishgan, lekin hozir shahar tashqarisida ham karyer kabi sun'iy joylarni tanlashadi."},{"s":134.65,"e":150.65,"t":"As you'd expect, leaves and grasses are used to build the nests, but even here the link with humans is evident as amazingly paper is often used, together with less surprising things like the feathers of other birds. These materials the swift probably catches in flight."},{"s":151.74,"e":160.09,"t":"Because they never land, swifts are very vulnerable to bad weather and in Europe retreat to their nest sites during periods of rain or high wind."},{"s":160.57,"e":170.33,"t":"I was once lucky enough to observe a large group of swifts travelling at great speed to get out of the way of a thunderstorm. It was an awesome sight that I'll never forget."},{"s":171.35,"e":183.55,"t":"As I said, swifts only spend a short time in Europe each year, generally June and July, with even the newborn birds making an incredibly long journey to Africa in about 48 hours."},{"s":184.41,"e":190.37,"t":"One strange fact I discovered in my research is that once it gets back to Africa, the bird is silent.","uz":"Tadqiqotimda aniqlagan g'alati fakt shuki, Afrikaga qaytgach, bu qush jim bo'lib qoladi."},{"s":190.87,"e":193.92,"t":"people there being unaware of that characteristic call."},{"s":195.0,"e":214.94,"t":"These swifts have always fascinated people, especially because the birds have always been attracted to towns and buildings. Traditionally in Europe, the bird was used as a symbol by the younger sons of wealthy families who, without land to inherit, were destined to wander the globe. I like that."}]},{"n":37,"ins":2,"title":"Bestseller secrets","dur":452.4,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The best-selling celebrity autobiographies have the struggles of the celebrities as the main point."},{"k":"p","t":"Some of such autobiographies don't contain any {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Successful cookbooks give people a sense of {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Recipes from popular cookbooks are normally used only for special occasions."},{"k":"p","t":"Successful sports books have {3} which seem to be the reason why people buy them."},{"k":"p","t":"One thing that makes history books popular is oral {4} which appeal to casual readers."},{"k":"p","t":"The main focus of self-help books nowadays is how people can improve their {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The element of specific {6} in books about crime seems to be the aspect that brings good sale numbers."}],"items":[{"a":["gossip"],"ps":64.6,"en":79.29,"si":8,"ev":"And contrary to what you might expect, the top sellers in this genre do not always include gossip.","hl":"gossip","uz":"Kutganingizning aksi o'laroq, bu janrdagi eng ko'p sotilgan kitoblarda har doim ham g'iybat bo'lavermaydi.","why":"\"Do not always include gossip\" → \"some don't contain any gossip\". Javob: gossip. Barchasida bor narsa — \"struggles\", tuzoq."},{"a":["sophistication"],"ps":80.7,"en":89.95,"si":9,"ev":"They offer an air of sophistication that has huge appeal.","hl":"sophistication","uz":"Ular o'ziga jalb qiladigan nafislik ruhini beradi.","why":"\"An air of sophistication\" → \"a sense of sophistication\". Javob: sophistication."},{"a":["anecdotes"],"ps":113.62,"en":123.9,"si":12,"ev":"And what these books have in common is a wealth of anecdotes.","hl":"anecdotes","uz":"Bu kitoblarning umumiy jihati — juda ko'p qiziqarli voqealar (latifalar).","why":"\"A wealth of anecdotes\" — javob: anecdotes. \"Dry, factual accounts\" — o'quvchilarga kamroq qiziq, tuzoq."},{"a":["accounts"],"ps":146.01,"en":156.38,"si":16,"ev":"The best sellers in this category are aimed at the ordinary reader, not serious students of the subject. And one feature they all share is their use of oral accounts.","hl":"accounts","uz":"Bu turkumdagi eng ko'p sotiladigan kitoblar fanni jiddiy o'rganuvchilarga emas, oddiy o'quvchiga mo'ljallangan. Ularning hammasida bir xususiyat bor — og'zaki xotiralardan foydalanish.","why":"\"Oral accounts\" — javob: accounts. \"Ordinary reader\" → \"casual readers\"."},{"a":["careers"],"ps":170.33,"en":188.0,"si":18,"ev":"Analysis … shows a move away from those dealing with personal relationships or happiness to those advising on how to get ahead in careers.","hl":"careers","uz":"Tahlil shaxsiy munosabatlar yoki baxt haqidagi kitoblardan martabada oldinga chiqish bo'yicha maslahatlarga o'tish borligini ko'rsatadi.","why":"Hozirgi asosiy mavzu — careers. Relationships va happiness — eski mavzular, tuzoq."},{"a":["procedures"],"ps":200.28,"en":214.65,"si":21,"ev":"The scientific procedures used in criminal investigations are a dominant feature these days, rather than the character of the detective.","hl":"procedures","uz":"Bugun asosiy xususiyat — detektivning xarakteri emas, jinoyatni tergov qilishda qo'llanadigan ilmiy protseduralar.","why":"\"Scientific procedures … dominant feature\" — javob: procedures. Detektiv xarakteri — avvalgi davr, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":3.51,"e":6.85,"t":"You will hear part of a talk about best-selling books."},{"s":18.14,"e":25.82,"t":"In my role as a publishing consultant, I've recently written a report on trends in the bestseller lists over the last five years."},{"s":26.39,"e":33.79,"t":"I've carried out an in-depth analysis of best-selling titles in various categories and have tried to identify some patterns."},{"s":34.42,"e":39.33,"t":"It's my conclusion that there are some common features in the books that have been most successful."},{"s":40.22,"e":43.84,"t":"First of all, the genre of their celebrity autobiography."},{"s":44.34,"e":50.37,"t":"These consistently top the charts, selling in vast numbers, but what makes them so popular?"},{"s":51.16,"e":57.85,"t":"They show the reader a world of glamour and they claim to give an accurate picture of the real person behind the celebrity."},{"s":58.81,"e":64.13,"t":"But my research shows that the most successful books all describe the celebrity's struggles."},{"s":64.6,"e":79.29,"t":"These may be connected with achieving fame or they may come after fame or both. And contrary to what you might expect, the top sellers in this genre do not always include gossip, even though this is generally assumed to be part of their appeal."},{"s":80.7,"e":89.95,"t":"books sell in large numbers and when I analysed the top sellers in this genre it was clear that they offer an air of sophistication that has huge appeal."},{"s":90.65,"e":100.61,"t":"People aren't buying books of simple, everyday recipes. Often the ingredients required are expensive and hard to find, and the recipes can be complex and challenging."},{"s":101.21,"e":112.54,"t":"People seem to buy these books because they show a world they aspire to, rather than something they will actually do, apart from for special occasions when they may well turn to recipes in these books."},{"s":113.62,"e":123.9,"t":"comes to books about sport, the best sellers have all been biographies or autobiographies of well-known figures. And what these books have in common is a wealth of anecdotes."},{"s":124.34,"e":132.48,"t":"It's clear that readers like the feeling of being on the inside, of getting a glimpse into the world of top professional sport through these funny stories."},{"s":132.98,"e":139.87,"t":"They are less interested in dry, factual accounts of how a career started or statistics about sporting achievements."},{"s":141.05,"e":145.5,"t":"One genre that has seen a huge rise in recent years is history books."},{"s":146.01,"e":156.38,"t":"The best sellers in this category are aimed at the ordinary reader, not serious students of the subject. And one feature they all share is their use of oral accounts.","uz":"Bu turkumdagi eng ko'p sotiladigan kitoblar fanni jiddiy o'rganuvchilarga emas, oddiy o'quvchiga mo'ljallangan. Ularning hammasida bir xususiyat bor — og'zaki xotiralardan foydalanish."},{"s":156.92,"e":169.12,"t":"Quoting from people who were speaking at the time, these books aimed to provide a human aspect to history, rather than just focusing on facts and figures. And this gives them more relevance to the ordinary person."},{"s":170.33,"e":188.0,"t":"Ever since they first appeared on the scene, self-help books have always featured high on bestseller lists. Analysis of the top self-help books of the last five years shows a move away from those dealing with personal relationships or happiness to those advising on how to get ahead in careers."},{"s":188.63,"e":193.41,"t":"This suggests a shift in the priorities of the people who buy this kind of book."},{"s":194.42,"e":199.55,"t":"When it comes to fiction, crime fiction has long been extremely popular of course."},{"s":200.28,"e":214.65,"t":"My analysis of bestsellers in this genre indicates that the scientific procedures used in criminal investigations are a dominant feature these days, rather than the character of the detective which used to be the cornerstone of books in this genre."},{"s":215.45,"e":222.46,"t":"This might well reflect the current popularity of TV crime dramas, with their focus on forensic science."},{"s":223.22,"e":225.66,"t":"Now, moving on to other kinds of fiction"}]},{"n":38,"ins":2,"title":"Life coaching","dur":344.0,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"When asked about their occupation, the speaker replies that she works in the construction business."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker states that people are too focused on what she refers to as 'don't wants'."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker uses the term '{1}' to talk about long-term plans."},{"k":"p","t":"One example of a personal goal that the speaker presents is getting better at time {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"An example of a business goal is coming up with fresh {3} ideas."},{"k":"p","t":"Training sessions are organised in a way to ensure there are no physical {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Discussing a person's {5} is not a part of coaching."},{"k":"p","t":"What life coaches do is they help people turn into {6} themselves."}],"items":[{"a":["(road) map"],"ps":79.77,"en":85.02,"si":7,"ev":"Think of the goal as a destination and our plan to reach it as a road map.","hl":"map","uz":"Maqsadni manzil, unga yetish rejasini esa yo'l xaritasi deb tasavvur qiling.","why":"\"Our plan to reach it as a road map\" — javob: (road) map."},{"a":["management"],"ps":97.21,"en":100.8,"si":10,"ev":"increasing self-confidence or improving time management skills.","hl":"management","uz":"…o'ziga ishonchni oshirish yoki vaqtni boshqarish ko'nikmalarini yaxshilash.","why":"\"Improving time management skills\" — javob: management."},{"a":["marketing"],"ps":101.5,"en":108.89,"si":11,"ev":"business goals can be identifying your target market, attracting new clients and innovative marketing ideas.","hl":"marketing","uz":"Biznes maqsadlari — maqsadli bozorni aniqlash, yangi mijozlar jalb qilish va yangi marketing g'oyalari bo'lishi mumkin.","why":"\"Innovative marketing ideas\" → \"fresh marketing ideas\". Javob: marketing."},{"a":["distractions"],"ps":132.63,"en":139.65,"si":15,"ev":"Sessions are conducted on the telephone, which allows for full concentration on what the client is saying without any physical distractions.","hl":"distractions","uz":"Mashg'ulotlar telefonda o'tkaziladi, bu hech qanday jismoniy chalg'ituvchilarsiz mijoz gapiga to'liq e'tibor berish imkonini beradi.","why":"\"Without any physical distractions\" — javob: distractions."},{"a":["past"],"ps":142.49,"en":145.92,"si":17,"ev":"I do not deal with your past. That is a therapist's job.","hl":"past","uz":"Men sizning o'tmishingiz bilan shug'ullanmayman. Bu — terapevtning ishi.","why":"\"I do not deal with your past\" — javob: past."},{"a":["problem-solvers"],"ps":155.45,"en":162.49,"si":20,"ev":"Coaches do not act as problem solvers, but serve as the catalyst for the client to find their own solutions.","hl":"problem solvers","uz":"Kouchlar muammo hal qiluvchi bo'lib harakat qilmaydi, balki mijozning o'z yechimlarini topishiga turtki bo'ladi.","why":"Kouch o'zi muammoni hal qilmaydi — mijozning o'zi \"problem-solver\"ga aylanadi. Javob: problem-solvers."}],"segs":[{"s":5.05,"e":10.01,"t":"You will hear someone who works as a life coach talking about her work."},{"s":28.09,"e":41.05,"t":"I am standing in the middle of a group of people at an event and someone asks the inevitable question, \"What do you do?\" When I say that I'm a life coach, I often encounter a puzzled stare followed by the comment, \"What's that?\""},{"s":41.82,"e":52.48,"t":"I tell them that I am really in the construction business and that I partner with people to discover what they truly want in their personal lives and how to build profitable businesses."},{"s":53.53,"e":61.53,"t":"most people know what they do not want and often make the mistake of focusing on the don't wants to the detriment of their real desires."},{"s":62.14,"e":68.48,"t":"Make no mistake, we get what we focus on, so it is up to you to focus on your true goals."},{"s":69.4,"e":74.4,"t":"With the help of a coach, you are held accountable for your actions in a non-judgmental way."},{"s":75.54,"e":79.04,"t":"The first step is to identify a specific goal."},{"s":79.77,"e":85.02,"t":"Think of the goal as a destination and our plan to reach it as a road map.","uz":"Maqsadni manzil, unga yetish rejasini esa yo'l xaritasi deb tasavvur qiling."},{"s":85.82,"e":91.81,"t":"Together we devise an action-oriented strategy to achieve results much faster than you can do alone."},{"s":92.6,"e":96.77,"t":"Goals can include personal changes such as getting fit or losing weight."},{"s":97.21,"e":100.8,"t":"increasing self-confidence or improving time management skills.","uz":"…o'ziga ishonchni oshirish yoki vaqtni boshqarish ko'nikmalarini yaxshilash."},{"s":101.5,"e":108.89,"t":"business goals can be identifying your target market, attracting new clients and innovative marketing ideas.","uz":"Biznes maqsadlari — maqsadli bozorni aniqlash, yangi mijozlar jalb qilish va yangi marketing g'oyalari bo'lishi mumkin."},{"s":110.55,"e":116.86,"t":"The two most important skills that a life coach has are intensive listening and incisive questions"},{"s":117.69,"e":122.94,"t":"on your own when dealing with problems, you may not see the wood for the trees."},{"s":123.74,"e":131.77,"t":"Sometimes the coach's questions may elicit only surface answers, but with further questions, the coach can get to the true issue."},{"s":132.63,"e":139.65,"t":"Sessions are conducted on the telephone, which allows for full concentration on what the client is saying without any physical distractions.","uz":"Mashg'ulotlar telefonda o'tkaziladi, bu hech qanday jismoniy chalg'ituvchilarsiz mijoz gapiga to'liq e'tibor berish imkonini beradi."},{"s":141.05,"e":142.01,"t":"as a life coach."},{"s":142.49,"e":145.92,"t":"I do not deal with your past. That is a therapist's job.","uz":"Men sizning o'tmishingiz bilan shug'ullanmayman. Bu — terapevtning ishi."},{"s":146.36,"e":151.26,"t":"My primary concern is where you are at the moment and where you want to go in the future."},{"s":151.96,"e":154.56,"t":"What do you want to change about the here and now?"},{"s":155.45,"e":162.49,"t":"Coaches do not act as problem solvers, but serve as the catalyst for the client to find their own solutions.","uz":"Kouchlar muammo hal qiluvchi bo'lib harakat qilmaydi, balki mijozning o'z yechimlarini topishiga turtki bo'ladi."},{"s":163.48,"e":166.97,"t":"I will point out your strengths and not just your problem areas."},{"s":167.77,"e":175.58,"t":"And sometimes the client has the answers, sometimes the coach does. It really doesn't matter where the answers come from as long as they are found."}]},{"n":39,"ins":2,"title":"The Short Goodbye","dur":410.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The play takes place in an industrial city in 1950s Britain."},{"k":"p","t":"The protagonists were working in a company producing car engines."},{"k":"p","t":"An interesting thing about the play was that both main characters had a regional {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The main characters spend much time exploring the topic of social {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The male character's plan was to get a degree and work as a {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"The woman's desire was to earn a living using her talent in {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"A noteworthy part of props is a {5} at the front part of the stage."},{"k":"p","t":"Easily noticeable, {6} standing at the back are another prominent feature of the play."}],"items":[{"a":["accent"],"ps":76.41,"en":82.59,"si":8,"ev":"Another feature of the play that broke new ground at the time was that the characters all spoke with a regional accent.","hl":"accent","uz":"O'sha davrda yangilik bo'lgan yana bir xususiyat — barcha qahramonlar mahalliy (hududiy) talaffuzda gapirgan.","why":"\"Spoke with a regional accent\" — javob: accent."},{"a":["attitudes"],"ps":116.44,"en":124.0,"si":13,"ev":"However, despite their lack of education, the characters in this play spent a lot of time discussing social attitudes.","hl":"attitudes","uz":"Biroq ma'lumotsiz bo'lishiga qaramay, bu spektakl qahramonlari ijtimoiy qarashlarni muhokama qilishga ko'p vaqt sarflashgan.","why":"\"Discussing social attitudes\" — javob: attitudes. Futbol va uy ishlari — kutilgan stereotip, tuzoq."},{"a":["lawyer"],"ps":124.98,"en":133.69,"si":14,"ev":"As the plot developed, the audience discovered that the main character, Colin, was planning to enroll at a college, and that his aim was to become a lawyer.","hl":"lawyer","uz":"Voqealar rivojida tomoshabinlar bosh qahramon Kolin kollejga kirishni rejalashtirgani va maqsadi advokat bo'lish ekanini bilib olishdi.","why":"\"His aim was to become a lawyer\" — javob: lawyer."},{"a":["art"],"ps":141.91,"en":146.46,"si":16,"ev":"She felt that her talents lay in art, and she was keen to do that professionally.","hl":"art","uz":"U o'z iste'dodi san'atda deb hisoblardi va bu bilan professional shug'ullanishni juda xohlardi.","why":"\"Her talents lay in art\" — javob: art."},{"a":["piano"],"ps":173.34,"en":180.77,"si":21,"ev":"Very prominent on the stage towards the front of it so that audiences couldn't miss it was a piano.","hl":"piano","uz":"Sahnaning old tomonida, tomoshabinlar ko'rmay qolmaydigan joyda pianino turardi.","why":"\"Towards the front … a piano\" — javob: piano."},{"a":["bookshelves"],"ps":188.38,"en":194.37,"si":23,"ev":"And at the back of the stage, again very visible to the audience, was a group of bookshelves.","hl":"bookshelves","uz":"Sahnaning orqasida, yana tomoshabinlarga yaqqol ko'rinadigan bir guruh kitob javonlari bor edi.","why":"\"At the back of the stage … bookshelves\" — javob: bookshelves."}],"segs":[{"s":3.06,"e":5.92,"t":"you will hear part of a talk about a play."},{"s":22.36,"e":33.95,"t":"The play The Short Goodbye by Richard Holder is virtually unknown today and is hardly ever produced, so it may be hard to understand the impact it had when it was first produced in 1957."},{"s":34.46,"e":39.2,"t":"but it represents an important landmark in the development of theatre in the UK."},{"s":39.8,"e":43.1,"t":"So, why was this place so remarkable at the time?"},{"s":43.99,"e":50.91,"t":"To begin with, it took place in an industrial city, which was almost unheard of as the setting for a plane those days."},{"s":51.45,"e":59.71,"t":"At the time, plays were often set in small towns and suburbs or country homes, and they tended to focus on the higher end of society."},{"s":60.5,"e":64.83,"t":"The short goodbye, on the other hand, dealt with the lives of factory workers."},{"s":65.34,"e":75.26,"t":"The main characters, a husband and wife named Colin and Sadie Thomas, were low-paid workers with little education, working in a factory that made car engines."},{"s":76.41,"e":82.59,"t":"Another feature of the play that broke new ground at the time was that the characters all spoke with a regional accent.","uz":"O'sha davrda yangilik bo'lgan yana bir xususiyat — barcha qahramonlar mahalliy (hududiy) talaffuzda gapirgan."},{"s":83.29,"e":88.51,"t":"Before this, what was then regarded as standard English in terms of accent was the norm."},{"s":89.27,"e":96.32,"t":"Even when characters were from a specific part of the country, authentic regional speech was rarely heard on the stage."},{"s":97.24,"e":108.8,"t":"So, the play set out to depict working class people at that time, and it caused quite a sensation, because these characters were not what working class people were assumed to be like."},{"s":109.37,"e":115.74,"t":"It was assumed that the men talked only about football, and the women discussed only household matters."},{"s":116.44,"e":124.0,"t":"However, despite their lack of education, the characters in this play spent a lot of time discussing social attitudes.","uz":"Biroq ma'lumotsiz bo'lishiga qaramay, bu spektakl qahramonlari ijtimoiy qarashlarni muhokama qilishga ko'p vaqt sarflashgan."},{"s":124.98,"e":133.69,"t":"As the plot developed, the audience discovered that the main character, Colin, was planning to enroll at a college, and that his aim was to become a lawyer.","uz":"Voqealar rivojida tomoshabinlar bosh qahramon Kolin kollejga kirishni rejalashtirgani va maqsadi advokat bo'lish ekanini bilib olishdi."},{"s":134.42,"e":140.99,"t":"His wife Sadie also had aspirations and didn't want to spend her life doing boring work and household chores."},{"s":141.91,"e":146.46,"t":"She felt that her talents lay in art, and she was keen to do that professionally.","uz":"U o'z iste'dodi san'atda deb hisoblardi va bu bilan professional shug'ullanishni juda xohlardi."},{"s":147.38,"e":151.77,"t":"So, both characters were people who had dreams and a desire to fulfil them."},{"s":152.5,"e":156.93,"t":"This portrayal of working-class people caused a sensation at the time."},{"s":157.75,"e":164.16,"t":"Now, let me just tell you about the stage set for the play when it was first produced in 1957."},{"s":165.05,"e":172.89,"t":"It showed a modest working class home of the time, but in keeping with the themes of the play, it was a little different."},{"s":173.34,"e":180.77,"t":"Very prominent on the stage towards the front of it so that audiences couldn't miss it was a piano.","uz":"Sahnaning old tomonida, tomoshabinlar ko'rmay qolmaydigan joyda pianino turardi."},{"s":181.4,"e":187.52,"t":"It wasn't played at all, but the director and set designer both felt that it would be a striking feature."},{"s":188.38,"e":194.37,"t":"And at the back of the stage, again very visible to the audience, was a group of bookshelves.","uz":"Sahnaning orqasida, yana tomoshabinlarga yaqqol ko'rinadigan bir guruh kitob javonlari bor edi."},{"s":194.87,"e":198.43,"t":"indicating that the inhabitants were interested in reading."},{"s":199.1,"e":207.17,"t":"So, the set surprised and fascinated the audience. When the curtain opened, they wanted to know what kind of people lived there."}]},{"n":40,"ins":2,"title":"Alex and his band","dur":409.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Alex is a part of a band with the name Storm Clouds."},{"k":"p","t":"The country Alex grew up in is Canada."},{"k":"p","t":"When Alex first saw his wife, he thought she looked beautiful and {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"What makes Alex and his band different from other groups is that they are completely {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The group uses an old {3} as their recording studio."},{"k":"p","t":"Alex uses the word {4} to describe the style of their music."},{"k":"p","t":"The newest album of their band is called {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"The latest album songs explore the theme of {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["unusual"],"ps":81.82,"en":95.61,"si":18,"ev":"She was singing at that festival and her voice was amazing… Her appearance was unusual, to my eye at least, but she was also incredibly attractive.","hl":"unusual","uz":"U o'sha festivalda kuylayotgandi, ovozi ajoyib edi… Tashqi ko'rinishi, hech bo'lmaganda menga, g'ayrioddiy, lekin juda jozibali edi.","why":"\"Unusual … but also incredibly attractive\" → \"beautiful and unusual\". Javob: unusual."},{"a":["self-funded"],"ps":105.78,"en":113.09,"si":21,"ev":"In this business of modern music, we are totally different from most other groups in that we are 100% self-funded.","hl":"self-funded","uz":"Zamonaviy musiqa sohasida biz boshqa guruhlardan tubdan farq qilamiz: 100 foiz o'z mablag'imiz hisobiga ishlaymiz.","why":"\"100% self-funded\" — javob: self-funded."},{"a":["church"],"ps":133.46,"en":136.35,"si":27,"ev":"It's actually a conversion from a disused church.","hl":"church","uz":"Aslida bu — tashlandiq cherkovdan qayta qurilgan joy.","why":"\"A conversion from a disused church\" — javob: church. \"Barn\" — Aleks yashaydigan joy, tuzoq."},{"a":["romantic"],"ps":156.31,"en":160.77,"si":33,"ev":"The unifying factor in all our songs is that they're romantic.","hl":"romantic","uz":"Barcha qo'shiqlarimizni birlashtiruvchi jihat — ular romantik.","why":"\"They're romantic\" — javob: romantic. Happy, sad, wild — kayfiyatlar, uslub emas."},{"a":["shadows"],"ps":168.44,"en":179.23,"si":36,"ev":"As you know, we had a lot of success with Rainbows, our last album. The current one, Shadows, is rather different.","hl":"Shadows","uz":"Bilasiz, oldingi albomimiz Rainbows katta muvaffaqiyat qozongan. Hozirgisi — Shadows — ancha boshqacha.","why":"Eng yangisi — Shadows. Rainbows — oldingi albom, tuzoq."},{"a":["childhood"],"ps":184.28,"en":189.41,"si":38,"ev":"All the songs that we've written for this latest album in some way … childhood.","hl":"childhood","uz":"Bu so'nggi albom uchun yozgan barcha qo'shiqlarimiz qaysidir ma'noda… bolalik haqida.","why":"Albom mavzusi — childhood."}],"segs":[{"s":1.68,"e":5.18,"t":"You will hear a member of a pop group called Alex Cortes"},{"s":5.52,"e":6.97,"t":"talking about his life."},{"s":13.3,"e":15.42,"t":"It's a pleasure to be here talking to you today."},{"s":16.54,"e":21.44,"t":"So, the first thing people always ask me about is how we chose the group's name."},{"s":22.2,"e":25.18,"t":"We actually started out calling ourselves the elements."},{"s":25.98,"e":31.29,"t":"But then we came across another group with that name, so we went for Storm Clouds instead."},{"s":32.22,"e":36.16,"t":"We were sitting there racking our brains trying to come up with something different."},{"s":37.14,"e":41.92,"t":"I looked out of the window for inspiration, and the sky was incredibly black and dramatic."},{"s":43.0,"e":46.3,"t":"Two seconds later, there was thunder and lightning and that was it."},{"s":47.29,"e":49.89,"t":"feel it fits the drama we tried to bring to our music."},{"s":51.42,"e":54.01,"t":"As you know, there are actually seven of us in the group."},{"s":54.55,"e":57.53,"t":"Five of us were born and raised in the USA."},{"s":58.07,"e":62.46,"t":"I was actually born there, though my parents moved to Canada when I was a baby."},{"s":63.58,"e":66.08,"t":"Final member of the group, my wife, Lara."},{"s":66.58,"e":69.44,"t":"was actually born and grew up in Cuba."},{"s":70.52,"e":73.25,"t":"We all started out in music as individual performers."},{"s":73.69,"e":76.99,"t":"and got together when we were at a music festival in New York one summer."},{"s":78.14,"e":81.18,"t":"I met Lara, my wife, on my 21st birthday."},{"s":81.82,"e":95.61,"t":"She was singing at that festival and her voice was amazing… Her appearance was unusual, to my eye at least, but she was also incredibly attractive.","uz":"U o'sha festivalda kuylayotgandi, ovozi ajoyib edi… Tashqi ko'rinishi, hech bo'lmaganda menga, g'ayrioddiy, lekin juda jozibali edi."},{"s":96.6,"e":100.93,"t":"combination of voice and looks had an instant impact on me."},{"s":101.43,"e":104.09,"t":"making me determined to be with her forever."},{"s":105.78,"e":113.09,"t":"In this business of modern music, we are totally different from most other groups in that we are 100% self-funded.","uz":"Zamonaviy musiqa sohasida biz boshqa guruhlardan tubdan farq qilamiz: 100 foiz o'z mablag'imiz hisobiga ishlaymiz."},{"s":113.66,"e":116.83,"t":"That means we don't have to answer to anyone else."},{"s":117.62,"e":120.51,"t":"we can make our own musical and business decisions."},{"s":121.02,"e":123.97,"t":"And that independence means a great deal to us all."},{"s":125.82,"e":130.24,"t":"Of course this means that we don't have access to the major record company studios."},{"s":130.97,"e":132.54,"t":"We've managed to make our own."},{"s":133.46,"e":136.35,"t":"It's actually a conversion from a disused church.","uz":"Aslida bu — tashlandiq cherkovdan qayta qurilgan joy."},{"s":137.08,"e":143.81,"t":"It's convenient because it's actually next door to the large old converted barn where I live with my family."},{"s":146.14,"e":148.89,"t":"It's hard to characterize our style of music."},{"s":149.37,"e":151.52,"t":"It's often called unconventional."},{"s":152.28,"e":154.53,"t":"But that slightly misses the mark in my opinion."},{"s":155.19,"e":155.77,"t":"for me."},{"s":156.31,"e":160.77,"t":"The unifying factor in all our songs is that they're romantic.","uz":"Barcha qo'shiqlarimizni birlashtiruvchi jihat — ular romantik."},{"s":161.88,"e":165.92,"t":"That's always there. Whether the song is happy or sad, wild,"},{"s":166.46,"e":167.23,"t":"or sentimental."},{"s":168.44,"e":179.23,"t":"As you know, we had a lot of success with Rainbows, our last album. The current one, Shadows, is rather different.","uz":"Bilasiz, oldingi albomimiz Rainbows katta muvaffaqiyat qozongan. Hozirgisi — Shadows — ancha boshqacha."},{"s":179.83,"e":183.13,"t":"A lot of the songs are slower with stronger melodies."},{"s":184.28,"e":189.41,"t":"All the songs that we've written for this latest album in some way … childhood.","uz":"Bu so'nggi albom uchun yozgan barcha qo'shiqlarimiz qaysidir ma'noda… bolalik haqida."},{"s":190.58,"e":194.53,"t":"Each member of the group brought very different experiences to this."},{"s":195.13,"e":198.14,"t":"and we've all contributed our ideas to the topic."},{"s":199.54,"e":202.97,"t":"Perhaps I could now just play you one track from this album?"},{"s":203.51,"e":204.86,"t":"before I take questions."}]},{"n":41,"ins":2,"title":"Lara's new start","dur":417.0,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Lara had been working as a lawyer before she was made redundant."},{"k":"p","t":"As soon as she returned to work after recovering from {1} she found out that she had lost her job."},{"k":"p","t":"She decided to travel to Central America as soon as she became unemployed."},{"k":"p","t":"Lara chose to focus on getting better at {2} when she came back from the trip."},{"k":"p","t":"Lara enjoyed watching the {3} during the time she worked for a holiday company."},{"k":"p","t":"Lara realised how {4} her life was previously."},{"k":"p","t":"Lara suggests that one shouldn't {5} if they suddenly find themselves unemployed."},{"k":"p","t":"Lara feels {6} towards her former employers."}],"items":[{"a":["flu"],"ps":43.29,"en":48.06,"si":7,"ev":"I lost my job in August. I'd just been off sick with flu.","hl":"flu","uz":"Avgustda ishimdan ayrildim. Endigina gripp bilan kasal bo'lib, ishga chiqmay turgan edim.","why":"\"Off sick with flu\" — javob: flu."},{"a":["skiing"],"ps":107.74,"en":118.43,"si":20,"ev":"I'd recently been skiing for the first time and I really enjoyed it, but had thought to myself that I'd never be able to get that good if I only did it once a year.","hl":"skiing","uz":"Yaqinda birinchi marta chang'i uchgandim, juda yoqdi, lekin yiliga bir marta uchsam hech qachon yaxshi o'rgana olmayman deb o'ylagandim.","why":"Fransuz tili va golf — boshqalarning misoli, tuzoq. Lara tanlagani — skiing."},{"a":["sunrise"],"ps":132.28,"en":141.6,"si":24,"ev":"I'm not normally someone who likes early mornings. But when I had to get up at 6am and saw the sunrise, it was all worth it.","hl":"sunrise","uz":"Odatda erta tongni yoqtiradigan odam emasman. Lekin soat 6 da turib, quyosh chiqishini ko'rganimda, bunga arzirdi.","why":"\"Saw the sunrise … it was all worth it\" — javob: sunrise."},{"a":["ordinary"],"ps":155.96,"en":160.8,"si":29,"ev":"I liked my life before, but I appreciate now that it was very ordinary.","hl":"ordinary","uz":"Avvalgi hayotim menga yoqardi, lekin endi uning juda oddiy bo'lganini tushunaman.","why":"\"I appreciate now … very ordinary\" — javob: ordinary."},{"a":["panic"],"ps":170.87,"en":176.03,"si":34,"ev":"First thing I'd say is to welcome it and above all, don't panic.","hl":"panic","uz":"Birinchi aytadiganim — buni xush qabul qiling va eng muhimi, vahimaga tushmang.","why":"\"Above all, don't panic\" — javob: panic."},{"a":["gratitude"],"ps":196.25,"en":202.75,"si":39,"ev":"My main feeling now towards the people who fired me is, honestly, one of gratitude.","hl":"gratitude","uz":"Meni ishdan bo'shatgan odamlarga hozirgi asosiy tuyg'um, rostini aytsam, minnatdorlik.","why":"\"One of gratitude\" — javob: gratitude."}],"segs":[{"s":2.3,"e":8.25,"t":"You will hear a woman called Lara King talking about her experiences after losing her job."},{"s":14.49,"e":20.09,"t":"My name's Lara King and I'm here to tell you about my experience of losing my job."},{"s":20.98,"e":23.42,"t":"I'd had a feeling I would get made redundant."},{"s":23.99,"e":28.03,"t":"One of my best friends worked as a banker and she'd lost her job."},{"s":28.5,"e":31.45,"t":"as had another one who was an IT consultant."},{"s":32.34,"e":37.79,"t":"I had a good job as a lawyer and the company I was employed by had just been taken over."},{"s":38.74,"e":42.17,"t":"been working there for three years and I loved it."},{"s":43.29,"e":48.06,"t":"I lost my job in August. I'd just been off sick with flu.","uz":"Avgustda ishimdan ayrildim. Endigina gripp bilan kasal bo'lib, ishga chiqmay turgan edim."},{"s":48.79,"e":50.56,"t":"I don't usually catch things."},{"s":51.06,"e":56.93,"t":"The last time I was ill was at school when I had bronchitis quite badly once."},{"s":57.69,"e":60.35,"t":"Anyway, I'd been off for over a week."},{"s":61.14,"e":66.46,"t":"Then on my first day back at work, I found I didn't have a job anymore."},{"s":67.61,"e":71.29,"t":"My first reaction was to rush back home to my parents in Ireland."},{"s":71.93,"e":73.79,"t":"but I decided to resist that."},{"s":74.52,"e":78.78,"t":"Then, within a week, I'd booked a flight to Central America."},{"s":79.29,"e":81.25,"t":"and spent a month travelling there."},{"s":81.98,"e":88.57,"t":"I thought to myself, I'm 33, I don't have any ties and I don't have to find a new job."},{"s":89.27,"e":94.11,"t":"I can use this as an opportunity to do something totally different."},{"s":95.64,"e":101.6,"t":"Anyone with a job like I had should have something they'd like to do if they get made redundant."},{"s":102.26,"e":106.78,"t":"something like improve their French or learn how to play golf."},{"s":107.74,"e":118.43,"t":"I'd recently been skiing for the first time and I really enjoyed it, but had thought to myself that I'd never be able to get that good if I only did it once a year.","uz":"Yaqinda birinchi marta chang'i uchgandim, juda yoqdi, lekin yiliga bir marta uchsam hech qachon yaxshi o'rgana olmayman deb o'ylagandim."},{"s":118.97,"e":124.0,"t":"So, it seemed like the perfect opportunity to spend more time in the mountains."},{"s":124.92,"e":128.45,"t":"I began working as a rep with a winter holiday company."},{"s":129.18,"e":131.55,"t":"It was like nothing I've ever done before."},{"s":132.28,"e":141.6,"t":"I'm not normally someone who likes early mornings. But when I had to get up at 6am and saw the sunrise, it was all worth it.","uz":"Odatda erta tongni yoqtiradigan odam emasman. Lekin soat 6 da turib, quyosh chiqishini ko'rganimda, bunga arzirdi."},{"s":142.1,"e":145.05,"t":"I don't think I've ever seen such beauty."},{"s":146.07,"e":147.1,"t":"six months ago."},{"s":147.7,"e":151.42,"t":"I was working at a computer all day, every day."},{"s":151.9,"e":155.17,"t":"And who knows what I'll be doing this time next year."},{"s":155.96,"e":160.8,"t":"I liked my life before, but I appreciate now that it was very ordinary.","uz":"Avvalgi hayotim menga yoqardi, lekin endi uning juda oddiy bo'lganini tushunaman."},{"s":161.24,"e":163.45,"t":"And there's an awful lot more out there."},{"s":164.63,"e":167.29,"t":"If one of my friends got made redundant tomorrow"},{"s":167.77,"e":169.05,"t":"What advice would I give?"},{"s":169.72,"e":170.05,"t":"Well"},{"s":170.87,"e":176.03,"t":"First thing I'd say is to welcome it and above all, don't panic.","uz":"Birinchi aytadiganim — buni xush qabul qiling va eng muhimi, vahimaga tushmang."},{"s":176.82,"e":180.03,"t":"See it as a chance to do something you've never done before."},{"s":181.24,"e":183.71,"t":"As for the people who've put you in that position."},{"s":184.54,"e":188.7,"t":"I think it's also crucial not to feel a sense of anger towards them."},{"s":189.3,"e":195.42,"t":"partly because there's no point, but also because they've actually given you an opportunity."},{"s":196.25,"e":202.75,"t":"My main feeling now towards the people who fired me is, honestly, one of gratitude.","uz":"Meni ishdan bo'shatgan odamlarga hozirgi asosiy tuyg'um, rostini aytsam, minnatdorlik."},{"s":203.45,"e":206.17,"t":"if you're given the chance to try something different."},{"s":206.78,"e":208.29,"t":"You should just take it."},{"s":221.3,"e":222.75,"t":"My name's Lara King."}]},{"n":42,"ins":2,"title":"Greenland expedition","dur":405.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"James Munro and Greg Hamilton managed to finish an unsupported expedition through Greenland."},{"k":"p","t":"According to James, the only things helping them in this expedition were {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Both James' parents worked as {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"James believes that his love for {3} made him more interested in adventures."},{"k":"p","t":"The expedition to the North Pole in 1995 fascinated James."},{"k":"p","t":"James admires Nansen for his breadth as he was a diplomat, an explorer as well as a {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"James is convinced that having control over one's {5} is essential for an explorer."},{"k":"p","t":"James believes that making use of {6} is the best way for inexperienced explorers to get sponsors."}],"items":[{"a":["kites"],"ps":51.48,"en":64.73,"si":5,"ev":"The only help that we did have was from kites, which, when the wind conditions were good, pulled us along as we skied.","hl":"kites","uz":"Bizga yagona yordam — varraklar edi: shamol yaxshi bo'lganda ular bizni tortib borardi.","why":"\"The only help … from kites\" — javob: kites. Motorli transport va hayvonlar ishlatilmagan."},{"a":["architects"],"ps":78.62,"en":84.48,"si":8,"ev":"In fact, my mum and dad were both architects, and neither of them were even particularly into sport.","hl":"architects","uz":"Aslida onam ham, otam ham arxitektor edi, ikkalasi ham sportga unchalik qiziqmasdi.","why":"\"Both architects\" — javob: architects. Tadqiqotchilar oilasi (explorers) — odamlarning taxmini, tuzoq."},{"a":["kayaking"],"ps":102.87,"en":107.52,"si":13,"ev":"It all started when I discovered I got a particular kick out of kayaking.","hl":"kayaking","uz":"Hammasi kayakda suzishdan alohida zavq olishimni bilganimdan boshlandi.","why":"\"A particular kick out of kayaking\" — javob: kayaking."},{"a":["geologist"],"ps":150.33,"en":156.32,"si":20,"ev":"He had great breadth, as is shown by the fact that he was also a diplomat and geologist.","hl":"geologist","uz":"Uning kengqamrovliligi shundan ko'rinadiki, u diplomat va geolog ham bo'lgan.","why":"Diplomat, tadqiqotchi va \"geologist\". Javob: geologist."},{"a":["mind"],"ps":160.28,"en":169.44,"si":22,"ev":"Reading Nansen's biography taught me that the key thing all explorers need in harsh conditions is the ability to keep their mind under control.","hl":"mind","uz":"Nansen tarjimai holini o'qib, barcha tadqiqotchilarga og'ir sharoitda eng kerakli narsa — ongini nazorat ostida tuta bilish ekanini bildim.","why":"\"Keep their mind under control\" — javob: mind. Tana (body) — yetarli emas, tuzoq."},{"a":["networking"],"ps":190.68,"en":197.79,"si":26,"ev":"In terms of gaining the necessary funding, don't spend months cold calling, but concentrate on networking.","hl":"networking","uz":"Kerakli mablag' topishda oylab notanish odamlarga qo'ng'iroq qilmang, tanishlar tarmog'iga e'tibor bering.","why":"Cold calling — tavsiya qilinmaydi; \"concentrate on networking\" — javob: networking."}],"segs":[{"s":2.14,"e":7.07,"t":"You'll hear a young Arctic explorer called James Monroe talking about his work."},{"s":19.58,"e":31.13,"t":"I feel very fortunate that at only 23 years old, I have already spent more than 18 weeks on an unsupported polar expedition, going from one side of Greenland to the other."},{"s":31.83,"e":34.91,"t":"I completed it last year together with Greg Hamilton."},{"s":35.54,"e":42.69,"t":"It was 2,198 kilometers and it was actually the longest unsupported polar expedition in history."},{"s":43.45,"e":50.72,"t":"By \"unsupported\" I mean that we pulled everything ourselves without the help of any motorized vehicles or animals."},{"s":51.48,"e":64.73,"t":"The only help that we did have was from kites, which, when the wind conditions were good, pulled us along as we skied, dragging our sleds behind us. I can assure you that it was still very hard work."},{"s":65.82,"e":69.5,"t":"People often ask me what first interested me in polar exploration."},{"s":70.2,"e":78.05,"t":"I think they imagine that I come from a family of explorers or something like that, but in fact I come from a pretty conventional family."},{"s":78.62,"e":84.48,"t":"In fact, my mum and dad were both architects, and neither of them were even particularly into sport.","uz":"Aslida onam ham, otam ham arxitektor edi, ikkalasi ham sportga unchalik qiziqmasdi."},{"s":85.11,"e":87.71,"t":"They often wonder where on earth I could have got it from."},{"s":88.6,"e":93.92,"t":"I was always very sporty and adored football from pretty much before I could walk."},{"s":94.49,"e":96.51,"t":"I did a lot of swimming and cycling too."},{"s":97.4,"e":102.08,"t":"I was about 15, I suppose, when I became hooked on adventurous activities."},{"s":102.87,"e":107.52,"t":"It all started when I discovered I got a particular kick out of kayaking.","uz":"Hammasi kayakda suzishdan alohida zavq olishimni bilganimdan boshlandi."},{"s":108.06,"e":112.89,"t":"That took me on some amazing long expeditions, and I guess I haven't looked back since."},{"s":113.94,"e":121.95,"t":"Also, when I was about 15, I learnt about an expedition which has gripped my imagination and held my admiration ever since."},{"s":122.74,"e":129.89,"t":"This was the 1995 Unsupported Journey by Richard Webber and Misha Malekoff to the North Pole."},{"s":130.78,"e":139.45,"t":"The distance and technical difficulty of their expedition was enormous and they kept going despite most so-called experts claiming they would fail."},{"s":140.79,"e":143.07,"t":"I love reading about other explorers."},{"s":143.74,"e":149.5,"t":"If I were to have a hero, it would undoubtedly be Fritjof Nansen, the Norwegian explorer."},{"s":150.33,"e":156.32,"t":"He had great breadth, as is shown by the fact that he was also a diplomat and geologist.","uz":"Uning kengqamrovliligi shundan ko'rinadiki, u diplomat va geolog ham bo'lgan."},{"s":157.3,"e":159.49,"t":"All in all, a quite remarkable man."},{"s":160.28,"e":169.44,"t":"Reading Nansen's biography taught me that the key thing all explorers need in harsh conditions is the ability to keep their mind under control.","uz":"Nansen tarjimai holini o'qib, barcha tadqiqotchilarga og'ir sharoitda eng kerakli narsa — ongini nazorat ostida tuta bilish ekanini bildim."},{"s":170.26,"e":176.0,"t":"if they can't manage that, then they won't succeed, even if their body is in top physical condition."},{"s":177.43,"e":186.53,"t":"I'm often asked to give advice to would-be explorers and I always say, \"You shouldn't just look at what has already been done and copy it, thinking it's the only way.\""},{"s":187.22,"e":189.85,"t":"Think of new challenges that you can attempt."},{"s":190.68,"e":197.79,"t":"In terms of gaining the necessary funding, don't spend months cold calling, but concentrate on networking.","uz":"Kerakli mablag' topishda oylab notanish odamlarga qo'ng'iroq qilmang, tanishlar tarmog'iga e'tibor bering."},{"s":198.33,"e":203.68,"t":"This is the only way to make the critical relationships which lead to big sums of funds."}]},{"n":43,"ins":2,"title":"Wood carving","dur":391.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"In her childhood, the speaker saw a piece of furniture with a hidden carving of a mouse on it."},{"k":"p","t":"The woman appreciates wood-carving artists as they have more patience than she has."},{"k":"p","t":"Di Marchi's old wooden {1} is his tool of choice."},{"k":"p","t":"A Dream in Venice depicts four steeds pulling a huge {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"In his first works Di Marchi used {3} as the material."},{"k":"p","t":"He later switched to wood as he believed it allowed him larger {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker prefers his carving of a {5} the most."},{"k":"p","t":"The woman uses the word {6} to describe the carver's works."}],"items":[{"a":["hammer"],"ps":69.56,"en":77.28,"si":9,"ev":"He prefers to use simple but familiar tools, including a hundred different kinds of chisel and an ancient hammer made of wood.","hl":"hammer","uz":"U oddiy, lekin tanish asboblarni afzal ko'radi: yuz xil iskana va yog'ochdan qilingan qadimiy bolg'a.","why":"\"An ancient hammer made of wood\" — javob: hammer. Iskanalar (chisel) — yuz xil, \"old wooden\" emas."},{"a":["pumpkin"],"ps":93.27,"en":100.93,"si":12,"ev":"This extraordinary creation is a huge pumpkin drawn by four horses.","hl":"pumpkin","uz":"Bu g'aroyib asar — to'rtta ot tortib borayotgan ulkan qovoq.","why":"\"Four steeds\" = \"four horses\". Javob: pumpkin."},{"a":["marble"],"ps":133.3,"en":136.83,"si":16,"ev":"He started off working in marble, later moving to bronze.","hl":"marble","uz":"U marmar bilan ishlashdan boshlagan, keyin bronzaga o'tgan.","why":"Birinchi material — marble. Bronza — keyingisi, tuzoq."},{"a":["scope"],"ps":141.72,"en":144.96,"si":18,"ev":"He said he did so because Wood offered greater scope.","hl":"scope","uz":"U yog'och kengroq imkoniyat bergani uchun shunday qilganini aytgan.","why":"\"Wood offered greater scope\" — javob: scope."},{"a":["jacket"],"ps":160.66,"en":170.4,"si":22,"ev":"The one I like best is a jacket. It just looks so realistic.","hl":"jacket","uz":"Menga eng yoqqani — kurtka. U juda haqiqiyga o'xshaydi.","why":"Speaker uchun — jacket. Mashina (car) — boshqalarning sevimlisi, tuzoq."},{"a":["incredible"],"ps":179.1,"en":196.73,"si":24,"ev":"In fact, the most appropriate adjective to describe his work is simply 'incredible'.","hl":"incredible","uz":"Aslida uning ishlarini tasvirlash uchun eng mos sifat — shunchaki \"aql bovar qilmas\".","why":"\"Wooden\" — qotib qolgan narsa uchun ishlatiladi, lekin asarlar unday emas. Javob: incredible."}],"segs":[{"s":3.35,"e":6.56,"t":"You'll hear a student talking about her favourite artist."},{"s":7.03,"e":9.63,"t":"a wood cover called Livio di Marche."},{"s":22.71,"e":30.56,"t":"So today I want to tell you about my favourite artist. He's an absolutely amazing wood carver called Livio Di Marchi."},{"s":31.0,"e":38.46,"t":"I've always loved wood carving, ever since I was a small child. One of my favorite toys was a lovely carved wooden bear."},{"s":39.0,"e":44.83,"t":"Also, an uncle had a table made by someone who'd carved a mouse at the top of one of the legs."},{"s":45.3,"e":51.01,"t":"You couldn't see it without crawling under the table, but it seems such a personal and fun thing to do."},{"s":51.9,"e":61.63,"t":"Wood carving is a wonderful kind of art, I think. You just have to marvel at the patience of the people who've spent endless hours creating their works for our pleasure."},{"s":62.14,"e":63.84,"t":"I'd never be able to do it, I"},{"s":64.6,"e":69.05,"t":"Anyway, Livio Di Marchi is a wood carver from Venice in Italy."},{"s":69.56,"e":77.28,"t":"He prefers to use simple but familiar tools, including a hundred different kinds of chisel and an ancient hammer made of wood.","uz":"U oddiy, lekin tanish asboblarni afzal ko'radi: yuz xil iskana va yog'ochdan qilingan qadimiy bolg'a."},{"s":77.75,"e":83.17,"t":"He is truly a master craftsman and some of his work is absolutely awesome."},{"s":83.96,"e":92.8,"t":"Many of his pieces are very famous. For example, he did one called \"A Dream in Venice\" that made an appearance in 1994."},{"s":93.27,"e":100.93,"t":"This extraordinary creation is a huge pumpkin drawn by four horses, which rear up when the driver pulls the reins."},{"s":101.4,"e":110.97,"t":"It can accommodate four people as it glides across the waters of the Venetian canals and was one of the jewels of the carnival that took place in the city that year."},{"s":111.58,"e":122.94,"t":"As a child, Dimaki's interest in ornamental carving led him to work and practice in a craftsman's workshop while studying art and drawing at a famous Venetian art academy."},{"s":123.58,"e":132.77,"t":"From an early age, he was demonstrating that he had enormous artistic talent for moulding materials, creating wonderfully detailed sculptures."},{"s":133.3,"e":136.83,"t":"He started off working in marble, later moving to bronze.","uz":"U marmar bilan ishlashdan boshlagan, keyin bronzaga o'tgan."},{"s":137.43,"e":141.18,"t":"However, it was not long before he gravitated towards wood."},{"s":141.72,"e":144.96,"t":"He said he did so because Wood offered greater scope.","uz":"U yog'och kengroq imkoniyat bergani uchun shunday qilganini aytgan."},{"s":145.53,"e":151.23,"t":"He felt he would be able to put it to a very wide range of uses, and indeed he has done so."},{"s":152.06,"e":155.04,"t":"He has created a wonderful variety of pieces."},{"s":155.64,"e":160.16,"t":"basket full of teddy bears, items of clothing, all sorts of things."},{"s":160.66,"e":170.4,"t":"The one I like best is a jacket. It just looks so realistic. You want to touch it because you're sure it must actually be made of leather. But it isn't."},{"s":171.1,"e":178.14,"t":"But many other people would say their favourite piece is a car. He's done several of those, and they're also amazingly realistic."},{"s":179.1,"e":196.73,"t":"We often use the word 'wooden' to describe something stiff, but Di Marche's works are very far from stiff in this sense. In fact, the most appropriate adjective to describe his work is simply 'incredible'. You just cannot believe that his objects are all made of wood."}]},{"n":44,"ins":2,"title":"Computer games","dur":407.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The speaker believes the computer games industry is a great career choice because it is creative."},{"k":"p","t":"Back at university the speaker got a degree in economics."},{"k":"p","t":"She applied for the job when her {1} shared a contact name with her."},{"k":"p","t":"At first she worked as a {2} for a big name in the industry."},{"k":"p","t":"The first game she worked on was called {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker was later transferred to the company's {4} department."},{"k":"p","t":"She derives particular pleasure from working on {5} games."},{"k":"p","t":"The speaker uses the word {6} to describe her career in the industry."}],"items":[{"a":["uncle"],"ps":79.32,"en":85.82,"si":9,"ev":"My uncle sent me the name of someone he knew at a major games company, so I decided to apply there first.","hl":"uncle","uz":"Amakim menga yirik o'yin kompaniyasidagi bir tanishining ismini yubordi va men avval o'sha yerga ariza berishga qaror qildim.","why":"Kontakt ismini — uncle yuborgan. Ota-onasi — sohaga borishni maslahat bergan, tuzoq."},{"a":["tester"],"ps":89.4,"en":95.13,"si":11,"ev":"I didn't have the skills to become a technical programmer of course, and started as a games tester.","hl":"tester","uz":"Albatta, texnik dasturchi bo'lishga malakam yetmasdi, shuning uchun o'yin sinovchisi bo'lib boshladim.","why":"\"Started as a games tester\" — javob: tester."},{"a":["jungle"],"ps":102.49,"en":110.59,"si":13,"ev":"It's called Jungle. It turned out to be a big seller.","hl":"Jungle","uz":"U \"Jungle\" deb ataladi. Juda yaxshi sotildi.","why":"Birinchi o'yin — Jungle."},{"a":["research"],"ps":128.54,"en":131.26,"si":18,"ev":"I was given a position in the research department.","hl":"research","uz":"Menga tadqiqot bo'limidan lavozim berildi.","why":"\"Research department\" — javob: research. Marketing — ariza bergan, lekin olmagan, tuzoq."},{"a":["adventure"],"ps":141.08,"en":162.3,"si":21,"ev":"It's also dabbled in old-fashioned arcade games, and it does some adventure games too. Those are the ones I personally most enjoy working on.","hl":"adventure","uz":"Kompaniya eski arkada o'yinlari bilan ham shug'ullangan, sarguzasht o'yinlari ham chiqaradi. Menga shaxsan eng yoqadigani — aynan shular.","why":"Kompaniya asosan sport o'yinlari qiladi, lekin unga eng yoqadigani — adventure. Sport — tuzoq."},{"a":["satisfying"],"ps":166.9,"en":173.85,"si":23,"ev":"Anyway, I'd certainly recommend a career in computer games. I'd say mine has been very satisfying.","hl":"satisfying","uz":"Kompyuter o'yinlari sohasini albatta tavsiya qilaman. Mening faoliyatim juda mamnunlik bag'ishladi.","why":"\"Very satisfying\" — javob: satisfying. Moliyaviy jihat — unchalik emas."}],"segs":[{"s":2.42,"e":6.56,"t":"You'll hear part of a talk about working in the computer games industry."},{"s":12.76,"e":16.13,"t":"I'm here today to talk to you about working in computer gaming."},{"s":16.63,"e":30.72,"t":"I'd certainly recommend it as a career. Not because it's glamorous, it has that reputation among some people, I believe, nor because it's a well-paid job. Generally it isn't. But rather because it's creative."},{"s":31.19,"e":37.02,"t":"And that's the fact that all things being equal correlates most highly with job satisfaction."},{"s":37.78,"e":42.91,"t":"People get jobs in the computer games industry after degrees in all sorts of subjects."},{"s":43.38,"e":50.14,"t":"Of course, if you've done a course in graphic design, that'll stand you in good stead, but it's certainly not essential."},{"s":50.65,"e":57.37,"t":"I myself graduated in economics and colleagues of mine did history, engineering and English."},{"s":57.85,"e":62.88,"t":"The degree itself is less important than the enthusiasm someone brings to the job."},{"s":63.67,"e":78.65,"t":"It goes without saying that everyone who joins the industry has themselves enjoyed playing games. My parents always told me I spent far too much time on them, so much so that they suggested I put it to good use and apply for work in the industry."},{"s":79.32,"e":85.82,"t":"My uncle sent me the name of someone he knew at a major games company, so I decided to apply there first.","uz":"Amakim menga yirik o'yin kompaniyasidagi bir tanishining ismini yubordi va men avval o'sha yerga ariza berishga qaror qildim."},{"s":86.65,"e":88.89,"t":"I was lucky enough to get taken on."},{"s":89.4,"e":95.13,"t":"I didn't have the skills to become a technical programmer of course, and started as a games tester.","uz":"Albatta, texnik dasturchi bo'lishga malakam yetmasdi, shuning uchun o'yin sinovchisi bo'lib boshladim."},{"s":95.93,"e":101.44,"t":"It taught me a huge amount and after six months I was able to do something more demanding."},{"s":102.49,"e":110.59,"t":"At first, I was assigned to one of the games the company was then in the process of developing. You may well know it. It's called Jungle."},{"s":111.03,"e":112.57,"t":"It turned out to be a big seller."},{"s":113.14,"e":120.67,"t":"Later, I worked on a game called Motor Show. That's less widely known, but it has a devoted niche following."},{"s":121.27,"e":125.15,"t":"Anyway, I learned a lot working on these two contrasting products."},{"s":125.94,"e":128.0,"t":"After six months, I moved on."},{"s":128.54,"e":131.26,"t":"I was given a position in the research department.","uz":"Menga tadqiqot bo'limidan lavozim berildi."},{"s":131.9,"e":135.81,"t":"I had applied for something in the marketing department but didn't get that."},{"s":136.25,"e":140.35,"t":"I was disappointed at the time but now feel it worked out for the best."},{"s":141.08,"e":162.3,"t":"It's also dabbled in old-fashioned arcade games, and it does some adventure games too. Those are the ones I personally most enjoy working on.","uz":"Kompaniya eski arkada o'yinlari bilan ham shug'ullangan, sarguzasht o'yinlari ham chiqaradi. Menga shaxsan eng yoqadigani — aynan shular."},{"s":162.78,"e":166.24,"t":"though each type of game has its own attractions of course."},{"s":166.9,"e":173.85,"t":"Anyway, I'd certainly recommend a career in computer games. I'd say mine has been very satisfying.","uz":"Kompyuter o'yinlari sohasini albatta tavsiya qilaman. Mening faoliyatim juda mamnunlik bag'ishladi."},{"s":174.36,"e":179.87,"t":"Not as financially rewarding as some of you might like, but that's not the main thing, is it?"},{"s":180.57,"e":186.56,"t":"When preparing for this talk, I asked some of my colleagues how they would sum up their careers."},{"s":187.16,"e":190.3,"t":"The most common word they used was 'challenging'."},{"s":191.0,"e":195.74,"t":"I don't feel that that puts a positive enough slant on a career in computer games."},{"s":196.47,"e":199.49,"t":"Anyway, let me now take any questions."}]},{"n":45,"ins":2,"title":"South Africa","dur":427.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Harriet was keen to visit South Africa because her grandfather spent his childhood there."},{"k":"p","t":"The reason she went to South Africa originally was to attend some rugby matches."},{"k":"p","t":"A company called Rainbow {1} helped her organise the trip."},{"k":"p","t":"The {2} was the first surprising thing about the country."},{"k":"p","t":"Harriet says that {3} were the animals that she most enjoyed seeing at the safari park."},{"k":"p","t":"She made a stop to visit a {4} farm on the east coast."},{"k":"p","t":"She suggests {5} as a good month to visit the country."},{"k":"p","t":"Harriet uses the word {6} to describe how she felt after the holiday."}],"items":[{"a":["tours"],"ps":84.66,"en":91.42,"si":11,"ev":"The school used a travel agent called Rainbow Tours and they were able to make arrangements for us too.","hl":"Tours","uz":"Maktab Rainbow Tours degan turagentlikdan foydalangan, ular biz uchun ham hamma narsani tashkil qila olishdi.","why":"\"Rainbow Tours\" — javob: tours. Safari Holidays — ko'rib chiqilgan, lekin tanlanmagan."},{"a":["light"],"ps":106.2,"en":117.41,"si":15,"ev":"As soon as I got off the plane after a overnight flight, I was impressed by the light there. was just so clear. different from what we have here.","hl":"light","uz":"Bir kechalik reysdan keyin samolyotdan tushishim bilan u yerdagi yorug'lik meni hayratga soldi. Juda tiniq edi, biznikidan butunlay boshqacha.","why":"Birinchi hayratlantirgan narsa — light. Issiqlik (warm) — kutilgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["cheetahs"],"ps":145.91,"en":151.65,"si":21,"ev":"Best of all for me were the cheetahs, which we saw when we went on a night drive.","hl":"cheetahs","uz":"Men uchun hammasidan zo'ri — tungi sayr paytida ko'rgan gepardlar bo'ldi.","why":"\"Best of all for me were the cheetahs\" — javob: cheetahs. Gippopotamlar — erining sevimlisi, tuzoq. (Transkriptdagi \"cheaters\" — aslida \"cheetahs\".)"},{"a":["crocodile"],"ps":169.56,"en":174.78,"si":25,"ev":"One day we broke our journey at a crocodile farm and learnt so much about them.","hl":"crocodile","uz":"Bir kuni yo'limizda timsoh fermasida to'xtadik va ular haqida ko'p narsa bildik.","why":"\"A crocodile farm\" — javob: crocodile. Zebra va tuyaqushlar — yo'lda ko'rilgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["April"],"ps":180.76,"en":188.54,"si":27,"ev":"I'm told the best time to go is April - it's cooler then, at night particularly - and so you've got more energy for sightseeing.","hl":"April","uz":"Aytishlaricha, borishga eng yaxshi vaqt — aprel: o'shanda salqinroq bo'ladi.","why":"Tavsiya — April. Yanvar — ular borgan oy, juda issiq bo'lgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["exhausted"],"ps":194.3,"en":201.15,"si":29,"ev":"We felt so relaxed during the trip. I was taken aback when we got home to discover how exhausted I was.","hl":"exhausted","uz":"Safar davomida o'zimizni juda xotirjam his qildik. Uyga qaytgach, qanchalik charchaganimni bilib hayron qoldim.","why":"\"How exhausted I was\" — javob: exhausted. \"Relaxed\" — safar paytidagi holat, tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":0.09,"e":7.61,"t":"Exercise 45. You'll hear a woman called Harriet O'Neill talking about a holiday tour of South Africa."},{"s":14.55,"e":19.04,"t":"I was really lucky last year to have the opportunity to visit South Africa."},{"s":19.64,"e":22.53,"t":"was absolutely the holiday of a lifetime."},{"s":23.1,"e":32.7,"t":"I went with my husband. He has some relatives who emigrated there recently, an uncle and some cousins. So we spent a bit of time with them which was good."},{"s":33.46,"e":37.18,"t":"Oddly enough, my grandfather was actually born in Johannesburg."},{"s":37.66,"e":46.24,"t":"but he'd left before he was ten years old. Still, that's always made me feel I have a connection with the country, and I've always wanted to go there."},{"s":47.13,"e":59.23,"t":"The main impetus for our visit, however, was that our sons mad on sport and his school had organised a tour so the boys in the first and second teams could play some rugby matches there."},{"s":59.9,"e":64.73,"t":"Quite a few of us parents decided to go out there at the same time to watch them play."},{"s":65.24,"e":70.81,"t":"which was quite scary, as the South African boys all seemed so much bigger than ours."},{"s":71.45,"e":78.21,"t":"But anyway, they all survived with no broken bones and we managed to have a really exciting holiday too."},{"s":79.0,"e":84.03,"t":"Although we were following the same route as the school tour, we travelled independently."},{"s":84.66,"e":91.42,"t":"The school used a travel agent called Rainbow Tours and they were able to make arrangements for us too.","uz":"Maktab Rainbow Tours degan turagentlikdan foydalangan, ular biz uchun ham hamma narsani tashkil qila olishdi."},{"s":92.28,"e":97.53,"t":"We considered organising our trip through another company called Safari Holidays."},{"s":98.36,"e":102.85,"t":"didn't use them in the end, though they also had some very good deals."},{"s":103.9,"e":105.63,"t":"was an amazing country."},{"s":106.2,"e":117.41,"t":"As soon as I got off the plane after a overnight flight, I was impressed by the light there. was just so clear. different from what we have here.","uz":"Bir kechalik reysdan keyin samolyotdan tushishim bilan u yerdagi yorug'lik meni hayratga soldi. Juda tiniq edi, biznikidan butunlay boshqacha."},{"s":118.17,"e":122.59,"t":"It was beautifully warm too of course, but we'd been expecting that."},{"s":123.54,"e":127.93,"t":"One of the best things we did was spend a weekend at a safari park."},{"s":128.66,"e":135.52,"t":"It was such a privilege to see so many beautiful animals in their natural habitat."},{"s":136.31,"e":140.73,"t":"and white rhinos, giraffes, elephants, aardvark,"},{"s":141.59,"e":144.73,"t":"I loved seeing lions sleeping in the bush."},{"s":145.91,"e":151.65,"t":"Best of all for me were the cheetahs, which we saw when we went on a night drive.","uz":"Men uchun hammasidan zo'ri — tungi sayr paytida ko'rgan gepardlar bo'ldi."},{"s":152.12,"e":154.49,"t":"My husband's favourites were the hippos."},{"s":155.9,"e":160.09,"t":"We saw interesting animals elsewhere as well as at the safari park."},{"s":160.66,"e":168.93,"t":"We hired a car to get around and we caught sight of lots of zebras and ostriches as we were driving along the east coast."},{"s":169.56,"e":174.78,"t":"One day we broke our journey at a crocodile farm and learnt so much about them.","uz":"Bir kuni yo'limizda timsoh fermasida to'xtadik va ular haqida ko'p narsa bildik."},{"s":175.74,"e":180.29,"t":"We went in January and it was a little hot for comfort at times."},{"s":180.76,"e":188.54,"t":"I'm told the best time to go is April - it's cooler then, at night particularly - and so you've got more energy for sightseeing.","uz":"Aytishlaricha, borishga eng yaxshi vaqt — aprel: o'shanda salqinroq bo'ladi."},{"s":188.98,"e":193.44,"t":"It's still plenty warm enough to lie on the beach in the daytime, if that's your thing."},{"s":194.3,"e":201.15,"t":"We felt so relaxed during the trip. I was taken aback when we got home to discover how exhausted I was.","uz":"Safar davomida o'zimizni juda xotirjam his qildik. Uyga qaytgach, qanchalik charchaganimni bilib hayron qoldim."},{"s":202.2,"e":205.47,"t":"I suppose we'd just done so much over a short time."},{"s":206.39,"e":210.27,"t":"Anyway we soon recovered and I hope we'll visit again someday."}]},{"n":46,"ins":2,"title":"The ancient city of Cuzco","dur":443.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The words open-air museum are sometimes used to describe the city because of its historic buildings."},{"k":"p","t":"Cuzco was originally designed in the shape of a {1} lion."},{"k":"p","t":"The Incas built houses in Cuzco without {2} to keep out the cold."},{"k":"p","t":"Ava says the {3} in Cuzco was a problem for some people but not for her."},{"k":"p","t":"Watching the rehearsals, Ava found the {4} dancing particularly impressive."},{"k":"p","t":"Ava was surprised by the wide range of costumes when the main parade began."},{"k":"p","t":"Ava believes the builders of the walls first made {5} of certain stones."},{"k":"p","t":"Ava had read there were no {6} at the ancient Festival of the Sun."}],"items":[{"a":["mountain"],"ps":60.18,"en":71.36,"si":3,"ev":"They planned and built the city so that it resembled a mountain lion and districts and individual streets still bear the names of body parts such as the head and back.","hl":"mountain","uz":"Ular shaharni tog' sheriga o'xshatib rejalashtirib qurishgan; tumanlar va ko'chalar hali ham bosh, orqa kabi tana qismlari nomi bilan ataladi.","why":"\"Resembled a mountain lion\" — javob: mountain."},{"a":["windows"],"ps":85.08,"en":96.25,"si":6,"ev":"Many of the original Inca homes there lacked windows and had just a single door.","hl":"windows","uz":"U yerdagi ko'plab asl inka uylarida deraza bo'lmagan, faqat bitta eshik bo'lgan.","why":"\"Lacked windows\" → \"without windows\". Javob: windows."},{"a":["sun"],"ps":102.87,"en":117.5,"si":8,"ev":"A number of the others were looking distinctly uncomfortable as the fierce sun began to beat down. But as an Australian, I'm accustomed to that.","hl":"sun","uz":"Boshqalarning bir qismi qattiq quyosh qizdira boshlaganda o'zini yomon his qila boshladi. Lekin men avstraliyalik sifatida bunga o'rganganman.","why":"Boshqalarga muammo, Avaga emas — sun. Balandlik (height) — hammaga qiyin bo'lgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["folk"],"ps":137.78,"en":145.79,"si":11,"ev":"What really stood out for me was the folk dancing, though some of the concerts and parades were well worth watching too.","hl":"folk","uz":"Menga eng ta'sir qilgani xalq raqslari bo'ldi, garchi ba'zi konsert va paradlar ham ko'rishga arziydigan bo'lsa-da.","why":"\"What really stood out\" — folk dancing. Konsert va paradlar — tuzoq."},{"a":["models"],"ps":184.86,"en":201.25,"si":16,"ev":"The only way the Incas could have achieved that … is by sculpting models in lighter materials to the exact size and shape required and then reproducing them in stone.","hl":"models","uz":"Inkalar buni faqat yengilroq materiallardan aynan kerakli o'lcham va shakldagi modellar yasab, keyin ularni toshda takrorlash orqali uddalagan bo'lishi mumkin.","why":"\"Sculpting models … then reproducing them in stone\" — javob: models."},{"a":["spectators"],"ps":209.37,"en":226.17,"si":18,"ev":"Looking at the vast crowds of spectators, I recalled a paper written by a local historian which made the point that in Inca times there weren't any. In one way or another, all the thousands of people at the festival in those days were participants.","hl":"spectators","uz":"Ulkan tomoshabinlar olomoniga qarab, mahalliy tarixchining inkalar davrida tomoshabinlar bo'lmagani haqidagi maqolasini esladim. U paytlarda festivaldagi minglab odamlarning hammasi ishtirokchi bo'lgan.","why":"\"In Inca times there weren't any (spectators)\" — hamma ishtirokchi edi. Javob: spectators."}],"segs":[{"s":2.81,"e":8.64,"t":"You'll hear a research student called Eva O'Neill talking about visiting Cuzco in Peru."},{"s":28.54,"e":50.43,"t":"Peruvian city of Cuzco is a total experience. From its location 11,000 feet up in the Andes Mountains, its history as the ancient capital of the Inca Empire, and its unique culture to the blend of Inca and Spanish architecture from different centuries that has led to researchers referring to it as an open-air museum."},{"s":51.35,"e":59.42,"t":"Its origins actually go back over a thousand years, but it was in the 13th century that the invading Incas reached Cuzco."},{"s":60.18,"e":71.36,"t":"They planned and built the city so that it resembled a mountain lion and districts and individual streets still bear the names of body parts such as the head and back.","uz":"Ular shaharni tog' sheriga o'xshatib rejalashtirib qurishgan; tumanlar va ko'chalar hali ham bosh, orqa kabi tana qismlari nomi bilan ataladi."},{"s":71.9,"e":76.19,"t":"while the tail was formed by straightening the point where two rivers joined."},{"s":77.37,"e":84.45,"t":"Although night-time temperatures in Cuzco can be quite mild, that is certainly not the case all year round."},{"s":85.08,"e":96.25,"t":"On account of that, many of the original Inca homes there lacked windows and had just a single door, which would have been covered by a thick mat during the chillier months."},{"s":96.82,"e":102.14,"t":"There would also have been a straw roof that had to be replaced every few years."},{"s":102.87,"e":117.5,"t":"My colleagues and I were there in late June and I noticed on the first afternoon that a number of the others were looking distinctly uncomfortable as the fierce sun began to beat down. But as an Australian, I'm accustomed to that."},{"s":118.52,"e":127.84,"t":"The height above sea level was another matter, leaving all of us short of breath at times, especially when climbing the steep hills around the city."},{"s":128.98,"e":137.05,"t":"Having arrived a couple of days ahead of the festival of the sun, we were able to watch some of the performers practicing for the big day."},{"s":137.78,"e":145.79,"t":"What really stood out for me was the folk dancing, though some of the concerts and parades were well worth watching too.","uz":"Menga eng ta'sir qilgani xalq raqslari bo'ldi, garchi ba'zi konsert va paradlar ham ko'rishga arziydigan bo'lsa-da."},{"s":146.87,"e":153.66,"t":"On the 24th, the day of the festival itself, the city centre was packed as the procession set off."},{"s":154.42,"e":168.83,"t":"The multi-coloured costumes were fabulous, even more varied than I'd imagined, as the participants moved slowly up the hill to the ancient site called 'Saksehwa Man', where the main ceremony would take place."},{"s":170.01,"e":173.25,"t":"That is where the magnificent walls are located."},{"s":174.01,"e":183.9,"t":"Standing nearly 6 metres tall and measuring up to 400 metres in length, they were built of huge stones that fitted together perfectly."},{"s":184.86,"e":201.25,"t":"Given that some of them weigh 200 tonnes each, the only way the Incas could have achieved that, my research indicates, is by sculpting models in lighter materials to the exact size and shape required and then reproducing them in stone."},{"s":202.2,"e":208.38,"t":"I stood there marveling at the sight of the walls and at the colourful scene as the ceremony began."},{"s":209.37,"e":226.17,"t":"Looking at the vast crowds of spectators, I recalled a paper written by a local historian which made the point that in Inca times there weren't any. In one way or another, all the thousands of people at the festival in those days were participants.","uz":"Ulkan tomoshabinlar olomoniga qarab, mahalliy tarixchining inkalar davrida tomoshabinlar bo'lmagani haqidagi maqolasini esladim. U paytlarda festivaldagi minglab odamlarning hammasi ishtirokchi bo'lgan."}]},{"n":47,"ins":2,"title":"Lena Horne","dur":242.4,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The 'talented tenth' was a label given to those African Americans who had good social positions and were educated."},{"k":"p","t":"She left school and began her singing career at the well-known Cotton Club."},{"k":"p","t":"Her mother was keen that Lena's singing career would bring about the collapse of racial {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Lena refused to sing for audiences of servicemen and prisoners which were {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"When Lena entered Hollywood, black actors were generally only hired to act in the roles of {3} and butlers."},{"k":"p","t":"While she was working for Hollywood, Lena found that, during the {4} process, much of her spoken work was removed from the film."},{"k":"p","t":"Lena spent a lot of the 1950s working in {5} due to her being considered a Communist."},{"k":"p","t":"Most people will remember Lena for her {6} voice."}],"items":[{"a":["barriers"],"ps":78.3,"en":88.93,"si":11,"ev":"All her life, Lena's mother Edna had hoped that Lena could use her performances to break down race barriers.","hl":"barriers","uz":"Butun umri davomida Lenaning onasi Edna qizi chiqishlari orqali irqiy to'siqlarni buzishiga umid qilgan.","why":"\"Break down race barriers\" → \"the collapse of racial barriers\". Javob: barriers."},{"a":["segregated"],"ps":113.85,"en":137.66,"si":17,"ev":"She noticed that she was always being asked to perform for groups which were segregated in terms of colour… She soon refused to perform for such occasions.","hl":"segregated","uz":"U doim rangi bo'yicha ajratilgan guruhlar oldida chiqish qilishni so'rashlarini payqadi… Tez orada bunday tadbirlarda chiqishdan bosh tortdi.","why":"\"Segregated in terms of colour\" — javob: segregated."},{"a":["maids"],"ps":152.63,"en":156.48,"si":20,"ev":"Black actors rarely had the chance to play anything more than maids and butlers.","hl":"maids","uz":"Qora tanli aktyorlarga oqsoch va xizmatkordan boshqa rol kamdan-kam berilardi.","why":"\"Maids and butlers\" — javob: maids."},{"a":["editing"],"ps":157.11,"en":170.33,"si":21,"ev":"She found that she rarely had the chance to act, and many of her lines were cut during the editing process.","hl":"editing","uz":"U kamdan-kam rol o'ynash imkoniga ega bo'lganini, ko'p so'zlari montaj jarayonida qirqib tashlanganini ko'rdi.","why":"\"Cut during the editing process\" — javob: editing."},{"a":["(night) clubs"],"ps":200.06,"en":213.98,"si":26,"ev":"She soon found herself blacklisted and unable to work on television or in the movies. At this time however, she continued to sing in night clubs.","hl":"clubs","uz":"Tez orada u qora ro'yxatga tushib, televideniye va kinoda ishlay olmay qoldi. Biroq bu davrda tungi klublarda qo'shiq aytishda davom etdi.","why":"TV va kino yopilgan — night clubs'da ishlagan. Javob: (night) clubs."},{"a":["resonant"],"ps":228.95,"en":242.34,"si":29,"ev":"But what she will be remembered for most of all must be her ability to move generations of audiences with her shimmering resonant voice.","hl":"resonant","uz":"Lekin uni eng avvalo avlodlarni ta'sirlantirgan jarangdor, yaltiroq ovozi uchun eslashadi.","why":"\"Remembered for most of all … resonant voice\" — javob: resonant."}],"segs":[{"s":3.93,"e":8.64,"t":"Last month, the renowned and much loved singer Lena Horne died in New York aged 92."},{"s":9.59,"e":14.27,"t":"This Afro-American singer and civil activist whet in America in the golden era of stage and screen."},{"s":14.74,"e":17.63,"t":"meeting such great names as Billie Holiday and Duke Ellington."},{"s":18.42,"e":23.23,"t":"We have with us here in the studio Joel Lightwater to tell us more about Lena Horne's remarkable life."},{"s":24.92,"e":25.6,"t":"Thank you, John"},{"s":26.39,"e":39.29,"t":"Leinohorn was born in 1917 to a Brooklyn family, described by a prominent writer as the \"talented tenth\", a name which was given to those members of the African-American community who were educated and socially prominent."},{"s":39.96,"e":52.51,"t":"Her family were activists in African American rights. Her grandmother, Cora Calhoun, was in fact the founding member of the NAACP, that is, the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People."},{"s":53.08,"e":54.94,"t":"Indeed, the age of two."},{"s":55.42,"e":58.11,"t":"Alina was photographed parading in a protest."},{"s":59.13,"e":68.45,"t":"A childhood was split between her grandparent's townhouse in Brooklyn and her mother's lodgings in Harlem, her father having left the family when Lena was only three years old."},{"s":69.02,"e":77.02,"t":"She went to school at Brooklyn Girls High, but when she started singing at the famous Cotton Club at the age of 16, she dropped out without a diploma."},{"s":78.3,"e":88.93,"t":"All her life, Lena's mother Edna had hoped that Lena could use her performances to break down race barriers. This was not an easy thing to do in the race-conscious culture of the time."},{"s":89.5,"e":96.0,"t":"At one point, Lena was advised to advertise her creamy complexion as Latin, something she refused to do."},{"s":96.66,"e":97.98,"t":"while later in her career,"},{"s":98.55,"e":103.55,"t":"studio executives in Hollywood suggested that she darken her skin colour with make-up"},{"s":104.7,"e":108.96,"t":"Matters relating to racial equality were always high up on Lena's priorities."},{"s":109.46,"e":113.37,"t":"during World War II when she was entertaining soldiers and prisoners of war."},{"s":113.85,"e":137.66,"t":"She noticed that she was always being asked to perform for groups which were segregated in terms of colour… She soon refused to perform for such occasions.","uz":"U doim rangi bo'yicha ajratilgan guruhlar oldida chiqish qilishni so'rashlarini payqadi… Tez orada bunday tadbirlarda chiqishdan bosh tortdi."},{"s":138.94,"e":148.29,"t":"After the war years, Lena had the opportunity to move into the glamorous world of Hollywood and she was the first African American to be signed on a long-term studio contract."},{"s":148.79,"e":152.13,"t":"However, this was an age when the colour barrier was still strong."},{"s":152.63,"e":156.48,"t":"Black actors rarely had the chance to play anything more than maids and butlers.","uz":"Qora tanli aktyorlarga oqsoch va xizmatkordan boshqa rol kamdan-kam berilardi."},{"s":157.11,"e":170.33,"t":"Although Lena was beginning to achieve a high level of notoriety, she found that she rarely had the chance to act, and many of her lines were cut during the editing process. Only in two incidences did she play a character that was central to the plot."},{"s":171.42,"e":180.29,"t":"But Lena's elegance and powerful voice were unlike anything that had come before, and both the public and the executives in the entertainment industry began to take note."},{"s":180.79,"e":186.97,"t":"By the mid-40s, Horn was the highest paid black actor in the country and her songs were instant classics."},{"s":188.15,"e":193.44,"t":"However, Horn's great fame could not prevent the wheels of the anti-communist machine from bearing down on her."},{"s":194.04,"e":199.52,"t":"During the 1950s, she was marked as a communist sympathizer as a result of her civil rights activism."},{"s":200.06,"e":213.98,"t":"She soon found herself blacklisted and unable to work on television or in the movies. At this time however, she continued to sing in night clubs.","uz":"Tez orada u qora ro'yxatga tushib, televideniye va kinoda ishlay olmay qoldi. Biroq bu davrda tungi klublarda qo'shiq aytishda davom etdi."},{"s":214.71,"e":220.16,"t":"Since the 16 year old danced her first steps on the stage of the Cotton Club, much has changed."},{"s":220.76,"e":228.03,"t":"Thanks to her continued musical, theatrical and political efforts, she paved the way for many other non-whites in the entertainment industry."},{"s":228.95,"e":242.34,"t":"But what she will be remembered for most of all must be her ability to move generations of audiences with her shimmering resonant voice singing the classic greats like Black Coffee and the unforgettable stormy weather."}]},{"n":48,"ins":2,"title":"Extreme snowboarding","dur":256.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Brad says there are no signs to warn extreme snowboarders of dangers."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad advises snowboarders always to follow the {1} when descending."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad always wears a {2} when he goes into the mountains."},{"k":"p","t":"According to Brad, you need a lot of confidence to set off down the mountain."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad particularly enjoys doing several jumps when he is going down a slope."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad says at first he found it difficult to do a good {3} on steep slopes."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad says you must never panic if you feel you're about to fall."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad advises against putting your weight on your {4} in a fall."},{"k":"p","t":"Brad always carries a {5} in case he is in difficulty following a fall."},{"k":"p","t":"In the future, Brad would most like to try {6} snowboarding."}],"items":[{"a":["guide"],"ps":45.4,"en":50.24,"si":4,"ev":"So it's up to you and your guide to make sure your route is as safe as possible.","hl":"guide","uz":"Shuning uchun yo'lingiz iloji boricha xavfsiz bo'lishi sizga va yo'lboshlovchingizga bog'liq.","why":"Yolg'iz tushmaslik va \"your guide\" bilan yurish — javob: guide."},{"a":["helmet"],"ps":81.98,"en":85.92,"si":9,"ev":"I always prefer to go on foot, with a helmet on, of course.","hl":"helmet","uz":"Men doim piyoda, albatta dubulg'a kiyib chiqishni afzal ko'raman.","why":"\"With a helmet on, of course\" — javob: helmet. Vertolyot — boshqalar tanlovi, tuzoq."},{"a":["landing"],"ps":138.01,"en":150.72,"si":15,"ev":"Whereas doing a reasonably good take-off seems to come fairly naturally to most of us, landing is a more complex skill to acquire, as I found in my early days.","hl":"landing","uz":"Yaxshi sakrab ko'tarilish ko'pchiligimizga tabiiy keladi, lekin qo'nish — o'rganish qiyinroq ko'nikma, buni dastlabki kunlarimda bilganman.","why":"\"In my early days\" = \"at first\" — landing qiyin bo'lgan. Take-off — oson, tuzoq."},{"a":["wrist"],"ps":176.82,"en":191.81,"si":18,"ev":"Remember that elbows, if you fall on them, are much stronger and less likely to be injured than wrists.","hl":"wrists","uz":"Esda tuting: tirsaklar bilaklardan ancha mustahkam va shikastlanishi kamroq.","why":"Bilakka (wrist) og'irlik tushirmang. Elbows — kuchliroq, tuzoq."},{"a":["device"],"ps":204.66,"en":216.25,"si":21,"ev":"I'd never go down a slope without a small device fastened to my body that sends out a signal to the rescue services if I get buried.","hl":"device","uz":"Qor ostida qolsam, qutqaruvchilarga signal yuboradigan kichik qurilmani tanamga mahkamlamasdan hech qachon tushmayman.","why":"\"A small device … sends out a signal\" — javob: device. Dori qutisi (medical kit) — boshqalarning tavsiyasi, tuzoq."},{"a":["parachute"],"ps":241.18,"en":244.61,"si":27,"ev":"But what I really dream about is parachute snowboarding.","hl":"parachute","uz":"Lekin men haqiqatan orzu qiladigan narsa — parashyutli snoubord.","why":"\"What I really dream about\" — parachute. O'qitish — \"might do one day\", tuzoq."}],"segs":[{"s":0.09,"e":5.6,"t":"Exercise 48. You will hear an expert snowboarder called Brad Mitchell."},{"s":6.2,"e":8.8,"t":"talking about the sport of extreme snowboarding."},{"s":27.9,"e":37.95,"t":"When you go extreme snowboarding, you head for the highest peaks and the steepest slopes, taking little more than a map and some basic survival equipment with you."},{"s":38.81,"e":44.96,"t":"Unlike in ski resorts, you won't see any signs telling you there are rocks or trees around."},{"s":45.4,"e":50.24,"t":"So it's up to you and your guide to make sure your route is as safe as possible.","uz":"Shuning uchun yo'lingiz iloji boricha xavfsiz bo'lishi sizga va yo'lboshlovchingizga bog'liq."},{"s":51.19,"e":54.4,"t":"Of course, you should never attempt to go down a slope on your own."},{"s":55.03,"e":64.03,"t":"It's essential to be accompanied by a guide who must go first every time as there may be no clear route down through the rocks and other dangers."},{"s":64.73,"e":73.95,"t":"They'll also show you the way up to your starting point, which may involve a long, difficult climb, and may wear a backpack containing supplies."},{"s":74.39,"e":81.34,"t":"I know some snowboarders like to take a helicopter up to the top and that's quick and easy, though expensive."},{"s":81.98,"e":85.92,"t":"I always prefer to go on foot, with a helmet on, of course.","uz":"Men doim piyoda, albatta dubulg'a kiyib chiqishni afzal ko'raman."},{"s":86.62,"e":92.8,"t":"When you finally get up there, the view is always completely different from the way it looked from below."},{"s":93.5,"e":98.62,"t":"People say to me it must take a lot of courage to start going down such a steep slope."},{"s":99.22,"e":108.29,"t":"But if you've reached that point, then you must be a pretty experienced snowboarder and what's really required is a tremendous amount of confidence."},{"s":108.89,"e":120.77,"t":"You never know exactly which way you're going to go or what you're going to encounter on your way down and you often find yourself having to make split second decisions but that's part of the fun."},{"s":121.56,"e":137.34,"t":"There is nothing quite as exciting as suddenly having to perform a series of jumps as you descend and then managing to stay on your feet afterwards. The ability to do that is obviously something that takes those new to extreme snowboarding quite some time to learn."},{"s":138.01,"e":150.72,"t":"Whereas doing a reasonably good take-off seems to come fairly naturally to most of us, landing is a more complex skill to acquire, as I found in my early days.","uz":"Yaxshi sakrab ko'tarilish ko'pchiligimizga tabiiy keladi, lekin qo'nish — o'rganish qiyinroq ko'nikma, buni dastlabki kunlarimda bilganman."},{"s":151.77,"e":163.52,"t":"Falling correctly is also something you need to practice, initially at low speed and on gentle slopes, and later in conditions more similar to those you'll encounter on the mountain."},{"s":164.34,"e":175.93,"t":"Rule one, when you lose your balance, is not to panic, or else you'll get tense and be far more likely to injure yourself than if you're relaxed and just let yourself go with the fall."},{"s":176.82,"e":191.81,"t":"Often the best thing to do is roll out of the fall, but it's natural to try to use your arms to try to slow yourself down, and if you do so, remember that elbows, if you fall on them, are much stronger and less likely to be injured than wrists."},{"s":192.7,"e":198.81,"t":"Following a high speed fall, you might find yourself covered by some of the white stuff that has fallen with you."},{"s":199.51,"e":204.22,"t":"There may be just a few feet of it, and you can usually pull yourself up to the surface."},{"s":204.66,"e":216.25,"t":"But if you can't, you're in big trouble. And that's why I'd never go down a slope without a small device fastened to my body that sends out a signal to the rescue services if I get buried."},{"s":217.27,"e":221.34,"t":"I know some safety experts recommend also taking a medical kit."},{"s":221.88,"e":228.09,"t":"But somehow I think that if I were buried under ice, my priority would be to get out or get rescued."},{"s":228.86,"e":231.01,"t":"I'm always looking for new challenges."},{"s":231.51,"e":236.64,"t":"Competition snowboarding was something I looked at, but there were just too many guys showing off."},{"s":237.34,"e":240.61,"t":"Teaching snowboarding is certainly something I might do one day"},{"s":241.18,"e":244.61,"t":"But what I really dream about is parachute snowboarding.","uz":"Lekin men haqiqatan orzu qiladigan narsa — parashyutli snoubord."},{"s":245.05,"e":250.85,"t":"going straight down a mountain, flying off a cliff, and then floating down to the valley below."},{"s":251.61,"e":253.73,"t":"Now that's what I call extreme."}]},{"n":49,"ins":2,"title":"Mooncake","dur":239.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Markus was staying in Japan when he first tried mooncake."},{"k":"p","t":"Markus's favourite kind of mooncake has a filling made of {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Markus says that he likes to have {2} with mooncake."},{"k":"p","t":"Mooncake is popular during the Moon Festival, which last year was held in September."},{"k":"p","t":"The mooncake Markus was given during the festival had the shape of a {3} on the top."},{"k":"p","t":"Markus was surprised to learn that mooncake is rarely made at home in China."},{"k":"p","t":"The people Markus was staying with received mooncake from their {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"His host family gave Markus a mooncake that had a slightly {5} flavour."},{"k":"p","t":"Markus was told that, many years ago, people used mooncakes to send secret messages to each other."},{"k":"p","t":"After people had read what was written on the mooncake, they {6} it."}],"items":[{"a":["nuts"],"ps":56.54,"en":67.29,"si":7,"ev":"I very much like those filled with egg, dried fruit or seeds, though for me, the one that really stands out has nuts inside.","hl":"nuts","uz":"Tuxum, quritilgan meva yoki urug' solinganlari juda yoqadi, lekin men uchun eng ajralib turadigani — ichida yong'oq bo'lgani.","why":"\"The one that really stands out\" — nuts. Egg, dried fruit, seeds — tuzoq."},{"a":["tea"],"ps":77.37,"en":81.18,"si":11,"ev":"Whatever the type of mooncake though, it is best accompanied by tea.","hl":"tea","uz":"Qanday turdagi oy pishirig'i bo'lmasin, unga eng yaxshi hamroh — choy.","why":"\"Best accompanied by tea\" — javob: tea. Sutli qahva — odatdagi sevimli ichimligi, tuzoq."},{"a":["rabbit"],"ps":110.3,"en":120.8,"si":16,"ev":"I noticed the form of a rabbit on the upper surface of the one I was about to bite into.","hl":"rabbit","uz":"Tishlamoqchi bo'lgan pishiriqning ustida quyon shaklini ko'rdim.","why":"\"The form of a rabbit on the upper surface\" — javob: rabbit. Gullar va nonvoy nomi — boshqalarida bo'ladi, tuzoq."},{"a":["employer"],"ps":143.13,"en":155.77,"si":21,"ev":"and at that time of year, many are received as presents in gift-wrapped boxes, often from relatives or friends. Although in the case of my host family, theirs was from the employer of both the man and the woman.","hl":"employer","uz":"Yilning shu paytida ko'plari sovg'a qutilarida, ko'pincha qarindosh yoki do'stlardan keladi. Lekin mezbon oilamizniki ham erga, ham xotinga ish beruvchidan kelgan.","why":"Odatda qarindosh yoki do'stlardan, lekin bu oila — employer'dan olgan. Javob: employer."},{"a":["salty"],"ps":168.57,"en":174.78,"si":25,"ev":"This one differed from the generally sweet varieties found elsewhere in China in that it tasted a little salty.","hl":"salty","uz":"Bu Xitoyning boshqa joylaridagi odatda shirin turlardan farq qilardi — biroz sho'r ta'mli edi.","why":"\"Tasted a little salty\" → \"slightly salty flavour\". Javob: salty."},{"a":["ate"],"ps":221.14,"en":227.23,"si":34,"ev":"Once the message had been received, the evidence soon disappeared when everyone ate the mooncakes.","hl":"ate","uz":"Xabar o'qilgach, hamma oy pishiriqlarini yeb qo'yishi bilan dalil tezda yo'q bo'lardi.","why":"\"Everyone ate the mooncakes\" — javob: ate."}],"segs":[{"s":3.8,"e":6.27,"t":"You will hear a man called Marcus Fisher"},{"s":6.78,"e":8.41,"t":"Talking about mooncake."},{"s":9.11,"e":11.36,"t":"traditional Asian bakery product."},{"s":24.02,"e":33.44,"t":"The mooncake has long been popular among the Chinese communities in many western societies, and of course it first appeared in China many centuries ago."},{"s":34.01,"e":38.14,"t":"and it's also extremely popular in countries such as Indonesia and Thailand."},{"s":38.78,"e":42.69,"t":"but I hadn't actually tasted it until I visited Japan some years ago."},{"s":43.42,"e":55.36,"t":"I enjoyed it so much that since then I have eaten it in places as far apart as Vietnam and the Philippines, each time being pleasantly surprised by the differences in appearance, ingredients and flavour."},{"s":56.54,"e":67.29,"t":"I very much like those filled with egg, dried fruit or seeds, though for me, the one that really stands out has nuts inside.","uz":"Tuxum, quritilgan meva yoki urug' solinganlari juda yoqadi, lekin men uchun eng ajralib turadigani — ichida yong'oq bo'lgani."},{"s":68.09,"e":69.85,"t":"All of these kinds are quite sweet."},{"s":70.65,"e":74.33,"t":"Of course are the more modern varieties filled with chocolate or ice cream."},{"s":74.87,"e":76.48,"t":"I'm not so keen on those."},{"s":77.37,"e":81.18,"t":"Whatever the type of mooncake though, it is best accompanied by tea.","uz":"Qanday turdagi oy pishirig'i bo'lmasin, unga eng yaxshi hamroh — choy."},{"s":81.78,"e":87.9,"t":"I certainly drank lots of it when I was in Shanghai last year, rather than my usual favourite coffee with milk."},{"s":88.6,"e":99.39,"t":"I was fortunate enough to be there while people were celebrating the Moon Festival, an annual event that sometimes takes place in October, although last autumn it was in September."},{"s":100.09,"e":103.36,"t":"In other years it's been held only just after the end of August."},{"s":104.28,"e":109.41,"t":"During the festival, I learnt a lot more about mooncake from the Chinese family I was staying with."},{"s":110.3,"e":120.8,"t":"I noticed the form of a rabbit on the upper surface of the one I was about to bite into, and it was pointed out to me that others may have flowers on the top, or the name of the baker's written there."},{"s":121.78,"e":125.85,"t":"The mooncake is traditionally seen as a way of bringing families closer together."},{"s":126.78,"e":129.92,"t":"I'd assumed that most Chinese people baked their own at home."},{"s":130.55,"e":136.41,"t":"But when I asked the family about that, they said few did, mainly because it's so difficult to prepare."},{"s":137.43,"e":142.65,"t":"Nowadays, of course, people in towns and cities often buy mooncakes in supermarkets."},{"s":143.13,"e":155.77,"t":"and at that time of year, many are received as presents in gift-wrapped boxes, often from relatives or friends. Although in the case of my host family, theirs was from the employer of both the man and the woman.","uz":"Yilning shu paytida ko'plari sovg'a qutilarida, ko'pincha qarindosh yoki do'stlardan keladi. Lekin mezbon oilamizniki ham erga, ham xotinga ish beruvchidan kelgan."},{"s":156.82,"e":161.28,"t":"Although living in Shanghai, the family originally came from the city of Ningbo."},{"s":161.72,"e":163.52,"t":"further up the coast to the northeast."},{"s":164.06,"e":167.68,"t":"and as a gift they gave me a mooncake to take with me when I left."},{"s":168.57,"e":174.78,"t":"This one differed from the generally sweet varieties found elsewhere in China in that it tasted a little salty.","uz":"Bu Xitoyning boshqa joylaridagi odatda shirin turlardan farq qilardi — biroz sho'r ta'mli edi."},{"s":175.42,"e":179.65,"t":"on account of the fact that it was made from locally produced ingredients that included meat."},{"s":180.82,"e":185.47,"t":"And by this time, I was becoming fascinated by everything connected with Mooncake."},{"s":186.04,"e":188.77,"t":"and I asked the family to tell me a little about its history."},{"s":189.66,"e":195.74,"t":"They told me it first became popular in the 14th century during the time of the Ming revolution."},{"s":196.41,"e":202.08,"t":"when people passed on secret messages to one another as writing on the top of four mooncakes."},{"s":202.97,"e":207.13,"t":"To understand the code, the cakes had to be cut into four slices each."},{"s":207.58,"e":210.94,"t":"and then joined with those from the other cakes to complete the message."},{"s":212.18,"e":220.35,"t":"This took place on the day of the Moon Festival, which then, as it still is today, was one of the most important dates in the Chinese calendar."},{"s":221.14,"e":227.23,"t":"Once the message had been received, the evidence soon disappeared when everyone ate the mooncakes.","uz":"Xabar o'qilgach, hamma oy pishiriqlarini yeb qo'yishi bilan dalil tezda yo'q bo'lardi."},{"s":228.38,"e":232.73,"t":"Another legend describes the passing of messages hidden inside mooncake"},{"s":233.24,"e":237.57,"t":"although presumably in that case the secret letter was burnt once it had been read."}]},{"n":50,"ins":2,"title":"Moving to the countryside","dur":261.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Fiona says the lack of street lights in the countryside created a contrast at night."},{"k":"p","t":"Some rooms in the house can be rather damp in winter."},{"k":"p","t":"At first, the {1} made it difficult for Fiona to sleep in the house."},{"k":"p","t":"Fiona finds she tends to get up later in the day than when she was in the city."},{"k":"p","t":"In the countryside, Fiona sees {2} from her bedroom window."},{"k":"p","t":"Fiona sometimes finds the slowness of the {3} where she lives rather irritating."},{"k":"p","t":"Out in the countryside, Fiona sometimes can't get {4} from friends."},{"k":"p","t":"The nearest bus stop is almost two kilometres away from where Fiona lives."},{"k":"p","t":"Fiona says you need to have a {5} in the country, but not in the city."},{"k":"p","t":"Fiona won't have to travel as far to the {6} as she would from her old home."}],"items":[{"a":["silence"],"ps":83.64,"en":96.54,"si":9,"ev":"For a while after we moved in, I'd keep waking up in the middle of the night owing to the total silence there.","hl":"silence","uz":"Ko'chib kelganimizdan keyin bir muddat u yerdagi to'liq sukunat sababli yarim tunda uyg'onib ketardim.","why":"Shovqin emas — \"total silence\". Javob: silence. Shahar shovqini — avval o'rgangan narsa, tuzoq."},{"a":["rabbits"],"ps":129.34,"en":143.42,"si":14,"ev":"Here I start the day to the sound of distant farm animals and the sight of rabbits in the open fields.","hl":"rabbits","uz":"Bu yerda kunni uzoqdagi uy hayvonlari ovozi va ochiq dalalardagi quyonlarni ko'rish bilan boshlayman.","why":"Derazadan ko'rinadi — rabbits. Bug'ular (deer) — hali ko'rmagan; mushuk, it, tulki — shaharda, tuzoq."},{"a":["internet"],"ps":151.48,"en":167.2,"si":16,"ev":"I must confess, though, that I can get a bit fed up with the speed of the internet connection here.","hl":"internet","uz":"Tan olishim kerak, bu yerdagi internet tezligidan biroz jonga tegaman.","why":"\"Fed up with the speed of the internet\" → \"slowness … irritating\". Javob: internet. Hayot sur'atiga (pace of life) — moslashgan, tuzoq."},{"a":["calls"],"ps":180.12,"en":192.54,"si":18,"ev":"There is, though, fairly weak mobile reception out here. Sometimes no signal at all. And when that happens, I may not receive calls they're trying to make to me, which can be annoying.","hl":"calls","uz":"Bu yerda mobil aloqa ancha zaif, ba'zan umuman signal yo'q. Shunday paytda do'stlarim qilayotgan qo'ng'iroqlarni qabul qila olmasligim mumkin.","why":"\"May not receive calls\" — javob: calls."},{"a":["car"],"ps":218.01,"en":221.89,"si":23,"ev":"You can live quite happily there without a car, but not here.","hl":"car","uz":"Shaharda mashinasiz ham bemalol yashash mumkin, bu yerda esa yo'q.","why":"\"Without a car, but not here\" — javob: car. Velosiped — juda uzoq va xavfli, tuzoq."},{"a":["university"],"ps":241.11,"en":250.27,"si":26,"ev":"…which I hope will be before I go to university next year. Fortunately, it'll be a shorter drive from here than from where I used to live.","hl":"university","uz":"…umid qilamanki, kelasi yil universitetga borishimdan oldin. Yaxshiyamki, bu yerdan u yerga avvalgi uyimdagidan yaqinroq.","why":"\"A shorter drive from here\" — university'ga. Javob: university."}],"segs":[{"s":3.03,"e":5.63,"t":"You will hear a student called Fiona Doyle"},{"s":6.26,"e":10.4,"t":"talking about living in the countryside after growing up in a city."},{"s":18.81,"e":29.63,"t":"Parents now both work from home, so they made the decision to move from our city centre flat to the countryside, although it meant big changes for the whole family."},{"s":30.26,"e":44.06,"t":"It was a winter evening when we first went to the village and as we walked along the pavement I remarked on how dark it was without the street lights of the city and how bright that made the lights of the car seem as they approached."},{"s":44.7,"e":54.88,"t":"I also noticed the sound of running water, and when we reached the house I was delighted to discover that it stood next to a little bridge over a stream."},{"s":55.42,"e":57.92,"t":"I soon decided I liked the house."},{"s":58.39,"e":62.81,"t":"It has thick stone walls, high ceilings and wooden floors."},{"s":63.35,"e":75.39,"t":"The central heating keeps the temperature in all the rooms pleasant throughout the year, although during the colder months those in the basement tend to get a bit damp, probably because of the stream."},{"s":76.12,"e":82.94,"t":"My room is actually on the other side of the house, so I don't hear it at night, which is a pity really."},{"s":83.64,"e":96.54,"t":"I was used to the constant big city background noise of traffic and voices, and for a while after we moved in, I'd keep waking up in the middle of the night owing to the total silence there."},{"s":97.27,"e":104.83,"t":"It doesn't bother me now, though. And these days, I look forward to settling down for the night in my large, comfortable bed."},{"s":105.46,"e":112.7,"t":"I rarely stay up any later than when I was in the flat, and in the mornings I normally wake up at the same time."},{"s":113.56,"e":121.12,"t":"There aren't the sounds of the city telling you it's time to get up, so I'm usually in far less of a hurry to do so."},{"s":122.04,"e":128.22,"t":"The atmosphere here is so relaxing and I have a wonderful view from the window of my room."},{"s":129.34,"e":143.42,"t":"Before I'd see city wildlife like cats, dogs and maybe the occasional fox. Here I start the day to the sound of distant farm animals and the sight of rabbits in the open fields."},{"s":144.28,"e":150.05,"t":"Apparently there are also deer around, though I haven't actually spotted any yet."},{"s":151.48,"e":167.2,"t":"The pace of life in the countryside is certainly slower, but I think I've adjusted pretty well to it. I must confess, though, that I can get a bit fed up with the speed of the internet connection here, compared with how fast it was in the flat downtown."},{"s":168.06,"e":179.68,"t":"In spite of that, I still managed to chat online with my friends there, more or less whenever I want. So I don't have the feeling of missing them that I thought I might have before I moved."},{"s":180.12,"e":192.54,"t":"There is, though, fairly weak mobile reception out here. Sometimes no signal at all. And when that happens, I may not receive calls they're trying to make to me, which can be annoying.","uz":"Bu yerda mobil aloqa ancha zaif, ba'zan umuman signal yo'q. Shunday paytda do'stlarim qilayotgan qo'ng'iroqlarni qabul qila olmasligim mumkin."},{"s":193.24,"e":198.21,"t":"I suppose poor public transport is another disadvantage of living in the country."},{"s":198.68,"e":205.79,"t":"There isn't a railway station within 5km. It's nearly a 2km walk to get to a bus stop."},{"s":206.62,"e":209.05,"t":"Taxis charge a fortune to come out here"},{"s":209.78,"e":217.37,"t":"It's so different from where I grew up. Where the buses stop right outside your home or you can take the underground."},{"s":218.01,"e":221.89,"t":"You can live quite happily there without a car, but not here.","uz":"Shaharda mashinasiz ham bemalol yashash mumkin, bu yerda esa yo'q."},{"s":222.58,"e":233.98,"t":"People say, \"Why not go by bike?\" But the reality is that it's just too far to ride anywhere from here, and dangerous on those country roads, especially in the dark."},{"s":234.74,"e":240.54,"t":"I'll just have to rely on my parents for lifts everywhere until I pass my driving test."},{"s":241.11,"e":250.27,"t":"…which I hope will be before I go to university next year. Fortunately, it'll be a shorter drive from here than from where I used to live.","uz":"…umid qilamanki, kelasi yil universitetga borishimdan oldin. Yaxshiyamki, bu yerdan u yerga avvalgi uyimdagidan yaqinroq."},{"s":250.81,"e":255.49,"t":"And I'll avoid the awful traffic on the roads in and out of the city too."}]}];
